-0002-0181-6832","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mehdi","key":"savaghebipau","last":"Savaghebi","locid":"7ebeb655-301a-474f-864b-63251327d474","name":"Savaghebi, Mehdi","orcid":"0000-0001-6188-0265","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-98f49922-b32c-4f42-bc77-edeee18217b5"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Accelerating the Diffusion of Industrial Microgrids : The Role and Potential of Industrial Cluster Organizations as Intermediaries","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-817874","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"We want to highlight the potential effect of offering automated insulin delivery (AID) systems to people with type 1 diabetes (T1D) and limited self-management. The AID is a promising technology that can improve glycemic control and enhance the quality of life for people with T1D.1 A central feature of AID is its dynamic correction that can mitigate the glucose excursions caused by insufficient meal announcements or carbohydrate inputs, which is common among people with limited self-management capacity. Despite this, most consensus reports and national treatment guidelines state that “AID systems still require basic diabetes management skills, including carbohydrate counting.”2 Furthermore, clinical trials investigating the effect of AID systems have primarily included participants already using traditional insulin pumps, thereby excluding participants who are not candidates for insulin pumps due to limited diabetes self-management practices, including carbohydrate counting.3 This case series reports the effect of transferring people with T1D and limited diabetes self-management from multiple daily injections (MDIs) to an AID system.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Nitschke, Mette J.","Hemmingsen, Maria H.","Nørgaard, Hanne H.","Robak, Kristina A.","Nørrevang, Pia","Andersen, Merete M.","Dejgaard, Thomas F.","Pedersen-Bjergaard, Ulrik","Kristensen, Peter Lommer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-820289"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artificial pancreas","Automated insulin delivery","Diabetes technology","Self management","Type 1 diabetes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of transition from multiple daily injection therapy to automated insulin delivery in people with type 000000000001 diabetes and limited diabetes self management","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-820289","identifier":[{"id":"39862064","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11760064","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85216260536","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-df87da96-e5d1-4178-aebb-7eea426b3da6"],"keyword":["artificial pancreas","automated insulin delivery","diabetes technology","self-management","type 1 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-809ED03446A144DD45AF4EB4EDF38BD4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital – North Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mette J.","key":"nitschkepau","last":"Nitschke","name":"Nitschke, Mette J.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria H.","key":"hemmingsenpau","last":"Hemmingsen","name":"Hemmingsen, Maria H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne H.","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","name":"Nørgaard, Hanne H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina A.","key":"robakpau","last":"Robak","name":"Robak, Kristina A.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"nørrevangpau","last":"Nørrevang","name":"Nørrevang, Pia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Merete M.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Merete M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas F.","key":"dejgaardpau","last":"Dejgaard","name":"Dejgaard, Thomas F.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Ulrik","key":"pedersenbjergaardpau","last":"Pedersen-Bjergaard","locid":"3337607d-37ca-406d-81de-725da3b21dda","name":"Pedersen-Bjergaard, Ulrik","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Peter L.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"755546fc-9645-4eb7-a30c-69352f8c87e2","name":"Kristensen, Peter Lommer","name_org":"Kristensen, Peter L.","orcid":"0000-0001-5431-824X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39862064"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/19322968251315184","issn":["19322968"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Diabetes Science and Technology","pages":"857-858","status":"p","title":"Journal of Diabetes Science and Technology","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85216260536"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-df87da96-e5d1-4178-aebb-7eea426b3da6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Effect of Transition From Multiple Daily Injection Therapy to Automated Insulin Delivery in People With Type 1 Diabetes and Limited Diabetes Self-Management","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-820289","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The thousand and one kinase (TAOK) proteins are a group of serine/threonine-protein kinases involved in signaling pathways, cytoskeleton regulation, and neuronal development. TAOK1 variants are associated with a neurodevelopmental disorder (NDD) characterized by distinctive facial features, hypotonia, and feeding difficulties. TAOK2 variants have been reported to be associated with autism and early-onset obesity. However, a distinct TAOK2-NDD has not yet been delineated. METHODS: We retrospectively studied the clinical and genetic data of individuals recruited from several centers with TAOK1 and TAOK2 variants that were detected through exome and genome sequencing. RESULTS: We report 50 individuals with TAOK1 variants with associated phenotypes, including neurodevelopmental abnormalities (100%), macrocephaly (83%), and hypotonia (58%). We report male genital anomalies and hypoglycemia as novel phenotypes. Thirty-seven unique TAOK1 variants were identified. Most of the missense variants clustered in the protein kinase domain at residues that are intolerant to missense variation. We report 10 individuals with TAOK2 variants with associated phenotypes, including neurodevelopmental abnormalities (100%), macrocephaly (75%), autism (75%), and obesity (70%). CONCLUSION: We describe the largest cohort of TAOK1-NDD to date, to our knowledge, expanding its phenotype and genotype spectrum with 30 novel variants. We delineated the phenotype of a novel TAOK2-NDD associated with neurodevelopmental abnormalities, autism, macrocephaly, and obesity.","author_count":72,"contributors":["Elkhateeb, Nour","Crookes, Renarta","Spiller, Michael","Pavinato, Lisa","Palermo, Flavia","Brusco, Alfredo","Parker, Michael","Park, Soo Mi","Mendes, Ariana Costa","Saraiva, Jorge M.","Hammer, Trine Bjørg","Nazaryan-Petersen, Lusine","Barakat, Tahsin Stefan","Wilke, Martina","Bhoj, Elizabeth","Ahrens-Nicklas, Rebecca C.","Li, Dong","Nomakuchi, Tomoki","Brilstra, Eva H.","Hunt, David","Johnson, Diana","Mansour, Sahar","Oprych, Kathryn","Mehta, Sarju G.","Platzer, Konrad","Schnabel, Franziska","Kiep, Henriette","Faust, Helene","Prinzing, Gillian","Wiltrout, Kimberly","Radley, Jessica A.","Serrano Russi, Alvaro H.","Atallah, Isis","Campos-Xavier, Belinda","Amor, David J.","Morgan, Angela T.","Fagerberg, Christina","Andersen, Ulla A.","Andersen, Charlotte B.","Bijlsma, Emilia K.","Bird, Lynne M.","Mullegama, Sureni V.","Green, Andrew","Isidor, Bertrand","Cogné, Benjamin","Kenny, Janna","Lynch, Sally A.","Quin, Shauna","Low, Karen","Herget, Theresia","Kortüm, Fanny","Levy, Rebecca J.","Morrison, Jennifer L.","Wheeler, Patricia G.","Narumanch, Tara Chandra","Peron, Kristina","Matthews, Nicole","Uhlman, Jillian","Bell, Lauren","Pang, Lewis","Scurr, Ingrid","Belles, Rebecca S.","Salbert, Bonnie Anne","Schaefer, Gerald Bradley","Green, Sarah","Ros, Andrea","Rodríguez-Palmero, Agustí","Višnjar, Tanja","Writzl, Karin","Vasudevan, Pradeep C.","Balasubramanian, Meena"],"cuid":["S02-099.64-804454"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Balasubramanian, Meena"],"country":["Australia","France","Germany","Ireland","Italy","Netherlands","Poland","Portugal","Slovenia","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Arnold Palmer Hospital for Children – Orlando Health","Boston Children's Hospital","Cambridge University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia","Coimbra University","Department of Neuroradiology, St George's University Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust, Blackshaw Road, London, SW17 0QT, UK.","East Tennessee State University","Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","Erasmus University Rotterdam","Geisinger Health System","Geisinger Medical Center","GeneDX Inc","Germans Trias","Germans Tr