{"abstract":"Eco-industrial clusters are increasingly recognized for facilitating sector coupling and integrating energy systems by leveraging the inherent flexibility of renewable energy sources, industrial demand, and energy storage solutions. This systemic integration promotes both economic efficiency and a sustainable energy transition. GreenLab Skive (GLS), a pioneering eco-industrial cluster in Denmark, exemplifies Power-to-X (PtX) technologies within an industrial symbiosis network. As part of GLS’s investment roadmap, it is essential to incorporate emerging technologies to enhance flexibility and profitability. One promising approach is to enable current and prospective cluster participants to contribute to providing frequency ancillary services for the electrical grid. To capitalize on this opportunity, it is necessary to identify and unlock the ancillary service capabilities of individual cluster components. This paper investigates the potential ancillary services that can be provided by components within GLS, specifically wind and solar farms, battery storage, heat pump systems, and power-to-X processes. The flexibility characteristics of these units are analyzed and compared through simulation studies focusing on start-up times, load variation capabilities, ramp rate limits, and operating ranges relevant to ancillary service provision. These insights are intended to inform future investment strategies and can serve as selection criteria within a smart energy system framework to identify which participants are best suited to contribute to ancillary service provision in GLS. This project is funded by Villum Fonden grant 65732 in collaboration with GreenLab.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Roozbehani, Sam","Savaghebi, Mehdi","Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","Nami, Hossein","Ardehali, Armin","Wenzel, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-827341"],"event":{"end":"2025-09-17","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2025-09-16","title":"11th International Conference on Smart Energy Systems","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Battery storage","Eco industrial clusters","GreenLab Skive","Heat pump systems","Power to X"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unlocking frequency ancillary services potential in eco industrial clusters","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-827341","ids":["dtu-06d2855e-1467-41a9-afe3-9b2cea8a46ab"],"keyword":["Battery storage","Eco-industrial clusters","Frequency ancillary services","GreenLab Skive","Heat pump systems","Power-to-X","Wind and solar farms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-33D1E15DE99A881C092845D8F781C68E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics, Energy Technology and Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sam","key":"roozbehanipau","last":"Roozbehani","locid":"8768dbac-e836-4152-afb8-39f8761d9c4f","name":"Roozbehani, Sam","orcid":"0000-0001-9834-8838","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mehdi","key":"savaghebipau","last":"Savaghebi","locid":"7ebeb655-301a-474f-864b-63251327d474","name":"Savaghebi, Mehdi","orcid":"0000-0001-6188-0265","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a1d488b0-5bf1-4eee-bdd5-cfe37a89528a","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hossein","key":"namipau","last":"Nami","name":"Nami, Hossein","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Armin","key":"ardehalipau","last":"Ardehali","name":"Ardehali, Armin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"wenzelpau","last":"Wenzel","name":"Wenzel, Henrik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["13. Climate Action","7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-06d2855e-1467-41a9-afe3-9b2cea8a46ab"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Unlocking Frequency Ancillary Services Potential in Eco-Industrial Clusters","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-827341","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Mozzarella cheese is a key ingredient in many cuisines, valued for its creamy texture and its exceptional popularity as a pizza topping. The unique melting and stretching behavior is closely linked to its structural anisotropy, which can be modulated by production conditions. The textural anisotropy of the cheese significantly influences its viscoelastic and thermodynamic properties when heated. This paper explores how process pa- rameters influence mozzarella structure, utilizing Fluorescence Anisotropy (FA) and Oblique Incidence Reflectometry (OIR) for anisotropy quantification. To corroborate the results, our study incorporates detailed microstructural analysis via X-ray computed tomography (CT). The ultimate product functionality of the mozzarella cheese is evaluated from both a consumer and quality perspective by assessing its performance in pizza baking. The key findings of our study indicate that the determinations of anisotropy by FA and OIR are highly correlated with each other and with important functional properties and process parameters. Functional parameters associated with blisters negatively correlate with anisotropy, while oiling and meltability exhibit a positive correlation with anisotropy values. The anisotropy values observed through FA and OIR further align closely with CT images, as well as with pizza functionality and consumer tests.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Patel, Harshkumar","Pieta, Pawel Tomasz","Wang, Lezhong","Bigdeli, Siavash Arjomand","Christensen, Anders Nymark","Dahl, Anders Bjorholm","Frisvad, Jeppe Revall","Bejder, Kristina Schmidt","Ortega-Anaya, Joana","Andersen, Ulf","Engelsen, Søren Balling","van den Berg, Frans W. J."],"cuid":["S02-099.73-804350"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Anisotropy","Computed tomography","Fluorescence","Incident Reflectometry","Mozzarella","Pizza functionality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization and quantification of anisotropy in mozzarella cheese exploring the impact of structural anisotropy on functional properties using complementary analytical technologies","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.foostr.2025.100425","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.73-804350","identifier":[{"id":"105001992533","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-351e6852-7e67-46f7-8102-e56cd55e0ae8","ku-162f30a7-ed36-426c-bb8a-faa2fdb9d802"],"keyword":["Anisotropy","Computed Tomography","Fluorescence","Incident Reflectometry","Mozzarella","Pizza functionality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1770CC8F3F6EA78A1A482AAEC1488C46"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/449440506/1-s2.0-S2213329125000206-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.foostr.2025.100425","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/398655695/1-s2.0-S2213329125000206-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Analytics and Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Visual Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"arla foods","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-ARLA","l3nl":"Arla Foods","l3nn":"Arla Foods","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Arla Foods","namevar":["Arla Foods"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-ARLA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Harshkumar","key":"patelpau","last":"Patel","locid":"9fd696a9-312a-4577-9994-ce2a33f129b8","name":"Patel, Harshkumar","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pawel Tomasz","key":"pietapau","last":"Pieta","locid":"2fe49bb5-6401-403b-b34e-e59131545850","name":"Pieta, Pawel Tomasz","orcid":"0009-0005-7634-6627","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lezhong","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"56ce96b4-5ddd-4830-ba4e-b94e35feed15","name":"Wang, Lezhong","orcid":"0000-0001-8433-1672","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Siavash","key":"bigdelipau","last":"Bigdeli","locid":"f0331bdc-af5c-4d12-8064-1fbe87032f97","name":"Bigdeli, Siavash Arjomand","name_org":"Bigdeli, Siavash","orcid":"0000-0003-2569-6473","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Nymark","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"ad9ef4bc-d943-459d-b52f-a11c61a9ab0d","name":"Christensen, Anders Nymark","orcid":"0000-0002-3668-3128","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Bjorholm","key":"dahlpau","last":"Dahl","locid":"c2bad3c8-b172-481b-bb99-d3c2bc4004ef","name":"Dahl, Anders Bjorholm","orcid":"0000-0002-0068-8170","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe Revall","key":"frisvadpau","last":"Frisvad","locid":"e7a06e6e-86d5-454f-a78b-c998215c6169","name":"Frisvad, Jeppe Revall","orcid":"0000-0002-0603-3669","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Schmidt","key":"bejderpau","last":"Bejder","name":"Bejder, Kristina Schmidt","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Joana","key":"ortegaanayapau","last":"Ortega-Anaya","name":"Ortega-Anaya, Joana","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulf","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Ulf","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Balling","key":"engelsenpau","last":"Engelsen","locid":"dd20dadd-5356-4314-bb70-4fe2b03328d5","name":"Engelsen, Søren Balling","orcid":"0000-0003-4124-4338","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frans W.J.","key":"vandenbergpau","last":"van den Berg","locid":"14f75f40-736f-4e4d-bb04-10290e036d0f","name":"van der Berg, Franciscus Winfried J","name_org":"van den Berg, Frans W.J.","orcid":"0000-0002-9170-9052","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.foostr.2025.100425","issn":["22133291"],"journal":"Food Structure","paperid":"100425","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Food Structure","volume":"44"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001992533"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Arla Foods","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-351e6852-7e67-46f7-8102-e56cd55e0ae8","ku-162f30a7-ed36-426c-bb8a-faa2fdb9d802"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Characterization and quantification of anisotropy in mozzarella cheese: Exploring the impact of structural anisotropy on functional properties using complementary analytical technologies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.73-804350","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Charcot-Marie Tooth (CMT) is a hereditary neuropathy characterized by muscle weakness and fatigue with no approved therapies. Preclinical studies implicate neuromuscular junction (NMJ) transmission deficits in muscle dysfunction in CMT. This study aimed to evaluate NMJ function in patients with CMT types 1 and 2, and to determine whether enhancing NMJ transmission can improve muscle function in preclinical CMT models. METHODS: First, an observational study involving single fiber electromyography (SFEMG) and clinical testing in patients with CMT 1 and 2 and healthy controls (HC) was conducted. Next, preclinical studies examined muscle function, specifically nerve-stimulated muscle force after partially inhibiting ClC-1 chloride channels with the novel small molecule NMD670. RESULTS: Twenty-one CMT patients (46.4 ± 14.4 years) and 10 HC (43.3 ± 12.7 years) were enrolled. SFEMG jitter (NMJ variability) was higher [median (range)] in the CMT patients [56 μs (35; 197 μs)] vs. HC [29 μs (19; 36 μs)], (p < 0.05). Blocking (NMJ failure) was higher in the CMT patients (13.4% (0.0; 90.9%)) vs. HC (0.0% (0.0; 4.5%)), (p < 0.05). In CMT, jitter and blocking correlated inversely with muscle strength, mobility, balance, and endurance. In CMT 1A and 2D mice, NMD670 increased both peak force and contractile endurance in vivo. INTERPRETATION: Our study suggests that NMJ dysfunction contributes to muscle dysfunction in patients with CMT 1 and 2. Furthermore, our preclinical data provide proof-of-mechanism for recovery of muscle function with ClC-1 inhibition in CMT mouse models. Collectively, these findings suggest that targeting NMJ dysfunction with ClC-1 inhibitors could enhance muscle function in CMT patients, warranting further clinical trials.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Grønnebæk, Thomas Skjærlund","Haahr-Lillevang, Helga","Skov, Martin","Kelly, Kristina","Kerr, Nathan R.","Viteri, Jose A.","Jaworek, Andrea","Bartlett, Amy","Bold, Jane","Hutchison, John","Quiroz, Jorge","Tankisi, Hatice","Pedersen, Thomas Holm","Andersen, Henning","Arnold, William David"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-796486"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Henning","Arnold, William David","Pedersen, Thomas Holm"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ohio State University","University of Missouri"],"keyword":["Adult","Animals","Disease Models Animal","Electromyography","Female","Humans","Male","Mice","Middle Aged","Synaptic Transmission physiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neuromuscular transmission deficits in patients with cmt and clc 000000000001 inhibition in cmt animal models","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/acn3.52252","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-796486","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11822784","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85213697524","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39670429","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-7d59bae6-a496-47d2-923a-e5545bbd431b"],"keyword":["Adult","Animals","Charcot-Marie-Tooth Disease/physiopathology","Chloride Channels/antagonists & inhibitors","Disease Models, Animal","Electromyography","Female","Humans","Male","Mice","Middle Aged","Neuromuscular Junction/physiopathology","Synaptic Transmission/physiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E8B21D4050F50BF73008183DC87907AF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/acn3.52252","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key