{"abstract":"In this population-based, nationwide Danish cohort study, bacterial meningitis in childhood was associated with increased neurological morbidity. The risks were highest among young children, who also received more antiepileptic medication. All children had increased frequency of hospital visits. These findings highlight the importance of follow-up after bacterial meningitis in children.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Graham, Emma E.","Tetens, Malte M.","Bodilsen, Jacob","Andersen, Nanna S.","Dessau, Ram","Ellermann-Eriksen, Svend","Franck, Kristina","Midgley, Sofie","Møller, Jens Kjølseth","Nielsen, Alex Christian","Nielsen, Lene","Søgaard, Kirstine K.","Østergaard, Christian","Lebech, Anne-Mette","Nygaard, Ulrikka","Omland, Lars H.","Obel, Niels"],"cuid":["S04-095.00-793021"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Graham, Emma E."],"keyword":["Adolescent","Anticonvulsants therapeutic use","Bacterial meningitis","Child","Child Preschool","Childhood","Cohort Studies","Cohort study","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Infant","Infant Newborn","Male","Meningitis Bacterial drug therapy","Nervous System Diseases","Neurological disorders","Pediatric"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"neurological disorders and use of healthcare services after bacterial meningitis in childhood a nationwide population based cohort study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"acc