{"abstract":"Allogenic hematopoietic cell transplantation (allo-HCT) with myeloablative conditioning traditionally requires 30 days of hospitalization after stem cell infusion. However, advancements in supportive and prophylactic care have allowed for a trend toward outpatient management of allo-HCT, potentially leading to improved patient quality of life and increased cost-effectiveness of the procedure. In 2014, fludarabine and treosulfan (FluTreo) conditioning was introduced as a myeloablative regimen with reduced toxicity at Copenhagen University Hospital, Rigshospitalet (CUH). After gaining experience with the regimen, an outpatient program was established. Here we share the outcomes of outpatient conditioning with FluTreo allo-HCT at CUH. This study was conducted to investigate the safety and feasibility of outpatient FluTreo allo-HCT, as well as to investigate the potentially improved cost-effectiveness of outpatient allo-HCT primarily through a reduction in hospital length of stay compared to the 30 days of hospitalization associated with standard myeloablative conditioning. This retrospective study included all patients undergoing FluTreo allo-HCT due to malignant diseases (n = 124) at CUH between 2018 and 2022. Patients received outpatient treatment (n = 91) unless certain circumstances necessitated planned hospitalization (n = 33). As conditioning, patients received i.v. fludarabine 90 mg/m2 and treosulfan either 30 or 42 g/m2. Statistical analyses included descriptive statistics and Kaplan-Meier survival analysis. The median duration of hospitalization in the outpatient group was 4 days (interquartile range [IQR], 0 to 12.5 days) from day -6 to day +28 compared to a median of 28 days (IQR, 26 to 34 days) in the inpatient group. Thirty-two patients (35%) in the outpatient group did not require hospitalization before day +28 post-transplantation. The remaining 59 patients (65%) were hospitalized after a median of 12 days (IQR, 7 to 16 days) from the start of conditioning, with a median stay of 10 days (IQR, 5 to 18 days). The outpatient group required significantly less i.v. antibiotics, i.v. opioids, and parenteral nutrition compared to the inpatient group, despite no differences in treatment toxicity, acute graft-versus-host disease, or relapse between the groups. The outpatient group experienced no early deaths during the first 3 months after transplantation, and 1-year nonrelapse mortality was 6%. Outpatient allo-HCT with FluTreo conditioning is feasible and safe in a selected group of patients, significantly reducing hospitalization days without compromising patient outcomes. Outpatient FluTreo allo-HCT potentially provides a more cost-effective and patient-friendly alternative compared to traditional in-patient management.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Schovsbo, Johanne Skovgaard","Kjeldsen, Lars","Nørskov, Kristina Holmegaard","Sengeløv, Henrik","Kornblit, Brian Thomas","Schjødt, Ida","Petersen, Søren Lykke","Nygaard, Marietta","Andersen, Niels Smedegaard","Mortensen, Bo Kok","Friis, Lone Smidstrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-800969"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Acute myeloid leukemia","Conditioning regimen","Fludarabine","Myelodysplastic syndrome","Outpatient"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outpatient management of patients conditioned with fludarabine and treosulfan prior to allogeneic hematopoietic cell transplantation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtct.2024.11.001","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-800969","identifier":[{"id":"39522721","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85210387710","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-fa172837-f2fa-4458-a71d-5569b230d080"],"keyword":["Acute myeloid leukemia","Allogenic hematopoietic cell transplantation","Conditioning regimen","Fludarabine","Myelodysplastic syndrome","Outpatient","Treosulfan"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7F0DF2EFFFC51058735D350ECD9E32A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtct.2024.11.001","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/424525259/1_s2.0_S2666636724007462_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Johanne Skovgaard","key":"schovsbopau","last":"Schovsbo","name":"Schovsbo, Johanne Skovgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","name":"Kjeldsen, Lars","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina Holmegaard","key":"nørskovpau","last":"Nørskov","name":"Nørskov, Kristina Holmegaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"sengeløvpau","last":"Sengeløv","name":"Sengeløv, Henrik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Brian Thomas","key":"kornblitpau","last":"Kornblit","name":"Kornblit, Brian Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ida","key":"schjødtpau","last":"Schjødt","name":"Schjødt, Ida","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren Lykke","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Søren Lykke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marietta","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","name":"Nygaard, Marietta","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels Smedegaard","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Niels Smedegaard","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo Kok","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, Bo Kok","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Lone Smidstrup","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","locid":"c9477b15-4c60-45e6-be1c-9a19c91f4826","name":"Friis, Lone Smidstrup","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39522721"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jtct.2024.11.001","issn":["26666367"],"issn_org":["26666375"],"issue":"1","journal":"Transplantation and Cellular Therapy","status":"p","title":"Transplantation and Cellular Therapy","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85210387710"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-fa172837-f2fa-4458-a71d-5569b230d080"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Outpatient Management of Patients Conditioned with Fludarabine and Treosulfan prior to Allogeneic Hematopoietic Cell Transplantation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-800969","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Advances in treating classic Hodgkin lymphoma (cHL) have improved cure rates, with overall survival exceeding 80%, resulting in a growing population of survivors at risk of long-term complications, particularly cardiac and pulmonary toxicity. Bleomycin, a key component of combination chemotherapy, is associated with bleomycin-induced pulmonary toxicity (BPT). Using label-free quantification nano liquid chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry, protein expression in diagnostic lymphoma samples from patients with and without BPT was compared. Results showed differential protein expression and disrupted cellular pathways, suggesting biological differences in BPT risk. Immunohistochemical analysis revealed higher expression of JAK3, BID, and MMP9, and lower expression of CD20, TPD52, and PIK3R4 in patients with BPT. High BID and low CD20 expression were associated with inferior overall survival, while high BID and low JAK3 and CD20 expression were linked to poorer progression-free survival. These findings highlight altered protein profiles in pretreatment cHL biopsies associated with BPT development.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Andersen, Maja Dam","Wolter, Katharina","Enemark, Marie Beck","Lauridsen, Kristina Lystlund","Hamilton-Dutoit, Stephen Jacques","Starklint, Jørn","D'Amore, Francesco Annibale","Ludvigsen, Maja","Honoré, Bent","Kamper, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805744"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Maja Dam","Honoré, Bent"],"keyword":["FFPE tissue","Prognosis","Proteomics","classic Hodgkin lymphoma cHL"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proteomic profiling identifies classic hodgkin lymphoma patients at risk of bleomycin pulmonary toxicity","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/10428194.2024.2434170","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-805744","identifier":[{"id":"85211113995","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39625996","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-02426e1c-146a-4fd7-bf53-77d84c689d61"],"keyword":["Bleomycin pulmonary toxicity (BPT)","FFPE-tissue","classic Hodgkin lymphoma (cHL)","prognosis","proteomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2737F1440A6CD90EC9A1231F19EE060E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/10428194.2024.2434170","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/433180884/Proteomic_profiling_identifies_classic_Hodgkin_lymphoma_patients_at_risk_of_bleomycin_pulmonary_toxicity.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Haematology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja Dam","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"23ba761f-55f2-41a8-80be-5b028946efbd","name":"Andersen, Maja Dam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Katharina","key":"wolterpau","last":"Wolter","locid":"acdee6f6-f5d7-4066-ac97-1c0579b13b96","name":"Wolter, Katharina","orcid":"0009-0000-2454-1133","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie Hairing","key":"enemarkpau","last":"Enemark","locid":"d7854a01-8da3-4657-8f9c-eebb7d2d8df3","name":"Enemark, Marie Beck","name_org":"Enemark, Marie Hairin