ame":"Brault, Jeffrey J.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Uma","key":"sankarpau","last":"Sankar","name":"Sankar, Uma","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"David H.","key":"drewrypau","last":"Drewry","name":"Drewry, David H.","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 9 10","first":"John W.","key":"scottpau","last":"Scott","name":"Scott, John W.","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Carol A.","key":"witczakpau","last":"Witczak","name":"Witczak, Carol A.","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kei","key":"sakamotopau","last":"Sakamoto","locid":"96cdccaf-7de8-4b0b-898c-e1ee3d972ee6","name":"Sakamoto, Kei","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37380024"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.molmet.2023.101761","issn":["22128778"],"journal":"Molecular Metabolism","paperid":"101761","status":"p","title":"Molecular Metabolism","volume":"75"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164661974"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b34f4a5a-8314-4d15-81b2-2ee7424b8440"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"CaMKK2 is not involved in contraction-stimulated AMPK activation and glucose uptake in skeletal muscle","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-684395","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"A method to detect and quantify aggregated α-synuclein (αSYN) fibrils in vivo would drastically impact the current understanding of multiple neurodegenerative diseases, revolutionizing their diagnosis and treatment. Several efforts have produced promising scaffolds, but a notable challenge has hampered the establishment of a clinically successful αSYN positron emission tomography (PET) tracer: the requirement of high selectivity over the other misfolded proteins amyloid β (Aβ) and tau. By designing and screening a library of 2-styrylbenzothiazoles based on the selective fluorescent probe RB1, this study aimed at developing a selective αSYN PET tracer. [3H]PiB competition binding assays identified PFSB (Ki = 25.4 ± 2.3 nM) and its less lipophilic analogue MFSB, which exhibited enhanced affinity to αSYN (Ki = 10.3 ± 4.7 nM) and preserved selectivity over Aβ. The two lead compounds were labeled with fluorine-18 and evaluated using in vitro autoradiography on human brain slices, where they demonstrated up to 4-fold increased specific binding in MSA cases compared to the corresponding control, reasonably reflecting selective binding to αSYN pathology. In vivo PET imaging showed [18F]MFSB successfully crosses the blood-brain barrier (BBB) and is taken up in the brain (SUV = 1.79 ± 0.02). Although its pharmacokinetic profile raises the need for additional structural optimization, [18F]MFSB represents a critical step forward in the development of a successful αSYN PET tracer by overcoming the major challenge of αSYN/Aβ selectivity.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Di Nanni, Adriana","Saw, Ran Sing","Battisti, Umberto Maria","Bowden, Gregory D.","Boeckermann, Adam","Bjerregaard-Andersen, Kaare","Pichler, Bernd J.","Herfert, Kristina","Herth, Matthias M.","Maurer, Andreas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-696005"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Tübingen"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a fluorescent probe as a lead compound for a selective α synuclein pet tracer development of a library of 000000000002 styrylbenzothiazoles and biological evaluation of sup 000000000018 sup f pfsb and sup 000000000018 sup f mfsb","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acsomega.3c04292","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-696005","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10468942","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85168991767","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37663501","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7fe05fc2-3ef8-47f1-a0d1-eafc115beb79"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3AA4C3D1025B541F4AB24F560D1E845B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/367835875/acsomega.3c04292.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acsomega.3c04292","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of tübingen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Tübingen","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Medicinal Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LUND","l3nl":"Lundbeck Pharma","l3nn":"Lundbeck","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck","namevar":["Lundbeck"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LUND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Adriana","key":"dinannipau","last":"Di Nanni","name":"Di Nanni, Adriana","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ran Sing","key":"sawpau","last":"Saw","name":"Saw, Ran Sing","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Umberto M.","key":"battistipau","last":"Battisti","locid":"101f6f81-0203-4a9d-b80c-b6470d4baa78","name":"Battisti, Umberto Maria","name_org":"Battisti, Umberto M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Gregory D.","key":"bowdenpau","last":"Bowden","name":"Bowden, Gregory D.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adam","key":"boeckermannpau","last":"Boeckermann","name":"Boeckermann, Adam","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kaare","key":"bjerregaardandersenpau","last":"Bjerregaard-Andersen","name":"Bjerregaard-Andersen, Kaare","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bernd J.","key":"pichlerpau","last":"Pichler","name":"Pichler, Bernd J.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina","key":"herfertpau","last":"Herfert","name":"Herfert, Kristina","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Matthias M.","key":"herthpau","last":"Herth","locid":"001339a3-ac7c-4378-bfd6-c13d689a5f6f","name":"Herth, Matthias M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"maurerpau","last":"Maurer","name":"Maurer, Andreas","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37663501"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acsomega.3c04292","issn":["24701343"],"issue":"34","journal":"ACS Omega","pages":"31450-31467","status":"p","title":"ACS Omega","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168991767"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Lundbeck Pharma","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7fe05fc2-3ef8-47f1-a0d1-eafc115beb79"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Fluorescent Probe as a Lead Compound for a Selective α-Synuclein PET Tracer : Development of a Library of 2-Styrylbenzothiazoles and Biological Evaluation of [<sup>18</sup>F]PFSB and [<sup>18</sup>F]MFSB","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-696005","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: The socioeconomic differences in survival are pronounced for patients diagnosed with head and neck cancer; disease stage at diagnosis is suggested to be a main driver of this association. This nationwide, population-based study investigates socioeconomic differences in the pre-diagnostic interval and disease stage at diagnosis. Material and Methods: Information on patient-reported symptoms, symptom onset and disease-specific factors was obtained from the nationwide population-based Danish Head and Neck Cancer Group (DAHANCA) database for patients diagnosed with head and neck squamous cell carcinoma between 2008 and 2019 in Denmark. Socioeconomic position (SEP) was measured by individual-level education, income and cohabitation status obtained from administrative registers. Socioeconomic differences in the interval from symptom onset to diagnosis were investigated in general linear models with 95% confidence intervals (CIs); overall and by subsite, symptom and comorbidity score. Consultation patterns prior to diagnosis were examined using methods for change-point detection. Associations with advanced-stage disease were estimated in logistic regression models. Results: Patients with low, medium and high SEP had a similar interval from patient-reported symptom onset to diagnosis of 10 weeks. Although this interval varied according to primary symptom and anatomical subsite, no apparent socioeconomic differences were observed within these subgroups. Aligned with the patient-reported symptom onset, a distinct increase in consultation rates was observed at 9 weeks (95% CI [7.3; 10.7]) for patients with low SEP and 7 weeks (95% CI [4.8; 9.2]) for patients with high SEP, with overlapping CIs. Patients with low compared to high SEP had increased odds for advanced-stage glottic and oral cavity squamous cell carcinoma. For the remaining subsites the association varied according to SEP-indicator and TNM-edition. Conclusion: The interval from symptom onset to diagnosis and consultation patterns were similar across SEP groups. Still, socioeconomic differences in stage at diagnosis were observed for some–but not all–subsites.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Halgren Olsen, Maja","Maltesen, Thomas","Lassen, Pernille","Kjaer, Trille Kristina","Johansen, Jørgen","Primdahl, Hanne","Andersen, Elo","Kristensen, Claus Andrup","Andersen, Maria","Farhadi, Mohammad","Overgaard, Jens","Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713946"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-21","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2023-06-20","title":"21st Acta Oncologica Symposium—BiGART 2023 - Biology-Guided Adaptive Radiotherapy","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Halgren Olsen, Maja"],"keyword":["Carcinoma Squamous Cell pathology","Diagnostic interval","Head and Neck Neoplasms","Head and neck cancer","Humans","Income","Inequality","Socioeconomic Factors","Socioeconomic position","Squamous Cell Carcinoma of Head and Neck","Symptoms","disease stage"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socioeconomic position and the pre diagnostic interval among patients diagnosed with head and neck squamous cell carcinoma a population based study from dahanca","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85169934797","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was funded by the Danish Cancer Society"],"id":"S01-000.00-713946","identifier":[{"id":"37672036","type