16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168915195"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0d69d78b-6fbd-4b42-a247-06a4caebd5ca","sdu-273b1a22-5df7-4f2b-828a-6a951b84525f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Cannabis-Based Medicine for Neuropathic Pain and Spasticity-A Multicenter, Randomized, Double-Blinded, Placebo-Controlled Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.76-685835","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"For organizations to stay competitive, organizational culture must constantly adapt to fit changes in the environment and organizational knowledge. Extant literature has analyzed how sudden events such as environmental jolts, threats or strategic cultural molding may change organizational culture, but the literature has neglected gradual, longitudinal changes to organizational culture. This paper presents an analysis of organizational culture change as a longitudinal organizational learning process. We use unique longitudinal interview data with 38 firms collected in 2006 and 2018 to analyze how the initial organizational culture and organizational learning change organization culture. Our findings show that organizations with different organizational cultures at the start of the studied period went through different organizational culture changes, while organizations with similar organizational cultures dis- played similar organizational culture changes. This indicates that an organization’s initial culture functions as a pattern for both learning and changes in organizational culture. Even when exposed to similar environmental development, organizations are so to speak caught in culture. Our findings contribute to the literature on both organizational learning and organizational culture with a much-needed integration of these to related perspectives on organizational knowledge.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wolf, Patricia","Kocher, Pierre-Yves","Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","Steppe, Jessica"],"cuid":["S02-080.99-704445"],"event":{"end":"2023-06-12","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2023-06-10","title":"83rd Annual Meeting of the Academy of Management","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"caught in culture how interaction between organizational culture and learning causes patterns in organizational culture change","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-080.99-704445","ids":["dtu-19afadf3-495f-471a-b221-d70ae8f8b982","dtu-4f668c29-618f-4f39-b5ae-841d0832592e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-47EDBB0151BA053C7CB55DB346157CEE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics, Business Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Patricia","key":"wolfpau","last":"Wolf","name":"Wolf, Patricia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Pierre-Yves","key":"kocherpau","last":"Kocher","name":"Kocher, Pierre-Yves","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a1d488b0-5bf1-4eee-bdd5-cfe37a89528a","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jessica","key":"steppepau","last":"Steppe","name":"Steppe, Jessica","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-19afadf3-495f-471a-b221-d70ae8f8b982","dtu-4f668c29-618f-4f39-b5ae-841d0832592e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Caught in culture? How interaction between organizational culture and learning causes patterns in organizational culture change","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.99-704445","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The RNA-binding ARS2 protein is centrally involved in both early RNA polymerase II (RNAPII) transcription termination and transcript decay. Despite its essential nature, the mechanisms by which ARS2 enacts these functions have remained unclear. Here, we show that a conserved basic domain of ARS2 binds a corresponding acidic-rich, short linear motif (SLiM) in the transcription restriction factor ZC3H4. This interaction recruits ZC3H4 to chromatin to elicit RNAPII termination, independent of other early termination pathways defined by the cleavage and polyadenylation (CPA) and Integrator (INT) complexes. We find that ZC3H4, in turn, forms a direct connection to the nuclear exosome targeting (NEXT) complex, hereby facilitating rapid degradation of the nascent RNA. Hence, ARS2 instructs the coupled transcription termination and degradation of the transcript onto which it is bound. This contrasts with ARS2 function at CPA-instructed termination sites where the protein exclusively partakes in RNA suppression via post-transcriptional decay.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Rouvière, Jérôme O.","Salerno-Kochan, Anna","Lykke-Andersen, Søren","Garland, William","Dou, Yuhui","Rathore, Om","Molska, Ewa Šmidová","Wu, Guifen","Schmid, Manfred","Bugai, Andrii","Jakobsen, Lis","Žumer, Kristina","Cramer, Patrick","Andersen, Jens S.","Conti, Elena","Jensen, Torben Heick"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-681396"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Torben Heick"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Multidisciplinary Sciences","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"keyword":["ARS2","CPA complex","INT complex","NEXT","PAXT","RNA decay","ZC3H4","early transcription termination"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ars000000000002 instructs early transcription termination coupled rna decay by recruiting zc000000000003h000000000004 to nascent transcripts","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85164271697","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-681396","identifier":[{"id":"85164271697","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37329882","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-868ab534-6b7c-444c-93c7-ca2b92c84c4d","sdu-779876ef-d66e-402d-a1e8-53a4b4e38236"],"keyword":["ARS2","CPA complex","INT complex","NEXT","PAXT","RNA decay","ZC3H4","early transcription termination"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6A85209BB4C6F9C51F5162663D7757BF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - RNA Biology and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biochemistry","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Biomedical Mass Spectrom