&s=LOI:S04-093.93-715743","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Transportation noise may induce cardiovascular disease, but the public health implications are unclear. OBJECTIVES: The study aimed to assess exposure-response relationships for different transportation noise sources and ischemic heart disease (IHD), including subtypes. METHODS: Pooled analyses were performed of nine cohorts from Denmark and Sweden, together including 132,801 subjects. Time-weighted long-term exposure to road, railway, and aircraft noise, as well as air pollution, was estimated based on residential histories. Hazard ratios (HRs) were calculated using Cox proportional hazards models following adjustment for lifestyle and socioeconomic risk factors. RESULTS: A total of 22,459 incident cases of IHD were identified during follow-up from national patient and mortality registers, including 7,682 cases of myocardial infarction. The adjusted HR for IHD was 1.03 [95% confidence interval (CI) 1.00, 1.05] per 10 dB formula presented for both road and railway noise exposure during 5 y prior to the event. Higher risks were indicated for IHD excluding angina pectoris cases, with HRs of 1.06 (95% CI: 1.03, 1.08) and 1.05 (95% CI: 1.01, 1.08) per 10 dB formula presented for road and railway noise, respectively. Corresponding HRs for myocardial infarction were 1.02 (95% CI: 0.99, 1.05) and 1.04 (95% CI: 0.99, 1.08). Increased risks were observed for aircraft noise but without clear exposure-response relations. A threshold at around 55 dB formula presented was suggested in the exposure-response relation for road traffic noise and IHD. DISCUSSION: Exposure to road, railway, and aircraft noise in the prior 5 y was associated with an increased risk of IHD, particularly after exclusion of angina pectoris cases, which are less well identified in the registries. https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP10745.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Pyko, Andrei","Roswall, Nina","Ögren, Mikael","Oudin, Anna","Rosengren, Annika","Eriksson, Charlotta","Segersson, David","Rizzuto, Debora","Andersson, Eva M","Aasvang, Gunn Marit","Engström, Gunnar","Gudjonsdottir, Hrafnhildur","Jørgensen, Jeanette T","Selander, Jenny","Christensen, Jesper Heile","Brandt, Jørgen","Leander, Karin","Overvad, Kim","Eneroth, Kristina","Mattisson, Kristoffer","Barregard, Lars","Stockfelt, Leo","Albin, Maria","Simonsen, Mette K","Tiittanen, Pekka","Molnar, Peter","Ljungman, Petter","Jensen, Steen Solvang","Gustafsson, Susanna","Lanki, Timo","Lim, Youn-Hee","Andersen, Zorana J","Sørensen, Mette","Pershagen, Göran"],"cuid":["S04-099.71-007021"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Pyko, Andrei"],"country":["Finland","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","City of Malmö","City of Stockholm","Danderyd Hospital","Danderyds Hospital","Environment and Health Administration","Finnish Institute for Health and Welfare","Finnish Ministry of Social Affairs and Health","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Lund University","National Institute for Health and Welfare","Norwegian Institute of Public Health","Region Stockholm","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Stockholm Environment and Health Protection Administration","Stockholm Gerontology Research Center","Stockholm University","Svensk kommun","Swedish Meteorological and Hydrological Institute","Umeå University","University of Eastern Finland","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["Angina pectoris","Environmental Exposure","Humans","Myocardial Infarction epidemiology","Myocardial Ischemia epidemiology","Noise Transportation adverse effects"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term exposure to transportation noise and ischemic heart disease a pooled analysis of nine scandinavian cohorts","src":["aau","au","ku","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://ehp.niehs.nih.gov/about-ehp/copyright-permissions","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP10745","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-099.71-007021","identifier":[{"id":"36607286","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85145955612","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9819217","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-90d784bc-33c6-4389-9f6a-b375e840204a","au-02ccdbce-d4bd-4440-8698-87b329b92a4c","ku-15655449-5e63-44e7-b55f-eb818646f301","ruc-2e731142-ae21-4f19-ad67-837dd917dc72"],"keyword":["Angina Pectoris","Environmental Exposure","Humans","Myocardial Infarction/epidemiology","Myocardial Ischemia/epidemiology","Noise, Transportation/adverse effects"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-9644037180BC4F95A3BC0ED4908EBF32"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/332993285/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"https://ehp.niehs.nih.gov/about-ehp/copyright-permissions","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP10745","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"https://ehp.niehs.nih.gov/about-ehp/copyright-permissions","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/88511314/EHP10745.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"region stockholm","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region