tus":"p","title":"Environmental Health Perspectives","volume":"131"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85145955612"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-90d784bc-33c6-4389-9f6a-b375e840204a","au-02ccdbce-d4bd-4440-8698-87b329b92a4c","ku-15655449-5e63-44e7-b55f-eb818646f301","ruc-2e731142-ae21-4f19-ad67-837dd917dc72"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Long-Term Exposure to Transportation Noise and Ischemic Heart Disease : A Pooled Analysis of Nine Scandinavian Cohorts","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.71-007021","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Of all emerging technologies, 3D Printing (or additive manufacturing) certainly made the top list of those that were predicted to “change the world”. Yet, nearly 40 years after is conception and 10 years after the 3D printing ‘hype’, it is hard to find situations where 3D printing has had a radical impact, aside from a few specific niches such as prosthetics and the aerospace industry. Among the predicted benefits of 3D printing was its positive impact on sustainability, by allegedly offering “waste-free manufacturing”. The promise was that only the quantity of material needed in production are actually used. As such, products can be manufactured on demand with only raw materials being transported and so on. Yet, so far, this promise has also struggled to materialise. However, there may be light at the end of the tunnel. As the study presented in this article indicates, where 3D printing has been implemented in industry, it would seem to be a driver of sustainability – particular as a circular economy enabler. - Thierry Rayna, Tech4Change Chair","author_count":3,"contributors":["Knudsen, Mette Præst","Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","Rayna, Thierry"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-637321"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","i3 CNRS","École Polytechnique"],"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000003d printing unexpected ecological benefits for industrials","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.polytechnique-insights.com/en/columns/science/3d-printing-unexpected-ecological-benefits-for-industrials/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-637321","ids":["sdu-dfd7587e-2822-45a5-89af-a7affbdd0129"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-95440ABEEBA427D74D3A18DC05A9340B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.polytechnique-insights.com/en/columns/science/3d-printing-unexpected-ecological-benefits-for-industrials/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM), Centre for Integrative Innovation Management (C*I2M)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"école polytechnique","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"École Polytechnique","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"i3 cnrs","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"i3 CNRS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Præst","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"efc4aa3e-11bb-4546-b241-8ce6dd970891","name":"Knudsen, Mette Præst","orcid":"0000-0002-2055-5308","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"46d2bbb6-cde6-45b4-b04d-dcbcbad97c83","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thierry","key":"raynapau","last":"Rayna","name":"Rayna, Thierry","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["sdu-dfd7587e-2822-45a5-89af-a7affbdd0129"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"3D printing : unexpected ecological benefits for industrials","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-637321","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Poor adherence to cancer treatment is commonly seen [Citation1–3] with consequences including worse overall survival and quality of life [Citation2]. In line with this, almost half (46%) of lung cancer patients did not receive optimal first-line treatment in a Danish nationwide cohort study [Citation4], which was associated with comorbidity, and socioeconomic resources amongst others. Depression has been identified as a risk factor for non-compliance to non-cancer medical treatment in a meta-analysis [Citation5]. Psychological symptoms like depression and anxiety are prevalent among cancer patients [Citation6] and studies show that this is especially so for lung cancer patients [Citation7–9] However, research on the link between anxiety and depression on treatment adherence among lung cancer patients is scarce. Two small prospective studies of non-small cell lung cancer patients (NSCLC) (n = 50–82) reported, that depression was associated with reduced treatment adherence [Citation2] and that anxiety symptoms were associated with reduced adherence to chemotherapy defined as a dose delay or reduction [Citation3]. Greer et al. [Citation3] concluded, that further research is needed to clarify the underlying mechanisms of the association between psychological factors and chemotherapy adherence. The aim of this prospective cohort study was to investigate the associations of anxiety and depression symptoms, measured by The Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale (HADS) [Citation10], with the completion of first-line treatment in newly diagnosed lung cancer patients in Denmark.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Josephine Maffait","Kjaer, Trille Kristina","Mellemgård, Anders","Stensøe Oksen, Marianne","Andersen, Ingelise","Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-690542"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between anxiety and depression symptoms and completion of first line treatment in newly diagnosed lung cancer patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/406088024/Association_between_anxiety_and_depression_symptoms_and_completion_of_first_line_treatment_in_newly_diagnosed_lung_cancer_patients.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-690542","identifier":[{"id":"37162449","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85159091226","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e4ef59cb-71d7-47b8-b4bf-9720534fd7d6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-251AD1D8DAFF695663947CAEBCAF2A0A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/406088024/Association_between_anxiety_and_depression_symptoms_and_completion_of_first_line_treatment_in_newly_diagnosed_lung_cancer_patients.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Josephine Maffait","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Josephine Maffait","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Trille Kristina","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","name":"Kjaer, Trille Kristina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"mellemgårdpau","last":"Mellemgård","name":"Mellemgård, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marianne","key":"stensøeoksenpau","last":"Stensøe Oksen","name":"Stensøe Oksen, Marianne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ingelise","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"f45f4a92-ee7a-4172-ba4e-6eeca82ddfef","name":"Andersen, Ingelise","orcid":"0000-0002-0076-265X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Susanne Oksbjerg","key":"daltonpau","last":"Dalton","locid":"84d10468-fe5d-4cc7-952f-1d89d961390f","name":"Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37162449"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2023.2207745","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"7","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"820-824","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159091226"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e4ef59cb-71d7-47b8-b4bf-9720534fd7d6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association between anxiety and depression symptoms and completion of first-line treatment in newly diagnosed lung cancer patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-690542","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We describe 10 cases of severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) variant BA.2.86 detected in Denmark, including molecular characteristics and results from wastewater surveillance that indicate that the variant is circulating in the country at a low level. This new variant with many spike gene mutations was classified as a variant under monitoring by the World Health Organization on 17 August 2023. Further global monitoring of COVID-19, BA.2.86 and other SARS-CoV-2 variants is highly warranted.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Morten","Møller, Frederik Trier","Gunalan, Vithiagaran","Baig, Sharmin","Bennedbæk, Marc","Christiansen, Lasse Engbo","Cohen, Arieh Sierra","Ellegaard, Kirsten","Fomsgaard, Anders","Franck, Kristina Træholt","Larsen, Nicolai Balle","Larsen, Tine Graakjær","Lassaunière, Ria","Polacek, Charlotta","Qvesel, Amanda Gammelby","Sieber, Raphael Niklaus","Rasmussen, Lasse Dam","Stegger, Marc","Spiess, Katja","Tang, Man Hung Eric","Vestergaard, Lasse Skafte","Andersen, Thomas Emil","Høgh, Silje Vermedal","Pedersen, Rune Micha","Skov, Marianne Nielsine","Steinke, Kat","Sydenham, Thomas Vognbjerg","Hoppe, Morten","Nielsen, Lene","Krause, Tyra Grove","Ullum, Henrik","Jokelainen, Pikka"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-691160"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Morten"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Murdoch University"],"keyword":["Covid 19","SARS CoV 2","Sequencing","Virus","WGS","Wastewater surveillance"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"first cases of sars cov 000000000002 