{"abstract":"Purpose: Producers of specialty products that apply nonindustrial production techniques to deliver high quality and authenticity to niche markets define themselves in opposition to industrial production. This forces them to strike a delicate balance between, on the one hand, emphasizing the symbolic value related to quality, creativity and distance from traditional industrial production, and on the other hand, ensuring profitability through commercial orientation. This paper aims to explore how new and established firms benefit from a different balance between a strategic orientation toward creativity and the symbolic value of specialty products and commercialization. Design/methodology/approach: Based on survey data from 99 specialty coffee roasters, this study uses statistical regression models to analyze how new versus established firms benefit from a strategic orientation toward creativity versus commercialization. Findings: The authors find that firms benefit from shifting the balance from a strategic orientation on creativity in new firms to a strategic orientation on commercialization in more established firms. This shift increases the likelihood that firms’ passion and creativity lead to commercial success. Originality/value: The findings demonstrate the importance of strategic orientation and emphasize that business owners need to revisit and adjust their strategic orientation as their businesses develop.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","Münchow, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-694885"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst"],"keyword":["Creative industries","Role theory","Strategic orientation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Coffeemind"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"creativity and commerce a shifting balance for specialty foods and beverages","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/333880817/Creativity_and_commerce_Green_Open_Acccess_Version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-694885","identifier":[{"id":"85168082574","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4b5fc738-5708-4c8e-b6b2-88b0a5b6fcad"],"keyword":["Artisan production","Craft-based production","Creative industries","Role theory","Speciality food and beverages","Strategic orientation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EEFC43B8E2EEBC1D6855C6354DB3B882"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/333880817/Creativity_and_commerce_Green_Open_Acccess_Version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics, Business Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Coffeemind"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a1d488b0-5bf1-4eee-bdd5-cfe37a89528a","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"münchowpau","last":"Münchow","name":"Münchow, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1108/jbs-02-2023-0022","issn":["02756668"],"issn_org":["20521197"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Business Strategy","pages":"247-256","publisher":"Emerald Group Publishing Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Business Strategy","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168082574"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4b5fc738-5708-4c8e-b6b2-88b0a5b6fcad"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Creativity and commerce: a shifting balance for specialty foods and beverages","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-694885","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"For organizations to stay competitive, organizational culture must constantly adapt to fit changes in the environment and organizational knowledge. Extant literature has analyzed how sudden events such as environmental jolts, threats or strategic cultural molding may change organizational culture, but the literature has neglected gradual, longitudinal changes to organizational culture. This paper presents an analysis of organizational culture change as a longitudinal organizational learning process. We use unique longitudinal interview data with 38 firms collected in 2006 and 2018 to analyze how the initial organizational culture and organizational learning change organization culture. Our findings show that organizations with different organizational cultures at the start of the studied period went through different organizational culture changes, while organizations with similar organizational cultures displayed similar organizational culture changes. This indicates that an organization’s initial culture functions as a pattern for both learning and changes in organizational culture. Even when exposed to similar environmental development, organizations are so to speak caught in culture. Our findings contribute to the literature on both organizational learning and organizational culture with a much-needed integration of these to related perspectives on organizational knowledge.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wolf, Patricia","Kocher, Pierre-Yves","Vaarst Andersen, Kristina","Steppe, Jessica Annalena"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-697345"],"event":{"end":"2023-08-08","place":"Boston, us","start":"2023-08-04","title":"Academy of Management Annual Meeting","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lucerne University of Applied Sciences and Arts","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"caught in culture patterns of organizational culture change","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://journals.aom.org/doi/abs/10.5465/AMPROC.2023.17406abstract","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-697345","ids":["sdu-c9d769a1-a572-4cc9-8ca2-66fdcd016ca9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C6319F2444DBA3898225821B33D6D624"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, SDU Climate Cluster","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ch","key":"lucerne university of applied sciences and arts","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Lucerne University of Applied Sciences and Arts","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Patricia","key":"wolfpau","last":"Wolf","locid":"abead8db-8d6e-4ef2-9373-fa3d867ea8e3","name":"Wolf, Patricia","orcid":"0000-0002-1242-6514","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pierre-Yves","key":"kocherpau","last":"Kocher","name":"Kocher, Pierre-Yves","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"vaarstandersenpau","last":"Vaarst Andersen","name":"Vaarst Andersen, Kristina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jessica Annalena","key":"steppepau","last":"Steppe","name":"Steppe, Jessica Annalena","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00650668"],"issue":"1","pages":"17406","publisher":"Academy of Management","series":"Academy of Management Proceedings","status":"p","title":"Academy of management proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c9d769a1-a572-4cc9-8ca2-66fdcd016ca9"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Caught in culture? : patterns of organizational culture change","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-697345","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Breast augmentation is one of the most performed cosmetic surgeries. Despite this, patient satisfaction following breast augmentation is poorly understood. Objectives: The aim of this study was to investigate what patient and surgical factors influence patient satisfaction following primary breast augmentation. Methods: The BREAST-Q Augmentation module was sent to all females undergoing primary breast augmentation at a single private clinic (Amalieklinikken, Copenhagen, Denmark) between 2012 and 2019. Patient and surgical characteristics at the time of surgery were obtained from the patients' medical records, and data on factors that occurred after the surgery (eg, breastfeeding) were obtained by patient contact. Multivariate linear regression modeled the impact of these factors on BREAST-Q outcomes. Results: A total of 554 females with a mean follow-up time of 5 years after primary breast augmentation were included in this study. Implant type and volume did not affect patient satisfaction. However, higher patient age was associated with significantly higher postoperative patient satisfaction, psychosocial well-being, and sexual well-being (P <. 05). Conversely, higher patient BMI, postoperative weight gain, and breastfeeding were associated with significantly lower satisfaction (P <. 05). Additionally, subglandular implant placement was associated with significantly lower satisfaction than submuscular implant placement (P <. 05). Conclusions: Implant type and volume did not affect patient satisfaction with breast augmentation. However, young age, higher BMI, subglandular implant placement, and postoperative weight gain were associated with lower patient satisfaction. These factors should be considered when aligning outcome expectations with breast augmentation.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf","Hemmingsen, Mathilde N","Larsen, Andreas","Weltz, Tim K","Strålman, Kristina B","Andersen, Peter S","Samardy, Faranak","Toyserkani, Navid M","Herly, Mikkel","Elberg, Jens J"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-702906"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jørgensen, Mads Gustaf"],"keyword":["Breast Implantation adverse effects","Breast implants","Female","Humans","Mammaplasty adverse effects","Patient Satisfaction","Retrospective Studies","Treatment Outcome","Weight Gain"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Plastic surgeons in private practice in Copenhagen"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"factors influencing patient satisfaction with breast augmentation a breast q effect of magnitude analysis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/asj/sjad204","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-702906","identifier":[{"id":"85174750788","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37378533","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-2d78bfc5-341e-4e27-a2ae-b241843f83b0"],"keyword":["Breast Implantation/adverse effects","Breast Implants","Female","Humans","Mammaplasty/adverse effects","Patient Satisfaction","Retrospective Studies","Treatment Outcome","Weight Gain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E0EE382BA523ECA8ED98A34109260F01"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/asj/sjad204","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark"