last":"Autzen","name":"Autzen, Anton","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01064223","22449078"],"issn_org":["01064223"],"newspaper":"Berlingske Tidende","status":"p","title":"Berlingske Tidende"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-3d8d86e5-956d-4e1d-b5ea-88076fec8f36"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Universiteterne har brug for en reformpause","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-749921","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Organizations’ ability to adapt their organizational culture in response to new environmental conditions is critical for their competitive advantage (Rindova et al., 2011). Such adaption implies organizational learning: Organizations’ cultural knowledge must develop to reflect the changed reality (Tsoukas & Chia, 2002) and accommodate new knowledge (Pachidi et al., 2021). Organizational learning, i.e., \"change in the organization's knowledge that occurs as a function of experience\" (Argote & Miron-Spektor, 2011: 1124), renders part of commonly held cognitions obsolete and requires developing new cultural knowledge (Sackmann, 1992). When organizational culture changes, the assumptions and values that motivate members’ cognition and behavior are reassessed (Coombs et al., 1992; Kuwada, 1998; Woiceshyn, 2000; Canato et al., 2013) and the cultural knowledge enriched (Howard-Grenville et al., 2011; Rindova et al., 2011; Weber & Dacin, 2011). This leads to organizational innovation by both adding new knowledge items as well as suppressing aspects of cultural knowledge. Several studies analyze changes in organizational culture in response to environmental jolts (Cloutier & Ravasi, 2000; Canato et al., 2013) or sudden threats (Ravasi & Schultz, 2006). However, organizational culture change often results from gradual changes in the environment over years or decades (Howard-Grenville et al., 2011). The preference for investigating sudden changes is natural given that gradual changes are hard to observe, what makes it difficult to collect data monitoring organizational culture over many years without certainty of detecting any changes. Yet, it leaves research on organizational culture with only partial insight into the phenomenon of organizational culture change. This paper contributes to the literature with insight into organizational culture change as a longitudinal organizational learning process and brought about by a combination of both sudden jolts and gradual changes in the environment.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Wolf, Patricia","Kocher, Pierre-Yves","Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","Steppe, Jessica"],"cuid":["S02-081.74-725028"],"event":{"end":"2023-09-19","place":"Linz, at","start":"2023-09-17","title":"24th International CINet Conference","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wolf, Patricia"],"country":["Norway","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lucerne University of Applied Sciences and Arts","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Innovation culture","Organizational learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patterns in organizational culture change imprints of the interaction between organizational culture and organizational learning","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-081.74-725028","ids":["dtu-488ab7fc-9e8e-467e-9c38-1f2b61f6b4a1","sdu-65082065-0cc0-4e47-ae2e-409bd2bd55a3"],"keyword":["Innovation culture","Organization culture change","Organizational learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-6D3B8CA84D4C8B7B824D4D7FAB0B21FB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, SDU Climate Cluster","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM), Centre for Integrative Innovation Management (C*I2M)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Engineering Technology and Didactics, Business Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"lucerne university of applied sciences and arts","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Lucerne University of Applied Sciences and Arts","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Patricia","key":"wolfpau","last":"Wolf","locid":"abead8db-8d6e-4ef2-9373-fa3d867ea8e3","name":"Wolf, Patricia","orcid":"0000-0002-1242-6514","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a1d488b0-5bf1-4eee-bdd5-cfe37a89528a","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pierre-Yves","key":"kocherpau","last":"Kocher","name":"Kocher, Pierre-Yves","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jessica Annalena","key":"steppepau","last":"Steppe","name":"Steppe, Jessica Annalena","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"541-552","place":"Linz","publisher":"Continuous Innovation Network","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 24th CINet Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-488ab7fc-9e8e-467e-9c38-1f2b61f6b4a1","sdu-65082065-0cc0-4e47-ae2e-409bd2bd55a3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Patterns in Organizational Culture Change: Imprints of the Interaction Between Organizational Culture and Organizational Learning?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.74-725028","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Persons with schizophrenia may experience decreased ability to perform activities of daily living (ADL) indicated by need for assistance in everyday life. Others are independent, but their quality of ADL task performance in terms of effort and efficiency may still be impacted. Aims/Objectives: The overall purpose of this study was to explore the quality of ADL task performance in subgroups with schizophrenia (independent/needing assistance). Materials and methods: Participants were in- and outpatients at a Psychiatric Hospital diagnosed with schizophrenia (n = 83). Their quality of ADL task performance was evaluated using the Assessment of Motor and Process Skills (AMPS). Evaluations were conducted at the hospital. Two subgroups (A: independent and B: needing assistance) were created based on AMPS ADL ability measures. Results: The majority in both subgroups had AMPS ADL ability measures within the risk zones. Further, the majority in subgroup A had ADL ability measures within age expectations but below mean for well persons of the same age. Both ineffective motor and process skills were identified in both subgroups Conclusions/Significance: Occupational therapy is indicated for persons with schizophrenia, both for independent persons and for persons needing assistance. This is to prevent decline in or to enhance ADL ability.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nielsen, Kristina Tomra","Andersen, Ulla","Wæhrens, Eva Ejlersen","von Bülow, Cecilie"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-716297"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Kristina Tomra"],"keyword":["Activities of Daily Living","Activities of Daily Living psychology","Assessment of Motor and Process Skills AMPS","Humans","Occupational Therapy","Occupational performance","Schizophrenia","Task Performance and Analysis","occupational performance skills"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quality of adl task performance in persons with schizophrenia looking beyond independence","src":["kp","sdu","ucn"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85146778883","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the Danish Association of Occupational Therapists under [Grant PP 1 17-R46-A1247] and OAK foundation under [Grant OCAY-18-774-OFIL]. First and foremost, the authors would like to express gratitude towards the participants, who made this study possible. In addition, the authors wish to thank Aalborg University Hospital–Psychiatry for supporting the study and especially the OTs for recruiting participants and conducting AMPS evaluations."],"id":"S03-100.00-716297","identifier":[{"id":"36635973","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85146778883","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["kp-2b54e24d-c1a9-49c1-b513-704fa67624ec","sdu-1c6f4308-7f57-4e03-aa3b-1dccb168651a","ucn-16adf574-7360-4ec5-9164-674721bc331c"],"keyword":["Activities of Daily Living/psychology","Activities of daily living","Assessment of Motor and Process Skills (AMPS)","Humans","Schizophrenia","Task Performance and Analysis","occupational performance","occupational performance skills","occupational therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-71D62D0809692F5EE42B70A3BCC330DD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Ergoterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Parker Instituttet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for sundhedsuddannelser - Dekan, Ergoterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, User Perspectives and Community-based Interventions"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Tomra","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2b848116-080f-4b20-bb1a-03255c905245","name":"Nielsen, Kristina Tomra","orcid":"0000-0002-4944-9453","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"301746a4-07cb-4628-ad78-43695f8f3e25","name":"Andersen, Ulla","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva Ejlersen","key":"wæhrenspau","last":"Wæhrens","locid":"fe83aa9f-d47c-461a-8386-72a380717f19","name":"Wæhrens, Eva Elisabet Ejlersen","name_org":"Wæhrens, Eva Ejlersen","orcid":"0000-0002-0846-1659","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie","key":"vonbülowpau","last":"von Bülow","name":"von Bülow, Cecilie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36635973"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/11038128.2023.2165541","issn":["11038128","16512014"],"issn_org":["11038128"],"issue":"6","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Occupational Therapy","pages":"873-882","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Occupational Therapy","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85146778883"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","KP","Universities","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-2b54e24d-c1a9-49c1-b513-704fa67624ec","sdu-1c6f4308-7f57-4e03-aa3b-1dccb168651a","ucn-16adf574-7360-4ec5-9164-674721bc331c"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Quality of ADL task performance in persons with schizophrenia : Looking beyond independence","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-716297","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Dette projekt er udført af en gruppe forskere fra Sektion for Landskabsarkitektur og Planlægning, Københavns Universitet, som et pilotprojekt, på foranledning af Gudenåkomitéen. Gudenåkomitéen er et samarbejde mellem de syv kommuner, der deler Gudenåens hovedløb: Hedensted, Horsens, Skanderborg, Silkeborg, Viborg, Favrskov og Randers Kommuner. Komitéen består af ét kommunalt bestyrelsesmedlem fra hver medlemskommune. Formålet med pilotprojektet er at skabe en platform for en kommende implementering af den Helhedsplan for Gudenåen som Gudenåkomitéen enedes om i 2021. De enkelte dele af pilotprojektet omfatter en række analyser af landbrug og landskab langs Gudenåens hovedløb, en identifikation af mulige strategiske projekter, en gennemgang af de gennemførte aktørworkshops og anvendelse af film som planlægnings- og dialogredskab. Resultaterne præsenteres dels i denne rapport, dels i form af en pilotfilm, der anviser mediets muligheder som analyse-, dialog- og kommunikationsredskab i forbindelse med inddragende planlægning. Pilotfilmen kan tilgås direkte via link i kapitel V.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Andersen, Erling","Andersen, Peter Stubkjær","Folvig, Sara","Jensen, Miriam","Jessen, Mette Juhl","Larsen, Kristina Cecilie","Løffler, Leah","Munck Petersen, Rikke","Vejre, Henrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-471736"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"landskabsanalyse for gudenådalen pilotprojekt i forbindelse med helhedsplan for gudenåen","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341016913/Landskabsanalyse_lr.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-471736","ids":["ku-82dc9851-b1de-4cf9-beb8-1588cdb0eb69"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1E8D9A8A29C2C273908320C323819A32"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/341016913/Landskabsanalyse_lr.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Landscape Architecture and Planning","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Spatial Change and Planning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Erling","key":"andersenerlingpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"ee71739a-2c1d-4ebf-93f0-db3419d00da5","name":"Andersen, Erling","orcid":"0000-0002-2178-2772","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Stubkjær","key":"andersenpeterstubkjærpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"bf71bafa-9fb3-41ca-be4c-d426de50e348","name":"Andersen, Peter Stubkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-3795-8939","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sara","key":"folvigsarapau","last":"Folvig","locid":"9e24f183-6cc5-4bda-8807-3db3f9afe4f0","name":"Folvig, Sara","orcid":"0000-0003-3382-7699","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Miriam","key":"jensenmiriampau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Miriam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette Juhl","key":"jessenmettejuhlpau","last":"Jessen","locid":"ff71260c-30d5-4e85-a7cf-1c538618f7b3","name":"Jessen, Mette Juhl","orcid":"0009-0007-0316-3189","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina Cecilie","key":"larsenkristinaceciliepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"efd93d1f-f798-46cb-9717-8f1f619c6651","name":"Larsen, Kristina Cecilie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Leah","key":"løfflerleahpau","last":"Løffler","locid":"0453c5e0-9faf-4dc5-8b0b-4d8fa03a3f20","name":"Løffler, Leah","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke","key":"munckpetersenrikkepau","last":"Munck Petersen","locid":"01b63bb6-47bd-48d3-ac0b-3c55663e3473","name":"Munck Petersen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0001-7788-6290","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"vejrehenrikpau","last":"Vejre","locid":"e4073dcd-d8a8-4d8a-b2c6-149ce705394b","name":"Vejre, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-6820-0389","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"marts 2023","pages":"155","publisher":"Institut for Geovidenskab og Naturforvaltning, Københavns Universitet","repno":"IGN Rapport, marts 2023","series":"IGN Rapport","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-82dc9851-b1de-4cf9-beb8-1588cdb0eb69"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Landskabsanalyse for Gudenådalen : Pilotprojekt i forbindelse med Helhedsplan for Gudenåen","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-471736","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Denne pilotfilm anviser filmmediets muligheder som analyse-, dialog- og kommunikationsredskab i forbindelse med samarbejdsdreven planlægning. Pilotfilmen er udført som en del af pilotprojektet ’Landskabsanalyse for Gudenådalen: Pilotprojekt i forbindelse med Helhedsplan for Gudenåen’. Pilotfilm og pilotprojekt er udført af en gruppe forskere fra Sektion for Landskabsarkitektur og Planlægning, Københavns Universitet, på foranledning af Gudenåkomitéen. Gudenåkomitéen er et samarbejde mellem de syv kommuner, der deler Gudenåens hovedløb: Hedensted, Horsens, Skanderborg, Silkeborg, Viborg, Favrskov og Randers Kommuner. Komitéen består af ét kommunalt bestyrelsesmedlem fra hver medlemskommune. Formålet med pilotprojektet er at skabe en platform for en kommende implementering af den Helhedsplan for Gudenåen som Gudenåkomitéen enedes om i 2021. De enkelte dele af pilotprojektet omfatter anvendelse af film som planlægnings- og dialogredskab og en række analyser af landbrug og landskab langs Gudenåens hovedløb, en identifikation af mulige strategiske projekter, en gennemgang af de gennemførte aktørworkshops. Resultaterne præsenteres dels i denne pilotfilm, dels i form af rapporten 'Landskabsanalyse for Gudenådalen: Pilotprojekt i forbindelse med Helhedsplan for Gudenåen', der samler rækken af analyser og udpegning af mulige strategiske projekter.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Munck Petersen, Rikke","Løffler, Leah","Andersen, Erling","Larsen, Kristina Cecilie","Pørksen, Kent"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-511718"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gudena dalen pilotfilm film som analyse dialog og kommunikationsredskab i pilotprojekt gudenådalen","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://video.ku.dk/video/82237059/gudenadalen-pilotfilm","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-511718","ids":["ku-c621e90d-1762-44fb-8431-eeace22eb715"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3C0B56CBEA23BB5B0DBEB129D71A24E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://video.ku.dk/video/82237059/gudenadalen-pilotfilm","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Landscape Architecture and Planning","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Landscape Architecture and Urbanism","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Spatial Change and Planning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke","key":"munckpetersenoth","last":"Munck Petersen","locid":"01b63bb6-47bd-48d3-ac0b-3c55663e3473","name":"Munck Petersen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0001-7788-6290","rank":1,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","first":"Leah","key":"løfflerpau","last":"Løffler","locid":"0453c5e0-9faf-4dc5-8b0b-4d8fa03a3f20","name":"Løffler, Leah","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Erling","key":"andersenoth","last":"Andersen","locid":"ee71739a-2c1d-4ebf-93f0-db3419d00da5","name":"Andersen, Erling","orcid":"0000-0002-2178-2772","rank":3,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina Cecilie","key":"larsenoth","last":"Larsen","locid":"efd93d1f-f798-46cb-9717-8f1f619c6651","name":"Larsen, Kristina Cecilie","rank":4,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"","first":"Kent","key":"pørksenoth","last":"Pørksen","name":"Pørksen, Kent","rank":5,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Københavns Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c621e90d-1762-44fb-8431-eeace22eb715"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gudenådalen Pilotfilm : Film som analyse-, dialog- og kommunikationsredskab i pilotprojekt Gudenådalen","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-511718","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Testosterone replacement therapy is known to improve sexual function in men younger than 40 years with pathological hypogonadism. However, the extent to which testosterone alleviates sexual dysfunction in older men and men with obesity is unclear, despite the fact that testosterone is being increasingly prescribed to these patient populations. We aimed to evaluate whether subgroups of men with low testosterone derive any symptomatic benefit from testosterone treatment. Methods: We did a systematic review and meta-analysis to evaluate characteristics associated with symptomatic benefit of testosterone treatment versus placebo in men aged 18 years and older with a baseline serum total testosterone concentration of less than 12 nmol/L. We searched major electronic databases (MEDLINE, Embase, Science Citation Index, and the Cochrane Central Register of Controlled Trials) and clinical trial registries for reports published in English between Jan 1, 1992, and Aug 27, 2018. Anonymised individual participant data were requested from the investigators of all identified trials. Primary (cardiovascular) outcomes from this analysis have been published previously. In this report, we present the secondary outcomes of sexual function, quality of life, and psychological outcomes at 12 months. We did a one-stage individual participant data meta-analysis with a random-effects linear regression model, and a two-stage meta-analysis integrating individual participant data with aggregated data from studies that did not provide individual participant data. This study is registered with PROSPERO, CRD42018111005. Findings: 9871 citations were identified through database searches. After exclusion of duplicates and publications not meeting inclusion criteria, 225 full texts were assessed for inclusion, of which 109 publications reporting 35 primary studies (with a total 5601 participants) were included. Of these, 17 trials provided individual participant data (3431 participants; median age 67 years [IQR 60–72]; 3281 [97%] of 3380 aged ≥40 years) Compared with placebo, testosterone treatment increased 15-item International Index of Erectile Function (IIEF-15) total score (mean difference 5·52 [95% CI 3·95–7·10]; τ2=1·17; n=1412) and IIEF-15 erectile function subscore (2·14 [1·40–2·89]; τ2=0·64; n=1436), reaching the minimal clinically important difference for mild erectile dysfunction. These effects were not found to be dependent on participant age, obesity, presence of diabetes, or baseline serum total testosterone. However, absolute IIEF-15 scores reached during testosterone treatment were subject to thresholds in patient age and baseline serum total testosterone. Testosterone significantly improved Aging Males’ Symptoms score, and some 12-item or 36-item Short Form Survey quality of life subscores compared with placebo, but it did not significantly improve psychological symptoms (measured by Beck Depression Inventory). Interpretation: In men aged 40 years or older with baseline serum testosterone of less than 12 nmol/L, short-to-medium-term testosterone treatment could provide clinically meaningful treatment for mild erectile dysfunction, irrespective of patient age, obesity, or degree of low testosterone. However, due to more severe baseline symptoms, the absolute level of sexual function reached during testosterone treatment might be lower in older men and men with obesity. Funding: National Institute for Health and Care Research Health Technology Assessment Programme.","author_count":39,"contributors":["Hudson, Jemma","Cruickshank, Moira","Quinton, Richard","Aucott, Lorna","Wu, Frederick","Grossmann, Mathis","Bhasin, Shalender","Snyder, Peter J.","Ellenberg, Susan S.","Travison, Thomas G.","Brock, Gerald B.","Gianatti, Emily J.","van der Schouw, Yvonne T.","Emmelot-Vonk, Marielle H.","Giltay, Erik J.","Hackett, Geoff","Ramachandran, Sudarshan","Svartberg, Johan","Hildreth, Kerry L.","Antonic, Kristina Groti","Tenover, Joyce Lisa","Tan, Hui Meng","Ho Chee Kong, Christopher","Tan, Wei Shen","Marks, Leonard S.","Ross, Richard J.","Schwartz, Robert S.","Manson, Paul","Roberts, Stephen A.","Andersen, Marianne","Magnussen, Line Velling","Aceves-Martins, Magaly","Gillies, Katie","Hernández, Rodolfo","Oliver, Nick","Dhillo, Waljit S.","Bhattacharya, Siladitya","Brazzelli, Miriam","Jayasena, Channa N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-697119"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Jayasena, Channa N."],"country":["Australia","Canada","Malaysia","Netherlands","Norway","Slovenia","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Aston University","Harvard Medical School","Health Services Research Unit","Imperial College London","Leiden University","Newcastle University","Palo Alto Veterans Affairs Health Care System","PathWest Laboratory Medicine WA","Stanford University","Taylor's University","The University of Sheffield","UiT The Arctic University of Norway","University Hospital of North Norway","University Hospitals Birmingham NHS Foundation Trust","University Medical Center Utrecht","University Medical Centre Ljubljana","University of Aberdeen","University of Colorado","University of Ljubljana","University of Manchester","University of Melbourne","University of Pennsylvania","University of Southern California","University of Texas MD Anderson Cancer Center","University of Western Ontario"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"symptomatic benefits of testosterone treatment in patient subgroups a systematic review individual participant data meta analysis and aggregate data meta analysis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S2666-7568(23)00169-1","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by the UK National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR)'s Health Technology Assessment Programme (project number 17/68/01). The views expressed herein are those of the authors and not necessarily those of the National Health Service, the NIHR Health Technology Assessment Programme, or the UK Department of Health and Social Care. The Health Services Research Unit at the University of Aberdeen is funded by the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government Health and Social Care Directorates. The Section of Endocrinology and Investigative Medicine at Imperial College London is funded by grants from the Medical Research Council, the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council, NIHR, an Integrative Mammalian Biology Capacity Building Award, and an FP7-HEALTH-2009-241592 EuroCHIP grant, and is supported by the NIHR Biomedical Research Centre Funding Scheme. WSD is funded by an NIHR Research Professorship. CNJ is funded by an NIHR Post-Doctoral Fellowship. ShB receives NIH research grant funding. The authors are grateful to the clinical and methodological experts and patient partners who contributed to the advisory group for this study. This work was supported by the UK National Institute for Health and Care Research (NIHR)'s Health Technology Assessment Programme (project number 17/68/01). The views expressed herein are those of the authors and not necessarily those of the National Health Service, the NIHR Health Technology Assessment Programme, or the UK Department of Health and Social Care. The Health Services Research Unit at the University of Aberdeen is funded by the Chief Scientist Office of the Scottish Government Health and Social Care Directorates. The Section of Endocrinology and Investigative Medicine at Imperial College London is funded by grants from the Medical Research Council, the Biotechnology and Biological Sciences Research Council, NIHR, an Integrative Mammalian Biology Capacity Building Award, and an FP7-HEALTH-2009-241592 EuroCHIP grant, and is supported by the NIHR Biomedical Research Centre Funding Scheme. WSD is funded by an NIHR Research Professorship. CNJ is funded by an NIHR Post-Doctoral Fellowship. ShB receives NIH research grant funding. The authors are grateful to the clinical and methodological experts and patient partners who contributed to the advisory group for this study."],"id":"S01-000.00-697119","identifier":[{"id":"85172893601","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37804846","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-6306e8aa-4296-485d-81d7-f7f1e211e187"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E9C60A651420F4D7D8FADADCB8BA1F68"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/242554462/PIIS2666756823001691.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S2666-7568(23)00169-1","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of aberdeen","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Aberdeen","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"newcastle university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Newcastle University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"health services research unit","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Health Services Research Unit","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of manchester","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Manchester","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"au","key":"university of melbourne","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Melbourne","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"harvard medi