{"abstract":"Follicular lymphoma (FL) is a lymphoid neoplasia characterized by an indolent clinical nature. Despite generally favorable prognoses, early progression and histological transformation (HT) to a more aggressive lymphoma histology remain the leading causes of death among FL patients. To provide a basis for possible novel treatment options, we set out to evaluate the expression levels of indoleamine 2,3-dioxygenase 1 (IDO1), an immunoinhibitory checkpoint molecule, in follicular and transformed follicular biopsies. The expression levels of IDO1 were assessed using immunohistochemical staining and digital image analysis in lymphoma biopsies from 33 FL patients without subsequent HT (non-transforming FL, nt-FL) and 20 patients with subsequent HT (subsequently transforming FL, st-FL) as well as in paired high-grade biopsies from the time of HT (transformed FL, tFL). Despite no statistical difference in IDO1 expression levels seen between the groups, all diagnostic and transformed lymphomas exhibited positive expression, indicating its possible role in novel treatment regimens. In addition, IDO1 expression revealed a positive correlation with another immune checkpoint inhibitor, namely programmed death 1 (PD-1). In summary, we report IDO1 expression in all cases of FL and tFL, which provides the grounds for future investigations of anti-IDO1 therapy as a possible treatment for FL patients.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Enemark, Marie Beck","Sørensen, Emma Frasez","Hybel, Trine Engelbrecht","Andersen, Maja Dam","Madsen, Charlotte","Lauridsen, Kristina Lystlund","Honoré, Bent","D'Amore, Francesco Annibale","Plesner, Trine Lindhardt","Hamilton-Dutoit, Stephen Jacques","Ludvigsen, Maja"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-692077"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Biopsy","Dioxygenases","Follicular lymphoma","Histological transformation","Humans","Indoleamine 2 3 dioxygenase","Lymphoma Follicular diagnosis","Neoplasm Recurrence Local"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ido000000000001 protein is expressed in diagnostic biopsies from both follicular and transformed follicular patients","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24087314","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-692077","identifier":[{"id":"37108483","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10139172","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85156209031","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c82ed845-8321-48ac-b2fd-db96d6e19a43","ku-0ebae375-cf70-4b0c-ae29-ab5f9ae38e19"],"keyword":["Biopsy","Dioxygenases","Humans","Lymphoma, Follicular/diagnosis","Neoplasm Recurrence, Local","follicular lymphoma","histological transformation","indoleamine 2,3-dioxygenase"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-60B383DE6519C47E46CAB77D31ACCAB9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms24087314","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/422065784/ijms-24-07314-v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/369361165/IDO1_Protein.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Haematology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie Beck Hairing","key":"enemarkpau","last":"Enemark","locid":"d7854a01-8da3-4657-8f9c-eebb7d2d8df3","name":"Enemark, Marie Beck","name_org":"Enemark, Marie Beck Hairing","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Emma Frasez","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1bb2cde9-ca25-4552-912f-cb126bef4766","name":"Sørensen, Emma Frasez","orcid":"0009-0003-4588-5607","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine Engelbrecht","key":"hybelpau","last":"Hybel","locid":"26f7e9a4-df6b-41cd-9a4d-ad08062fb253","name":"Hybel, Trine Engelbrecht","orcid":"0000-0003-0166-8558","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja Dam","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"23ba761f-55f2-41a8-80be-5b028946efbd","name":"Andersen, Maja Dam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"9dff