ocal.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.94-015890","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Dette kapitel handler om fænomenet feber i en sygeplejefaglig kontekst. Når sygeplejersken møder borgere og patienter med feber, er feber oftest et symptom på sygdom. Derfor skal sygeplejersken observere, analysere og reflektere i situationen, således at observationerne kobles til viden om feber og underliggende årsager hertil – og på denne baggrund igangsætte hensigtsmæssige interventioner.Formålet med dette kapitel er at understøtte, at den studerende tilegner sig forståelse for feber og patienten med feber, for at opnå handlekompetencer til klinisk beslutningstagen og klinisk lederskab. Kapitlet giver et indblik i, hvordan det subjektivt kan opleves at have feber samtidigt med at der er fokus på dataindsamling ved brug af sygeplejerskens sanser til observationer samt udførelse af objektive målinger af temperaturen og kritisk refleksion over de indsamlede data.Feberfaserne bliver gennemgået for at give indblik i, hvordan sygeplejersken kan arbejde målrettet på at forebygge forværring i febertilstanden og at understøtte fysiologiske behov samt støtte patienten i forløbet. Den tilegnede viden om feber har også til hensigt at understøtte forebyggelse af komplikationer, som kan opstå som følge af febertilstanden. Sådanne komplikationer kan fx være dehydrering som følge af den forhøjede temperatur, insufficient ernæring som følge af manglende appetit eller decubitus som følge af immobilisation.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Knudsen, Kristina Kvisgaard","Andersen, Anna Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-681072"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Feber","Klinisk beslutningstagen","Klinisk lederskab","Sygepleje","Temperaturregulering","grundlæggende sygepleje"],"level":"edu","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feber","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-681072","ids":["via-4d44c931-20ab-4e59-b45f-36561602da85"],"keyword":["Klinisk beslutningstagen","Temperaturregulering","feber","feberfaser","grundlæggende sygepleje","klinisk lederskab","sygepleje"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6C2F1A84058ADE94FCB3DACBEA4C22CE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Uddannelser, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen Horsens"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Viborg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Kvisgaard","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"6e6401c5-3a09-4c3c-8094-c2beebd9c088","name":"Knudsen, Kristina Kvisgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Marie","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Anna Marie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Susanne","key":"jastruppedh","last":"Jastrup","name":"Jastrup, Susanne","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorte","key":"helvingrasmussenpedh","last":"Helving Rasmussen","name":"Helving Rasmussen, Dorte","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"3. udgave","isbn":["9788702339710"],"pages":"244-263","place":"København","publisher":"Munksgaard","series":"Grundbog i sygepleje","status":"p","title":"Klinik: grundbog i sygepleje"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All University Colleges","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-4d44c931-20ab-4e59-b45f-36561602da85"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Feber","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-681072","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The socioeconomic differences in survival are pronounced for patients diagnosed with head and neck cancer; disease stage at diagnosis is suggested to be a main driver of this association. This nationwide, population-based study investigates socioeconomic differences in the pre-diagnostic interval and disease stage at diagnosis. MATERIAL AND METHODS: Information on patient-reported symptoms, symptom onset and disease-specific factors was obtained from the nationwide population-based Danish Head and Neck Cancer Group (DAHANCA) database for patients diagnosed with head and neck squamous cell carcinoma between 2008 and 2019 in Denmark. Socioeconomic position (SEP) was measured by individual-level education, income and cohabitation status obtained from administrative registers. Socioeconomic differences in the interval from symptom onset to diagnosis were investigated in general linear models with 95% confidence intervals (CIs); overall and by subsite, symptom and comorbidity score. Consultation patterns prior to diagnosis were examined using methods for change-point detection. Associations with advanced-stage disease were estimated in logistic regression models. RESULTS: Patients with low, medium and high SEP had a similar interval from patient-reported symptom onset to diagnosis of 10 weeks. Although this interval varied according to primary symptom and anatomical subsite, no apparent socioeconomic differences were observed within these subgroups. Aligned with the patient-reported symptom onset, a distinct increase in consultation rates was observed at 9 weeks (95% CI [7.3; 10.7]) for patients with low SEP and 7 weeks (95% CI [4.8; 9.2]) for patients with high SEP, with overlapping CIs. Patients with low compared to high SEP had increased odds for advanced-stage glottic and oral cavity squamous cell carcinoma. For the remaining subsites the association varied according to SEP-indicator and TNM-edition. CONCLUSION: The interval from symptom onset to diagnosis and consultation patterns were similar across SEP groups. Still, socioeconomic differences in stage at diagnosis were observed for some - but not all - subsites.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Halgren Olsen, Maja","Maltesen, Thomas","Lassen, Pernille","Kjaer, Trille Kristina","Johansen, Jørgen","Primdahl, Hanne","Andersen, Elo","Kristensen, Claus Andrup","Andersen, Maria","Farhadi, Mohammed","Overgaard, Jens","Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-692842"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Halgren Olsen, Maja"],"keyword":["Diagnostic interval","Head and neck cancer","Inequality","Socioeconomic position","Symptoms","disease stage"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socioeconomic position and the pre diagnostic interval among patients diagnosed with head and neck squamous cell carcinoma a population based study from dahanca","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85169934797&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was funded by the Danish Cancer Society"],"id":"S01-000.00-692842","identifier":[{"id":"37672036","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85169934797","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-96184374-3ce9-4764-8981-7ac362982577"],"keyword":["Diagnostic interval","disease stage","head and neck cancer","inequality","socioeconomic position","symptoms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-6CEF01E3B