Severinsen, Marianne","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Mia Klinten","key":"grandmiaklintenpau","last":"Grand","locid":"43f57b9c-d90a-4d31-96d9-3a3348bdb369","name":"Grand, Mia Klinten","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Mary","key":"jardenmarypau","last":"Jarden","locid":"f716d3db-6f75-41b0-94a0-884f7dcd1259","name":"Jarden, Mary","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"møllertompau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Tom","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"kjeldsenlarspau","last":"Kjeldsen","name":"Kjeldsen, Lars","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34839055"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.leukres.2021.106756","issn":["01452126","18735835"],"issn_org":["01452126"],"journal":"Leukemia Research","paperid":"106756","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Leukemia Research","volume":"112"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85119927292"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","amgros i/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-07b726a9-eb3e-4b8e-b390-ac3ad5e5e58a","au-7cf2aa30-bd72-4fda-9086-555000a2e42a","ku-faf34ca0-4e5a-4825-b3e3-06a538079063","sdu-140197b3-1f85-45fb-8e17-8c0331c79f57"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A national Danish proof of concept on feasibility and safety of home -based intensive chemotherapy in patients with acute myeloid leukemia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-100.00-000401","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Novel therapies for the treatment of acute myeloid leukemia (AML) are urgently needed as current treatments do not cure the majority of AML patients. Here, we report on a domain-focused, kinome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 screen to identify protein kinase targets for the treatment of AML, which led to the identification of Rio-kinase 2 (RIOK2) as a potential novel target. We show that loss of RIOK2 leads to a decrease in protein synthesis and to ribosomal instability followed by apoptosis in leukemic cells, but not in fibroblasts. Moreover, we demonstrate that the ATPase function of RIOK2 is required for cell survival. By using a small molecule inhibitor, we show that pharmacological inhibition of RIOK2 similarly leads to loss of protein synthesis and apoptosis and affects leukemic cell growth in vivo. Our results provide proof-of-concept for targeting RIOK2 as a potential treatment for AML patients.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Messling, Jan-Erik","Agger, Karl","Andersen, Kasper Langebjerg","Kromer, Kristina","Kuepper, Hanna Maria","Lund, Anders H","Helin, Kristian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-453340"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"targeting riok000000000002 atpase activity leads to decreased protein synthesis and cell death in acute myeloid leukemia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379867251/bloodbld2021012629.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-453340","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8759535","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34359076","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85122667766","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6434e80d-7801-4683-a7cb-a56d2740c75a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A9135B99C8DD30FAAF143DE421CAC84C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/379867251/bloodbld2021012629.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, BRIC, Helin Group","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, The Danish Stem Cell Center"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jan-Erik","key":"messlingpau","last":"Messling","locid":"604c4ca0-95b2-4220-a83d-de9c185ecbf0","name":"Messling, Jan-Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-3843-0041","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karl","key":"aggerpau","last":"Agger","locid":"3384fd8c-8590-43f9-b523-071a60f498e4","name":"Agger, Karl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper L","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"b9354928-b93d-4a95-901c-ac139bed5223","name":"Andersen, Kasper Langebjerg","name_org":"Andersen, Kasper L","orcid":"0000-0002-5127-113X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristina","key":"kromerpau","last":"Kromer","name":"Kromer, Kristina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanna Maria","key":"kuepperpau","last":"Kuepper","name":"Kuepper, Hanna Maria","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders H","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"197f8063-ab66-4565-a8bc-808c4e5380f2","name":"Lund, Anders H","orcid":"0000-0002-7407-3398","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian","key":"helinpau","last":"Helin","locid":"b95e097b-b1b4-44db-b097-0c3990dadf63","name":"Helin, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-1975-6097","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34359076"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1182/blood.2021012629","issn":["00064971","15280020"],"issn_org":["00064971"],"issue":"2","journal":"Blood","pages":"245-255","status":"p","title":"Blood","volume":"139"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122667766"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6434e80d-7801-4683-a7cb-a56d2740c75a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Targeting RIOK2 ATPase activity leads to decreased protein synthesis and cell death in acute myeloid leukemia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453340","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Most patients with isolated rapid eye movement sleep behaviour disorder (iRBD) convert to Parkinson's disease (PD), dementia with Lewy bodies, or multiple system atrophy within 15 years of diagnosis. Furthermore, iRBD patients develop non-motor symptoms similar to those of manifest PD patients and display dysfunction of the sympathetic and parasympathetic nervous system, comparable to that seen in PD. However, progression rates of autonomic dysfunction in iRBD have not been studied with objective measures in detail, which is the aim of this study. Methods: Twenty-two iRBD patients were included at baseline and 14 participated in follow-up after 3 years. Colonic transit time (CTT) was examined using radio opaque markers, colonic volume was defined on abdominal computed tomography (CT) scans, Iodine-123-metaiodobenzylguanidine ([123I]MIBG) scintigraphy was performed to assess cardiac sympathetic innervation, and 3,4-dihydroxy-6-(18F) fluoro-L-phenylalanine ([18F]FDOPA) positron emission tomography (PET) scan determined nigrostriatal dopamine storage capacity. All examinations were performed at baseline and after 3 years. Results: iRBD patients displayed increased CTT (p = 0.001) and colonic volume (p = 0.01) at follow-up compared to baseline. Furthermore, [123I]MIBG uptake and [18F]FDOPA uptake showed progressive reductions at follow-up (p = 0.02 and p = 0.002, respectively). No correlations were seen between changes in intestinal or cardiac measurements and dopaminergic function. Conclusion: Using objective markers, the present study documented that intestinal dysfunction and cardiac sympathetic degeneration worsen in the majority of iRBD patients over a 3-year period. The absent correlation between these markers and nigrostriatal dopaminergic dysfunction suggests that progressive gastrointestinal and cardiac dysfunction in iRBD is caused mainly by non-dopaminergic mechanisms.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Fedorova, Tatyana D.","Knudsen, Karoline","Andersen, Katrine B","Horsager, Jacob","Skjærbæk, Casper","Beier, Christoph P.","Sommerauer, Michael","Svendsen, Kristina Bacher","Otto, Marit","Borghammer, Per"],"cuid":["S02-097.06-021767"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fedorova, Tatyana D."],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Forschungszentrum Jülich","Jülich Research Centre ( FZJ )","University Hospital Cologne","University of Cologne"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"imaging progressive peripheral and central dysfunction in isolated rem sleep behaviour disorder after 000000000003 years of follow up","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.parkreldis.2022.07.005","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.06-021767","identifier":[{"id":"35853349","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85134483869","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7ce3f648-400a-41cf-b07c-1bcf181cd382","sdu-4dfb53e8-78c9-4a1e-90c1-08c879dd3e27"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-09ABEA05B064F715AF9710D1D68F645A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/205417183/1_s2.0_S1353802022002231_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/326133244/Imaging_progressive_peripheral_and_central_dysfunction_in_isolated_REM_sleep_behaviour_disorder_after_3_years_of_follow_up.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.parkreldis.2022.07.005","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Nuclear Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Neurology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"university of cologne","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cologne","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"jülich research centre","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Jülich Research Centre ( FZJ )","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"university hospital cologne","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Hospital Cologne","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"forschungszentrum jülich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Forschungszentrum Jülich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tatyana D.","key":"fedorovapau","last":"Fedorova","name":"Fedorova, Tatyana D.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karoline","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"a4315190-0d6d-49d4-9215-918e5c6d1ce6","name":"Knudsen, Karoline","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Katrine B.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"c88550a9-f836-408f-b04b-5055ed2ffa1d","name":"Andersen, Katrine B","name_org":"Andersen, Katrine B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob","key":"horsagerpau","last":"Horsager","locid":"381add70-79b3-40a0-b999-1df09991360f","name":"Horsager, Jacob","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Casper","key":"skjærbækpau","last":"Skjærbæk","locid":"32271fb9-570a-414b-b6e6-1228cb8f9f1e","name":"Skjærbæk, Casper","orcid":"0000-0003-2823-8785","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph P.","key":"beierpau","last":"Beier","locid":"8ab43a70-1e6e-4f42-af0a-d4cdf5216339","name":"Beier, Christoph Patrick","name_org":"Beier, Christoph P.","orcid":"0000-0001-8268-1492","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5 6 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"sommerauerpau","last":"Sommerauer","name":"Sommerauer, Michael","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina B.","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"0961cd36-eb75-4053-9559-0a28fc827503","name":"Svendsen, Kristina Bacher","name_org":"Svendsen, Kristina B.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marit","key":"ottopau","last":"Otto","locid":"8ba0455d-4d88-4ff3-a91b-d0a9b0cc5921","name":"Otto, Marit","orcid":"0000-0002-1508-9269","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"borghammerpau","last":"Borghammer","locid":"f2bbb76e-a61c-44b8-a0d5-94620cb1c19b","name":"Borghammer, Per","orcid":"0000-0001-6391-8052","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35853349"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.parkreldis.2022.07.005","issn":["13538020","18735126"],"issn_org":["13538020"],"journal":"Parkinsonism & Related Disorders","pages":"99-104","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","status":"p","title":"Parkinsonism & Related Disorders","title_org":"Parkinsonism and Related Disorders","volume":"101"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134483869"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7ce3f648-400a-41cf-b07c-1bcf181cd382","sdu-4dfb53e8-78c9-4a1e-90c1-08c879dd3e27"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Imaging progressive peripheral and central dysfunction in isolated REM sleep behaviour disorder after 3 years of follow-up","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.06-021767","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Equine osteoarthritis (OA) is a heterogeneous, degenerative disease of the musculoskeletal system with multifactorial causation, characterized by a joint metabolic imbalance. Extracellular vesicles are nanoparticles involved in intracellular communication. Mesenchymal stem cell (MSC) therapy is a form of regenerative medicine that utilizes their properties to repair damaged tissues. Despite its wide use in veterinary practice, the exact mechanism of action of MSCs is not fully understood. The aim of this study was to determine the synovial fluid extracellular vesicle protein cargo following integrin α10β1-selected mesenchymal stem cell (integrin α10-MSC) treatment in an experimental model of equine osteoarthritis with longitudinal sampling. Methods: Adipose tissue derived, integrin α10-MSCs were injected intraarticularly in six horses 18 days after experimental induction of OA. Synovial fluid samples were collected at day 0, 18, 21, 28, 35, and 70. Synovial fluid was processed and extracellular vesicles were isolated and characterized. Extracellular vesicle cargo was then analyzed using data independent acquisition mass spectrometry proteomics. Results: A total of 442 proteins were identified across all samples, with 48 proteins differentially expressed (FDR ≤ 0.05) between sham-operated control joint without MSC treatment and OA joint treated with MSCs. The most significant pathways following functional enrichment analysis of the differentially abundant protein dataset were serine endopeptidase activity (p = 0.023), complement activation (classical pathway) (p = 0.023), and collagen containing extracellular matrix (p = 0.034). Due to the lack of an OA group without MSC treatment, findings cannot be directly correlated to only MSCs. Discussion: To date this is the first study to quantify the global extracellular vesicle proteome in synovial fluid following MSC treatment of osteoarthritis. Changes in the proteome of the synovial fluid-derived EVs following MSC injection suggest EVs may play a role in mediating the effect of cell therapy through altered joint homeostasis. This is an important step toward understanding the potential therapeutic mechanisms of MSC therapy, ultimately enabling the improvement of therapeutic efficacy.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Clarke, Emily J.","Johnson, Emily","Caamaño Gutierrez, Eva","Andersen, Camilla","Berg, Lise Charlotte","Jenkins, Rosalind E.","Lindegaard, Casper","Uvebrant, Kristina","Lundgren-Åkerlund, Evy","Turlo, Agnieszka","James, Victoria","Jacobsen, Stine","Peffers, Mandy J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-451505"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Liverpool","University of Nottingham","Xintela AB"],"keyword":["Biologics","Equine","Extracellular vesicles","Osteoarthritis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"temporal extracellular vesicle protein changes following intraarticular treatment with integrin α000000000010β000000000001 selected mesenchymal stem cells in equine osteoarthritis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fvets.2022.1057667","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-451505","identifier":[{"id":"85143404489","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9730043","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36504839","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-610a10cb-4ba3-414c-8780-9532ce4584c7"],"keyword":["MSC therapy","biologics","equine","extracellular vesicles","osteoarthritis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B5B75AE47B0