versity","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Association of Smoking, Comorbidity, Clinical Stage, and Treatment Intent With Socioeconomic Differences in Survival After Oropharyngeal Squamous Cell Carcinoma in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.99-006545","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background Tuberculosis (TB) screening programmes among asylum seekers tend to focus on chest radiography (CXR) for early diagnosis, whereas knowledge on sputum examination is limited. We evaluated active TB screening using CXR and sputum culture among asylum seekers arriving in Denmark. In addition, we assessed the coverage of a voluntary health assessment. Methods Between 1 February 2017 and 31 March 2019, all newly arrived asylum seekers in Denmark >= 18 years from TB high-incidence countries or risk groups, who attended a voluntary general health assessment, were offered active TB screening with CXR and spot sputum examination. Sputum samples were examined by culture and smear microscopy. Results Coverage of the general health assessment was 65.1%. Among 1,154 referred for active TB screening, 923 (80.0%) attended. Of these, 854 were screened by CXR and one case of active TB was identified equivalent to a yield of 0.12%. Sputum samples were collected from 758 and one M. tuberculosis culture-positive TB case (also identified by CXR) was identified, equivalent to a yield of 0.13%. No cases were found by sputum culture screening only. In addition, screening found three cases of malignant disease. Conclusion We suggest that TB screening should focus on asylum seekers from TB high-incidence countries. Furthermore, early health assessments should be of high priority to ensure migrant health.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Kristensen, Kristina Langholz","Norredam, Marie","Jensen, Sidse Graff","Seersholm, Niels","Jorgensen, Marie Louise","Exsteen, Banoo Bakir","Huber, Franziska Grundtvig","Munk-Andersen, Ebbe","Lillebaek, Troels","Ravn, Pernille"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-501261"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Asylum seekers","CARE","Coverage","Entry","Europe","Immigrants","Migrants","Screening","Surveillance","Tuberculosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Danish Red Cross"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tuberculosis screening among newly arrived asylum seekers in denmark","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-501261","identifier":[{"id":"36000199","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000844086000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85136814669","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b48698b5-9943-4f89-8034-4f72e973cfdb"],"keyword":["Asylum seekers","CARE","ENTRY","EUROPE","IMMIGRANTS","LOW-INCIDENCE COUNTRIES","MIGRANTS","SURVEILLANCE","coverage","screening","sputum culture","tuberculosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B9DC52495507FC30870B00C5E21F55A8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital – North Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","No