5","23744243"],"issn_org":["23744235"],"issue":"11","journal":"Infectious Diseases","status":"p","title":"Infectious Diseases","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85136814669"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b48698b5-9943-4f89-8034-4f72e973cfdb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tuberculosis screening among newly arrived asylum seekers in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-501261","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Carefully considered assay design is essential for PCR-based methods used in circulating DNA (cirDNA) studies. Broadly speaking, there are three main contexts in which cirDNA is subjected to PCR amplification and analyses: (1) in order to quantitate overall cirDNA, or a particular cirDNA sequence; (2) in order to detect mutations or methylation; and (3) as part of sequencing library preparation. In addition to general considerations about primer/probe design, it is equally important to understand the nature and composition of cirDNA in order to optimize analyses. Throughout the research literature, many different approaches have been taken to amplify and quantify cirDNA. Differences in analytical methods influence results, such that studies become incomparable and this hampers the progress of promising clinical biomarkers.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Andersen, Rikke Fredslund"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-583812"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Rikke Fredslund"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"optimal design of pcr assays for circulating dna","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85143921790","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-583812","identifier":[{"id":"85143921790","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-24ebb7d6-d60a-4e90-ab74-0fd5c5c0a377"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5536D182018B51FBB882C0FF32652394"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke F.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"e82f9773-7004-444a-8176-b55f6342dd3d","name":"Andersen, Rikke Fredslund","name_org":"Andersen, Rikke F.","orcid":"0000-0002-5894-7745","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristina","key":"wartonpedh","last":"Warton","name":"Warton, Kristina","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Goli","key":"samimipedh","last":"Samimi","name":"Samimi, Goli","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1142/9789811244681_0005","eisbn":["9789811244698"],"isbn":["9789811244674"],"pages":"113-137","publisher":"World Scientific","status":"p","subtitle":"Purification and Analysis Techniques","title":"Cell-Free Circulating DNA"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-24ebb7d6-d60a-4e90-ab74-0fd5c5c0a377"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Optimal Design of PCR Assays for Circulating DNA","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-583812","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Tumour-associated macrophages (TAMs) support cancer cell survival and suppress anti-tumour immunity. Tumour infiltration by CD163pos TAMs is associated with poor outcome in several human malignancies, including multiple myeloma (MM). Signal transducer and activator of transcription 3 (STAT3) is over-activated in human cancers, and specifically within TAMs activation of STAT3 may induce an immunosuppressive (M2-like) phenotype. Therefore, STAT3-inhibition in TAMs may be a future therapeutic strategy.We investigated TAM markers CD163, CD206, and activated STAT3 (pSTAT3) in patients with MGUS (n = 32) and MM (n = 45), as well as healthy controls (HCs, n = 13).Blood levels of the macrophage biomarkers sCD163 and sCD206, and circulating cytokines, as well as bone marrow mRNA expression of CD163 and CD206, were generally increased in MGUS and MM patients, compared to HCs, but to highly similar levels. By immunohistochemistry, bone marrow levels of pSTAT3 were increased specifically within CD163pos cells in both MGUS and MM patients.In conclusion, macrophage-related inflammatory changes, including activation of STAT3, were present already at the MGUS stage, at similar levels as in MM. Specific increase in pSTAT3 levels within CD163pos cells supports that the CD163 scavenger receptor may be a useful target for future delivery of STAT3-inhibitory drugs to TAMs in MM patients.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Andersen, Morten Nørgaard","Andersen, Niels Frost","Lauridsen, Kristina Lystlund","Etzerodt, Anders","Sorensen, Boe Sandahl","Abildgaard, Niels","Plesner, Trine Lindhardt","Hokland, Marianne","Møller, Holger Jon"],"cuid":["S02-099.91-023668"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Morten N."],"keyword":["Biomarker","Bone marrow microenvironment","CD163","Cancer","Expression","MGUS","MODEL","Macrophage","Mechanisms","Multiple myeloma","Prognosis","Progression","STAT3","Tumor associated macrophages","monoclonal gammopathy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stat000000000003 is over activated within cd000000000163 sup pos sup bone marrow macrophages in both multiple myeloma and the benign pre condition mgus","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85107300716","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The work was supported by the Department of Clinical Biochemistry, Aarhus University Hospital, Denmark; The Faculty of Health, Aarhus University, Denmark; The Danish Cancer Research Foundation; The Cancer Foundation (Denmark), The Memorial Foundation of Max and Inge Wørzner, and by The Memorial Foundation of Eva and Henry Frænkel."],"id":"S02-099.91-023668","identifier":[{"id":"85107300716","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34061243","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10992042","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000656827500001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-972b3dd8-9333-4367-a947-8cd150971a11","sdu-1280745c-9ca5-43a0-b9ea-db1cdde7aac6"],"keyword":["BIOMARKER","Bone marrow microenvironment","CANCER","CD163","EXPRESSION","MECHANISMS","MGUS","MODEL","MONOCLONAL GAMMOPATHY","Macrophage","Multiple myeloma","PROGNOSIS","PROGRESSION","STAT3","TUMOR-ASSOCIATED MACROPHAGES","UNDETERMINED SIGNIFICANCE"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-222C42A2A1BE90317490BBEA33B14B69"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Skou-bygningen","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Haematology","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of clinical biochemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Haematology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten N","key":"andersenmortennørgaardpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"5820fa2e-0f0e-4429-badc-9e264f102231","name":"Andersen, Morten Nørgaard","name_org":"Andersen, Morten N","orcid":"0000-0003-0820-7789","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels F","key":"andersennielsfrostpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"d1f8badc-e2a8-4075-a157-fe526d01d545","name":"Andersen, Niels Frost","name_org":"Andersen, Niels F","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels F.","key":"andersennielsfpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Niels F.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina L","key":"lauridsenkristinalystlundpau","last":"Lauridsen","locid":"8f422b25-045f-4f98-be11-9ce47094c03b","name":"Lauridsen, Kristina Lystlund","name_org":"Lauridsen, Kristina L","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina L.","key":"lauridsenkristinalpau","last":"Lauridsen","name":"Lauridsen, Kristina L.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"etzerodtanderspau","last":"Etzerodt","locid":"c0b60588-6275-45c0-8ad2-bb91a248ff22","name":"Etzerodt, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-6757-2068","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Boe S","key":"sorensenboesandahlpau","last":"Sorensen","locid":"df36b88d-a4e0-49db-9e8e-78f8dc2120c0","name":"Sorensen, Boe Sandahl","name_org":"Sorensen, Boe S","orcid":"0000-0002-9472-8099","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Boe S.","key":"sorensenboespau","last":"Sorensen","name":"Sorensen, Boe S.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"abildgaardnielspau","last":"Abildgaard","locid":"595418b9-29f8-4fd3-8663-1b32eab3451a","name":"Abildgaard, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-6852-2014","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"plesnertrinelindhardtpau","last":"Plesner","locid":"21d950aa-6771-4a21-bcca-f259cf629e33","name":"Plesner, Trine Lindhardt","name_org":"Plesner, Trine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"plesnertrinepau","last":"Plesner","name":"Plesner, Trine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne","key":"hoklandmariannepau","last":"Hokland","locid":"b69f1338-b4a9-46f8-855a-d5fff1f2f948","name":"Hokland, Marianne","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Holger J","key":"møllerholgerjonpau","last":"Møller","locid":"b08dc9ce-d595-49c6-833a-4ec9b4223a05","name":"Møller, Holger Jon","name_org":"Møller, Holger J","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Holger J.","key":"møllerholgerjpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Holger J.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34061243"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00262-021-02952-1","issn":["03407004","14320851"],"issn_org":["03407004"],"issue":"1","journal":"Cancer Immunology, Immunotherapy","pages":"177-187","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Cancer Immunology, Immunotherapy","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85107300716"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-972b3dd8-9333-4367-a947-8cd150971a11","sdu-1280745c-9ca5-43a0-b9ea-db1cdde7aac6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"STAT3 is over-activated within CD163<sup>pos</sup> bone marrow macrophages in both Multiple Myeloma and the benign pre-condition MGUS","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.91-023668","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Re-entering the labour market after a period of unemployment can be challenging for seniors. This study investigates personal as well as circumstantial barriers and facilitators of re-employment. Unemployed seniors in Denmark (≥50 years, n = 1636) from the first wave (mid-2018) of the SeniorWorkingLife study were prospectively followed until March 2020 in national registers on labour market participation. Using weighted logistic-regression-modelled odds ratios (ORs), we estimated the association between personal and circumstantial factors at baseline and re-employment during follow-up. During follow-up, 28% re-entered paid employment. The desire to have a job (reference: not having the desire to have a job) increased the likelihood of re-employment (OR 2.35, 95% CI 1.14-4.85). Contrastingly, a higher age (60-63 vs. 50-54 years; OR 0.36, 95% CI 0.16-0.79) and poor health (OR 0.32, 95% CI 0.16-0.61) decreased the likelihood of re-employment. Sex, education and belief that age constitutes a barrier to re-employment were not associated with the likelihood of re-employment. Unemployed seniors desiring to have a job are more likely to get a job. However, a higher age and poor health are important barriers that should be taken into account, e.g., by ensuring employment opportunities for these groups in society.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Thomassen, Kristina","Sundstrup, Emil","Vinstrup, Jonas","Seeberg, Karina Glies Vincents","Andersen, Lars L."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-766930"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Employment","Humans","Muskelskeletbesvær","Occupational","Occupations","Prospective Studies","Return to work","Seniorer","Seniors","Unemployment","Worker"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"barriers and facilitators of re employment among senior workers prospective cohort study","src":["aau","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph191811536","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-766930","identifier":[{"id":"36141808","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85138329046","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a533d074-5fa5-4abb-998f-f81ca83a1527","nfa-71eac880-6869-4c19-af32-aa2653771b67"],"keyword":["Employment","Humans","Muskelskeletbesvær","Occupations","Prospective Studies","Seniorer","occupational","re-employment","return to work","seniors","unemployment","unemployment characteristics","worker"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7E1230A5ABE52BDF6476B459D70D8F67"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/488239089/ijerph_19_11536_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph191811536","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Musculoskeletal Disorders and Physical Workload"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Sport Sciences - Performance and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"thomassenpau","last":"Thomassen","name":"Thomassen, Kristina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil","key":"sundstruppau","last":"Sundstrup","locid":"688eab9a-3ad9-48b8-aad2-397c0a8ee105","name":"Sundstrup, Emil","orcid":"0000-0001-7408-222X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"vinstruppau","last":"Vinstrup","locid":"436e0a0d-1629-4634-9588-e909dfbe49b5","name":"Vinstrup, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-8430-0139","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karina Glies Vincents","key":"seebergpau","last":"Seeberg","locid":"8d8f8314-7bf8-482a-b519-9d56bdaff123","name":"Seeberg, Karina Glies Vincents","orcid":"0000-0003-2679-7591","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Louis","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"7698b281-bcfb-47ec-b41e-3ea20ceb5e52","name":"Andersen, Lars L.","name_org":"Andersen, Lars Louis","orcid":"0000-0003-2777-8085","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36141808"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ijerph191811536","issn":["16604601","16617827"],"issn_org":["16617827"],"issue":"18","journal":"International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health","paperid":"11536","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Environmental Research and Public Health","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138329046"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a533d074-5fa5-4abb-998f-f81ca83a1527","nfa-71eac880-6869-4c19-af32-aa2653771b67"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Barriers and Facilitators of Re-Employment among Senior Workers : Prospective Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-766930","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Aging increases the risk of chronic diseases, which can challenge the ability to work and thereby push senior workers out of the labour market. This study investigates the association between non-communicable diseases (NCDs) and work ability among workers ≥50 years (senior workers) with physically demanding and sedentary work, respectively. Methods: In the SeniorWorkingLife study, 12,879 senior workers replied to a questionnaire survey on work and health in 2018. Associations between the type and number of NCD and work ability (scale 0–10) were modelled using a general linear model adjusting for potential confounders and combined with model-assisted weights from national registers. Results: A higher number of NCD (multi-morbidity) was progressively associated with a lower work ability (trend test, p-value < 0.001). Physical work influenced the association between the number of NCDs and work ability. For specific diseases, mental disorders, including burn-out syndrome (least square mean difference (LSMD): −1.46, 95% CI: −1.61 to −1.32) and stress (LSMD: −1.18, 95% CI: −1.29 to −1.07), demon-strated a stronger association with a lower work ability compared with somatic diseases, such as back diseases (LSMD: −0.72, 95%CI: −0.80 to −0.64). Conclusions: Multimorbidity was progressively associated with a lower work ability in senior workers, especially among those with physical work.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Seeberg, Karina Glies Vincents","Skovlund, Sebastian Venge","Bláfoss, Rúni","Thomassen, Kristina","Malchow-Møller, Lasse","Sundstrup, Emil","Andersen, Lars L."],"cuid":["S03-099.81-766477"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Seeberg, Karina Glies Vincents"],"keyword":["Chronic Disease","Cross Sectional Studies","Humans","Mental disorder","Multimorbidity","Musculoskeletal Diseases","Noncommunicable Diseases epidemiology","Occupations","Somatic disease","Work Capacity Evaluation","Work ability","Workers","Workplace"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the interplay between multimorbidity physical work demands and work ability cross sectional study among 000000000012 000000000879 senior workers","src":["aau","nfa","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph19095023","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Author L.L.A. obtained a grantfrom TrygFonden, Denmark https://www.trygfonden.dk/ english (accessed on 10 April 2022)."],"id":"S03-099.81-766477","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9103436","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85128377245","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35564418","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-03fb0913-15ee-4986-94c0-38746a165e84","nfa-8cb0a39b-a5a8-42b8-9c7f-e89410403e55","sdu-0cc878e4-df46-4e69-9e6b-f0a71e98917e"],"keyword":["Cross-Sectional Studies","Humans","Noncommunicable Diseases/epidemiology","Occupations","Work Capacity Evaluation","chronic disease","mental disorder","multimorbidity","musculoskeletal diseases","somatic disease","work ability","workers","workplace"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-3163A05837B091568E32D39D1832A492"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/470426290/ijerph_19_05023_v3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph19095023","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/202878375/ijerph_19_05023_v3.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Musculoskeletal Disorders and Physical Workload"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Muscle Physiology and Biomechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Sport Sciences - Performance and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karina Glies Vincents","key":"seebergpau","last":"Seeberg","locid":"8d8f8314-7bf8-482a-b519-9d56bdaff123","name":"Seeberg, Karina 