":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8bffc514-d71e-40ba-b979-910dfb03ec5e","name":"Andersen, Zorana Jovanovic","name_org":"Andersen, Zorana J","orcid":"0000-0003-4138-9828","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Göran","key":"pershagenpau","last":"Pershagen","name":"Pershagen, Göran","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 32 11","country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"5bf2a665-def4-499c-9c63-0c440da72e20","name":"Sørensen, Mette","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34605674"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1289/ehp8949","issn":["00916765","15529924"],"issn_org":["00916765"],"issue":"10","journal":"Environmental Health Perspectives","paperid":"107002","publisher":"Public Health Services, US Dept of Health and Human Services","status":"p","title":"Environmental Health Perspectives","volume":"129"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117630033"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-aae3fa9f-23c1-4858-a9f0-290305004836","au-a49f814c-e21e-42df-8432-01f78aa57602","ku-6cbc9ef5-52e9-4e04-98c6-a20c2b53eb2b","ruc-15b318cb-798a-40c5-832b-5efb4ae0ea90"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Long-Term Exposure to Transportation Noise and Risk of Incident Stroke : A Pooled Study of Nine Scandinavian Cohorts","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.85-008247","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Digital imaging of dermatological patients is a novel approach to remote assessment and has recently become more relevant since telehealth and remote decentralized clinical trials are gaining ground. Objective: We aimed to investigate whether photographs taken by a smartphone are of adequate quality to allow severity assessments to be made and to explore the usefulness of an established atopic dermatitis severity assessment instrument on photograph evaluation. Methods: During scheduled visits in a previously published study, the investigating doctor evaluated the severity of atopic dermatitis using the Scoring AD (SCORAD) index and took photographs of the most representative lesions (target lesions) with both a smartphone and a digital single-lens reflex camera (DSLR). The photographs were then assessed by 5 dermatologists using the intensity items of the SCORAD (iSCORAD), which consists of erythema, oedema/papulation, excoriations, lichenification, oozing/crusts, and dryness (scale 0-3, maximum score 18). The mean iSCORAD of the photographs was calculated and compared with in-person assessments using Pearson correlation and Bland-Altman plots. Intraclass correlation coefficients were used for interrater reliability. Results: A total of 942 photographs from 95 patients were assessed. The iSCORAD based on smartphone photographs correlated strongly with the evaluations performed in person (iSCORAD: r=0.78, P<.001; objective SCORAD: r=0.81, P<.001; and total SCORAD: r=0.78, P<.001). For iSCORAD specifically, a Bland-Altman plot showed a difference in mean score of 1.31 for in-person and remote iSCORAD. In addition, the interrater agreement between the 5 rating dermatologists was 0.93 (95% CI 0.911-0.939). A total of 170 lesions were photographed, and the difference in mean scores was 1.32, 1.13, and 1.43 between in-person and remote evaluations based on photographs taken by a DSLR camera, a smartphone without flash, and a smartphone with flash, respectively. Conclusions: In terms of quality, remote atopic dermatitis severity assessments based on photographs are comparable to in-person assessments, and smartphone photos can be used to assess atopic dermatitis severity to a similar degree as photographs from a DSLR camera. Further, the variation in how the dermatologists in this study rated the iSCORAD based on the photographs was very low.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Ali, Zarqa","Joergensen, Kristina Melbardis","Andersen, Anders Daniel","Chiriac, Andrei","Bjerre-Christensen, Theis","Manole, Ionela","Dutei, Ana Maria","Deaconescu, Irina","Suru, Alina","Serban, Adina","Isberg, Ari Pall","Dahiya, Priyanka","Thomsen, Simon Francis","Zibert, John Robert"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-471523"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agreement","Assessment","Atopic dermatitis","EASI","Eczema","Photo","Photographs","Remote assessment","SCORAD","Severity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"remote rating of atopic dermatitis severity using photo based assessments proof of concept and reliability evaluation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/24766","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-471523","identifier":[{"id":"85106924979","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8188317","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34032580","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-828414b5-604c-46df-8a7d-1d9e68ce8b6d"],"keyword":["Agreement","Assessment","Atopic dermatitis","EASI","Eczema","Photo","Photographs","Remote assessment","SCORAD","Severity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ACBD043BF17391951ACFC1CFB336E632"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/280287158/Remote_rating_of_atopic_dermatitis.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/24766","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Omhu A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Inflammation, Metabolism and Oxidation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Zarqa","key":"alipau","last":"Ali","name":"Ali, Zarqa","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristina Melbardis","key":"joergensenpau","last":"Joergensen","name":"Joergensen, Kristina Melbardis","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders Daniel","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Anders Daniel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andrei","key":"chiriacpau","last":"Chiriac","name":"Chiriac, Andrei","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Theis","key":"bjerrechristensenpau","last":"Bjerre-Christensen","name":"Bjerre-Christensen, Theis","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ionela","key":"manolepau","last":"Manole","name":"Manole, Ionela","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ana Maria","key":"duteipau","last":"Dutei","name":"Dutei, Ana Maria","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Irina","key":"deaconescupau","last":"Deaconescu","name":"Deaconescu, Irina","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Alina","key":"surupau","last":"Suru","name":"Suru, Alina","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adina","key":"serbanpau","last":"Serban","name":"Serban, Adina","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ari Pall","key":"isbergpau","last":"Isberg","name":"Isberg, Ari Pall","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Priyanka","key":"dahiyapau","last":"Dahiya","name":"Dahiya, Priyanka","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Simon Francis","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"045de28d-7e61-4908-8fa9-afd09ac8234a","name":"Thomsen, Simon Francis","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"John Robert","key":"zibertpau","last":"Zibert","name":"Zibert, John Robert","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34032580"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2196/24766","issn":["2561326X"],"issue":"5","journal":"JMIR Formative Research","paperid":"e24766","status":"p","title":"JMIR Formative Research","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85106924979"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","omhu a/s (biz)","studies&me"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-828414b5-604c-46df-8a7d-1d9e68ce8b6d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Remote rating of atopic dermatitis severity using photo-based assessments : Proof-of-concept and reliability evaluation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-471523","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Randomized controlled trials (RCTs) indicate that bacille Calmette-Guérin (BCG) vaccination provides broad beneficial \"nonspecific\"protection against infections. We investigated the effect on in-hospital mortality of providing BCG immediately upon admission to a neonatal intensive care unit (NICU), rather than BCG-at-discharge. The pretrial NICU mortality was 13% and we hypothesized that BCG would reduce mortality by 40%. Methods: Parallel-group, open-label RCT was initiated in 2013 in Guinea-Bissau. Neonatal intensive care unit-admitted neonates were randomized 1:1 to BCG+oral polio vaccine (OPV) immediately (intervention) versus BCG+OPV at hospital discharge (control; usual practice). The trial was discontinued due to decreasing in-hospital mortality and major NICU restructuring. We assessed overall and disease-specific mortality by randomization allocation in cox proportional hazards models providing mortality rate ratios (MRRs). Results: We recruited 3353 neonates, and the overall mortality was 3.1% (52 of 1676) for BCG-vaccinated neonates versus 3.3% (55 of 1677) for controls (MRR=0.94; 0.64-1.36). For noninfectious causes of death, the MRR was 1.20 (0.70-2.07), and there tended to be fewer deaths from infections in the BCG group (N=14) than among controls (N=21) (MRR=0.65; 0.33-1.28). Conclusions: Providing BCG+OPV to frail neonates was safe and might protect against fatal infection in the immediate newborn period. Deaths due to prematurity and perinatal complications were unaffected by BCG.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Schaltz-Buchholzer, Frederik","Aaby, Peter","Monteiro, Ivan","Camala, Luis","Faurholt Simonsen, Simone","Nørtoft Frankel, Hannah","Lindberg Larsen, Kristina","Golding, Christian N","Kollmann, Tobias R","Amenyogbe, Nelly","Benn, Christine Stabell","Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-585484"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","America, North","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Schaltz-Buchholzer, Frederik"],"country":["Australia","Canada","Guinea-Bissau"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bandim Health Project","Telethon Kids Institute","University of British Columbia (UBC)"],"keyword":["Bacille Calmette Guérin vaccine","Neonatal mortality","Nonspecific effects of vaccines"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immediate bacille calmette guérin vaccination to neonates requiring perinatal treatment at the maternity ward in guinea bissau a randomized controlled trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/191576066/Manuscript_Clean.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-585484","identifier":[{"id":"85109108967","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33893799","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-2adfc29d-ba94-4a74-b373-e0ac480bd2d2"],"keyword":["bacille Calmette-Guérin vaccine","neonatal mortality","nonspecific effects of vaccines","vaccination at birth"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6B90E38E2E366581EA3C9E3D2AE39144"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/191576066/Manuscript_Clean.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gw","key":"bandim health project","loc":["Guinea-Bissau","Africa"],"name":"Bandim Health Project","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"telethon kids institute","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Telethon Kids Institute","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"university of british columbia","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of British Columbia (UBC)","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik","key":"schaltzbuchholzerpau","last":"Schaltz-Buchholzer","locid":"0acc453e-bdff-4bd0-b030-be32696a2e97","name":"Schaltz-Buchholzer, Frederik","orcid":"0000-0001-7643-8322","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"aabypau","last":"Aaby","name":"Aaby, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivan","key":"monteiropau","last":"Monteiro","name":"Monteiro, Ivan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luis","key":"camalapau","last":"Camala","name":"Camala, Luis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Simone","key":"faurholtsimonsenpau","last":"Faurholt Simonsen","name":"Faurholt Simonsen, Simone","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hannah","key":"nørtoftfrankelpau","last":"Nørtoft Frankel","name":"Nørtoft Frankel, Hannah","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg Larsen","name":"Lindberg Larsen, Kristina","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian N","key":"goldingpau","last":"Golding","name":"Golding, Christian N","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias R","key":"kollmannpau","last":"Kollmann","name":"Kollmann, Tobias R","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Nelly","key":"amenyogbepau","last":"Amenyogbe","name":"Amenyogbe, Nelly","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christine","key":"stabellbennpau","last":"Stabell Benn","locid":"ad42068c-800c-4c51-93c0-eb068fd03b8a","name":"Benn, Christine Stabell","name_org":"Stabell Benn, Christine","orcid":"0000-0001-6102-3810","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"bjerregaardandersenpau","last":"Bjerregaard-Andersen","locid":"a8a0b3c8-4070-4770-86b2-1cb837092b6b","name":"Bjerregaard-Andersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4128-5714","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33893799"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/infdis/jiab220","issn":["00221899","15376613"],"issn_org":["00221899"],"issue":"11","journal":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","pages":"1935-1944","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Infectious Diseases","volume":"224"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85109108967"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2adfc29d-ba94-4a74-b373-e0ac480bd2d2"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Immediate Bacille Calmette-Guérin vaccination to neonates requiring perinatal treatment at the maternity ward in Guinea-Bissau : A randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-585484","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Clusters may originate from random and accidental events, but the emergence and growth of successful clusters depend on favorable framework conditions and the agency of central organizational actors such as universities, cluster organization, incumbent industry firms, funding sources and start-ups. This paper analyses how the roles and importance of these central organizational actors change throughout the emergence and growth of an innovative cluster. Based on an in-depth case study of the robotics cluster in Odense, Denmark, we develop a theoretical framework for how the roles of organizational actors change throughout the early life cycle of a spontaneously emerging cluster.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","Rasmussen, Erik Stavnsager","Madsen, Tage Koed"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-593850"],"event":{"end":"2021-09-14","place":"Gøteborg, se","start":"2021-09-10","title":"International 22nd CINet Conference","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"who takes the lead how roles and importance of organizational actors change throughout the early life cycle of a cluster","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-593850","ids":["sdu-47d520ec-d53a-432c-97a0-c587ac87f42d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-57D1174E7139A39BD90C263BCA56769B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM), Centre for Integrative Innovation Management","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM), Centre for Integrative Innovation Management (C*I2M)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"46d2bbb6-cde6-45b4-b04d-dcbcbad97c83","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Erik Stavnsager","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"75db9f06-020a-47a0-a7e1-37fe7d28ee06","name":"Rasmussen, Erik Stavnsager","orcid":"0000-0002-2448-9838","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tage Koed","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"a9e04f87-078a-4064-97ec-5337ddb911df","name":"Madsen, Tage Koed","orcid":"0000-0002-0093-5100","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Continuous Innovation Network","status":"p","subtitle":"22nd CINet Conference","title":"International CINet Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-47d520ec-d53a-432c-97a0-c587ac87f42d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Who Takes The Lead? : How Roles And Importance Of Organizational Actors Change Throughout The Early Life Cycle Of A Cluster","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-593850","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Premature death from all causes and cardiovascular disease (CVD) causes is higher among persons with diabetes. Objective: To investigate the association between time spent cycling and all-cause and CVD mortality among persons with diabetes, as well as to evaluate the association between change in time spent cycling and risk of all-cause and CVD mortality. Design, Setting, and Participants: This prospective cohort study included 7459 adults with diabetes from the European Prospective Investigation into Cancer and Nutrition study. Questionnaires regarding medical history, sociodemographic, and lifestyle information were administered in 10 Western European countries from 1992 through 2000 (baseline examination) and at a second examination 5 years after baseline. A total of 5423 participants with diabetes completed both examinations. The final updated primary analysis was conducted on November 13, 2020. Exposures: The primary exposure was self-reported time spent cycling per week at the baseline examination. The secondary exposure was change in cycling status from baseline to the second examination. Main Outcomes and Measures: The primary and secondary outcomes were all-cause and CVD mortality, respectively, adjusted for other physical activity modalities, diabetes duration, and sociodemographic and lifestyle factors. Results: Of the 7459 adults with diabetes included in the analysis, the mean (SD) age was 55.9 (7.7) years, and 3924 (52.6%) were female. During 110 944 person-years of follow-up, 1673 deaths from all causes were registered. Compared with the reference group of people who reported no cycling at baseline (0 min/wk), the multivariable-adjusted hazard ratios for all-cause mortality were 0.78 (95% CI, 0.61-0.99), 0.76 (95% CI, 0.65-0.88), 0.68 (95% CI, 0.57-0.82), and 0.76 (95% CI, 0.63-0.91) for cycling 1 to 59, 60 to 149, 150 to 299, and 300 or more min/wk, respectively. In an analysis of change in time spent cycling with 57 802 person-years of follow-up, a total of 975 deaths from all causes were recorded. Compared with people who reported no cycling at both examinations, the multivariable-adjusted hazard ratios for all-cause mortality were 0.90 (95% CI, 0.71-1.14) in those who cycled and then stopped, 0.65 (95% CI, 0.46-0.92) in initial noncyclists who started cycling, and 0.65 (95% CI, 0.53-0.80) for people who reported cycling at both examinations. Similar results were observed for CVD mortality. Conclusion and Relevance: In this cohort study, cycling was associated with lower all-cause and CVD mortality risk among people with diabetes independent of practicing other types of physical activity. Participants who took up cycling between the baseline and second examination had a considerably lower risk of both all-cause and CVD mortality compared with consistent noncyclists.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Ried-Larsen, Mathias","Rasmussen, Martin Gillies","Blond, Kim","Overvad, Thure Filskov","Overvad, Kim","Steindorf, Karen","Katzke, Verena","Andersen, Julie L M","Petersen, Kristina E N","Aune, Dagfinn","Tsilidis, Kostas K","Heath, Alicia K","Papier, Keren","Panico, Salvatore","Masala, Giovanna","Pala, Valeria","Weiderpass, Elisabete","Freisling, Heinz","Bergmann, Manuela M","Verschuren, W M Monique","Zamora-Ros, Raul","Colorado-Yohar, Sandra M","Spijkerman, Annemieke M W","Schulze, Matthias B","Ardanaz, Eva M A","Andersen, Lars Bo","Wareham, Nick","Brage, Søren","Grøntved, Anders"],"cuid":["S03-094.48-007313"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ried-Larsen, Mathias"],"country":["Colombia","France","Germany","Greece","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bellvitge Biomedical Research Institute","Bellvitge University Hospital","Biomedical Research Institute of Murcia","Biomedical Research Institute of Murcia - Arrixaca","CIBER Epidemiologia Y Salud Publica","Carlos III Health Institute (ISCIII) (CIBER)","Centre for Infectious Disease Control","Centro de Investigación Biomédica en Red (CIBER)","Fondazione IRCCS Istituto Nazionale dei Tumori","German Cancer Research Center","German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ)","German Center for Diabetes Research","German Institute of Human Nutrition","German Institute of Human Nutrition Potsdam-Rehbruecke","IRCCS Fondazione Istituto Nazionale per lo studio e la cura dei tumori - Milano","Imperial College London","Institute for the Study and Prevention of Cancer","International Agency for Research on Cancer","National Cancer Institute of Milan","National Institute for Public Health and the Environment (RIVM)","National Institute of Public Health and the Environment","Navarra Institute for Health Research","Prevention and Clinical Network (ISPRO)","Public Health Institute of Navarra","Universidad de Antioquia","University of Antioquia","University of Cambridge","University of Ioannina","University of Naples Federico II","University of Oxford","University of Potsdam","Utrecht University","Western Norway University of Applied Sciences","World Health Organization"],"keyword":["Air pollution","Exercise","Heart disease","Leisure time","Life Expectancy","Mediterranean diet","Physical activity","Risk Factors","Short term exposure","US ADULTS"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"OT":["Biomedical Research Institute of Murcia(IMIB-Arrixaca)"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of cycling with all cause and cardiovascular disease mortality am