{"abstract":"Metazoan RNA polymerase II activity is promiscuous within and outside of conventional genes. Lykke-Andersen et al. show that cleavage and polyadenylation (CPA) and integrator (INT) transcription termination complexes operate genome-wide in sequence- and context-dependent manners, respectively. The INT complex is suggested to take part in quality control of non-productive transcription.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Lykke-Andersen, Søren","Žumer, Kristina","Molska, Ewa","Rouvière, Jérôme O.","Wu, Guifen","Demel, Carina","Schwalb, Björn","Schmid, Manfred","Cramer, Patrick","Jensen, Torben Heick"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-133548"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cramer, Patrick","Jensen, Torben Heick","Lykke-Andersen, Søren"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Biophysics"],"keyword":["Integrator complex","Pervasive transcription"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrator is a genome wide attenuator of non productive transcription","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2020.07.17.208702v1.full.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-133548","identifier":[{"id":"33385327","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85099681533","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-076d973b-fadd-4340-854e-095c25287a30"],"keyword":["cleavage and polyadenylation complex","genome-wide transcription termination","integrator complex","pervasive transcription"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C296BFA00E53597E6A3B65F5380AC476"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2020.07.17.208702v1.full.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics, Department of Molecular Biology and Genetics - RNA Biology and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max planck institute of biophysics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute of Biophysics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"lykkeandersenpau","last":"Lykke-Andersen","locid":"18a39eed-b06f-4bc2-8a23-963f62e41925","name":"Lykke-Andersen, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"žumerpau","last":"Žumer","name":"Žumer, Kristina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ewa Šmidová","key":"molskapau","last":"Molska","locid":"9b1f7bb8-a231-4c6d-b728-aacd6f480d09","name":"Molska, Ewa","name_org":"Molska, Ewa Šmidová","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jérôme O.","key":"rouvièrepau","last":"Rouvière","locid":"6e58b4ad-4bd5-4ae8-a9dd-560a2deaff0f","name":"Rouvière, Jérôme O.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Guifen","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","locid":"26ce7e4b-77f0-4465-be8b-65cb6222dcb1","name":"Wu, Guifen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Carina","key":"demelpau","last":"Demel","name":"Demel, Carina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Björn","key":"schwalbpau","last":"Schwalb","name":"Schwalb, Björn","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Manfred","key":"schmidpau","last":"Schmid","locid":"4cab8443-1ab8-404d-b12f-1a836ef138ba","name":"Schmid, Manfred","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick","key":"cramerpau","last":"Cramer","name":"Cramer, Patrick","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Heick","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a08c2bdc-4318-45f1-bb8a-1cabcb464b01","name":"Jensen, Torben Heick","orcid":"0000-0001-5127-1239","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33385327"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.molcel.2020.12.014","issn":["10972765","10974164"],"issn_org":["10972765"],"issue":"3","journal":"Molecular Cell","publisher":"Cell Press","status":"p","title":"Molecular Cell","volume":"81"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85099681533"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-076d973b-fadd-4340-854e-095c25287a30"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Integrator is a genome-wide attenuator of non-productive transcription","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-133548","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Introduction Moped riders have a comparably high risk of getting seriously injured or killed in road traffic crashes. The moped is the first motor vehicle legally available to adolescents, but knowledge about young moped riders is limited. The few existing studies indicate that violations are a key factor in crash involvement. Method Using the Theory of Planned Behaviour, the purpose of this study is to explore and identify key beliefs underlying engagement in violations among adolescent moped riders. We conducted four focus groups including 35 participating adolescents aged between 15 and 17. We analysed the data using a four step directed content analysis approach. Results Engagement in violations was associated with affective and functional advantages such as excitement, saving time, convenience and avoidance of expenses and parent involvement. Level of approval varied across violations and was expressed directly as well as indirectly by both parents and peers. Strong beliefs in good riding skills and the ability to keep control over the moped facilitated engagement in violations. Actual and expected apprehension by the police was the main barrier, thus preventing engagement in violations. Conclusion Advantages associated with engagement in violations, approval from peers, parents and general society, and a strong belief in the ability to avoid negative consequences facilitate engagement in violations among young moped riders. Inclusion of the identified beliefs in preventive measures is discussed.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Møller, Mette","Krogh Andersen, Sandra Kristina","Bonde, Nanna Skou","Hagenzieker, Marjan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-339005"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Møller, Mette"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology"],"keyword":["Adolescence","Focus Groups","Road safety","Theory of planned behaviour","Young road users"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"engagement in violations among young moped riders using a qualitative approach to reveal underlying beliefs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/238950902/R1_Manuscript_changes_not_shown.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-339005","identifier":[{"id":"85099380394","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-736c9724-4aaf-417e-bc11-4be1e32b672d"],"keyword":["Adolescence","Focus groups","Moped","Powered two-wheelers","Road safety","Theory of planned behaviour","Young road users"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E2DAC863817C550A183B0B529BE7F203"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/238950902/R1_Manuscript_changes_not_shown.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transport","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transport, Transport Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"bc2c2ce5-846a-48d8-8f1c-98639e8c7604","name":"Møller, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-0012-8691","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sandra Kristina","key":"kroghandersenpau","last":"Krogh Andersen","locid":"b35dc181-b805-4bfd-8753-398a7f4021f4","name":"Krogh Andersen, Sandra Kristina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nanna Skou","key":"bondepau","last":"Bonde","locid":"f3163949-cb40-41ce-ae66-9c54a00af84b","name":"Bonde, Nanna Skou","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marjan","key":"hagenziekerpau","last":"Hagenzieker","name":"Hagenzieker, Marjan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jth.2020.101002","issn":["22141405","22141413"],"issn_org":["22141405"],"journal":"Journal of Transport & Health","paperid":"101002","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Transport & Health","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85099380394"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-736c9724-4aaf-417e-bc11-4be1e32b672d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Engagement in violations among young moped riders – Using a qualitative approach to reveal underlying beliefs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-339005","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Intellectual property (IP) and the protection of IP is of increasing importance to firms’ competitiveness, and firms must be able to defend their IP when it is infringed upon. In most markets, IP and the defense of IP is a stringent legal process, but in developing markets and markets undergoing changes, this is not necessarily so. The Chinese IP system and protection is comparatively new, and the system is still under development. In this study, we analyze the relationship between firms’ previous litigation experience and litigation outcomes using a sample of 10,211 court cases tried in China between 2001 and 2009. We find that despite litigation being a rare event for most firms, plaintiffs’ prior litigation experience and especially prior successful litigation experience or experience with specific case types is related to their likelihood of a positive outcome. However, plaintiffs’ successful application of prior litigation experience is contingent on the type of litigation case.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","Beukel, Karin","Tyler, Beverly B."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-045141"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Virginia Polytechnic Institute and State University"],"keyword":["D83","O43","Organizational learning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Circular Food Technology, Copenhagen"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"learning to litigate the relationship between past litigation experience and litigation outcomes in the chinese intellectual property system","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41471-021-00118-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-045141","identifier":[{"id":"85120307421","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a8b7a54c-c263-4090-b248-0df75bcc46e6","sdu-b61e3e47-4ab5-4e73-8329-01b40ecd7a13"],"keyword":["D83","IP litigation","K41","Learning to litigate","Litigation experience","N45","O43","Organizational learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8880C348B4176EC45D37EFD2A058AFB1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/202961883/VaarstAndersen2021_Article_LearningToLitigateTheRelations.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s41471-021-00118-4","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/289164769/Learning_to_litigate_The_relationship_between_past_litigation_experience_and_litigation_outcomes_in_the_Chinese_intellectual_property_system.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM), Centre for Integrative Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"Univers