øj, Carsten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33011524"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jad.2020.09.110","issn":["01650327","15732517"],"issn_org":["01650327"],"journal":"Journal of Affective Disorders","pages":"453-459","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Affective Disorders","volume":"278"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091742171"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ca517318-99ed-4634-a731-9da927537a7d","sdu-6d4a2a3b-0771-4edc-88ca-22977ddb6b66"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Association between neonatal homecare for preterm infants and incidence of severe postpartum depression in mothers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.39-046195","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This workshop aims to bring together Research through Design (RtD) practitioners in the DIS community, giving them a space to present, debate, and discuss issues emerging from their work. In particular, our goal is to catalyze a focused conversation on contexts and specific situations of research through design, discussing the ins-and-outs of working in a specific context and with particular issues of consequence. Building on the success of prior RtD and design research workshops at HCI conferences, this workshop will focus on how RtD artifacts operate in these contexts, with the goal of connecting diverse artefacts with broader methods in HCI and Design.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Odom, William","Pierce, James","Andersen, Kristina","Boucher, Andy","Chatting, David","Gaver, William"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384560"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","California College of the Arts","Eindhoven University of Technology","Goldsmiths, University of London","Simon Fraser University"],"keyword":["Context","ISSUES","Research through Design","practice based design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rtd in situ discussing the domains and impact of design research","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85550909/DIS20_RtD_Workshop_Abstract_CR.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384560","identifier":[{"id":"85090152462","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-dfedc8ee-9cab-4297-ac94-f37aa792bb95"],"keyword":["Research through design","context","issues","practice-based design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E075F6328B35800662992E00E2F953F9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85550909/DIS20_RtD_Workshop_Abstract_CR.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, IxD Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"simon fraser university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Simon Fraser University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"california college of the arts","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"California College of the Arts","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"goldsmiths university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Goldsmiths, University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","locid":"3ad26d6b-4619-4a9f-a1b6-8424aab1dd52","name":"Jenkins, Tom","orcid":"0000-0001-6135-410X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"William","key":"odompau","last":"Odom","name":"Odom, William","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"piercepau","last":"Pierce","name":"Pierce, James","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Kristina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Andy","key":"boucherpau","last":"Boucher","name":"Boucher, Andy","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"chattingpau","last":"Chatting","name":"Chatting, David","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"William","key":"gaverpau","last":"Gaver","name":"Gaver, William","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3393914.3395913","eisbn":["9781450379878"],"pages":"401-404","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"DIS' 20 Companion: Companion Publication of the 2020 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090152462"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-dfedc8ee-9cab-4297-ac94-f37aa792bb95"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"RtD in Situ : Discussing the Domains and Impact of Design Research","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384560","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The majority of tuberculosis (TB) cases in low-incidence countries occur in migrants. Only few studies have assessed the long-term TB risk in migrants after immigration, and datasets have not considered this across a range of diverse migrant groups. This nationwide study aimed to investigate long-term TB risk among migrants according to migrant status and region of origin. METHODS: This cohort study included all migrants aged  ≥ 18 years who obtained residence in Denmark from 1993 to 2015, with a mean follow-up of 10.8 years [standard deviation (SD) 7.3]. Migrants were categorized based on legal status of residence and region of origin. Incidence rates (IR) and rate ratios (IRR) were estimated by Poisson regression. RESULTS: A total of 142 314 migrants were included. Across all migrants, the TB risk was highest during year 1 of residence (IR 275/100 000 person-years; 95% CI 249-305) followed by a gradual decline, though TB risk remained high for over a decade. Compared with the Danish-born population, the IRRs after 7-8 years were particularly higher among former asylum seekers (IRR 31; 95% CI 20-46), quota refugees (IRR 31; 95% CI 16-71), and family-reunified with refugees (IRR 22; 95% CI 12-44). Sub-Saharan African migrants also experienced elevated risk (IRR 75; 95% CI 51-109). The proportion of migrants with pulmonary TB was 52.4%. CONCLUSION: All migrant groups experienced an initial high TB risk, but long-term risk remained high in key migrant groups. Most European countries focus TB screening on or soon after arrival. Our study suggests that approaches to TB screening should be adapted, with migrant populations benefiting from long-term access to preventive health services.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Kristensen, Kristina Langholz","Ravn, Pernille","Petersen, Jørgen Holm","Hargreaves, Sally","Nellums, Laura B.","Friedland, Jon S.","Andersen, Peter Henrik","Norredam, Marie","Lillebaek, Troels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-469265"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","St. George's University of London","University of Nottingham"],"keyword":["Asylum seekers","Immigration","Long term risk","Migrant","Refugees","Tuberculosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term risk of tuberculosis among migrants according to migrant status a cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-469265","identifier":[{"id":"85089014102","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32380550","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7ea830a4-3dee-40e7-9f20-7b22ecfa924f"],"keyword":["Tuberculosis","asylum seekers","immigration","long-term risk","migrant","refugees"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-840AEEC67D4C57151E4560A8F65C0BC1"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: infection medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"st george s university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"St. George's University of London","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of nottingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Nottingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina Langholz","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Kristina Langholz","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Pernille","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"3f19690c-0d72-4d09-a542-a309efd6fb0a","name":"Ravn, Pernille","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jørgen Holm","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"33c1c5b2-2e1e-4259-b4d7-04657a2bdb9b","name":"Petersen, Jørgen Holm","orcid":"0000-0003-3979-7443","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Sally","key":"hargreavespau","last":"Hargreaves","name":"Hargreaves, Sally","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Laura B.","key":"nellumspau","last":"Nellums","name":"Nellums, Laura B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jon S.","key":"friedlandpau","last":"Friedland","name":"Friedland, Jon S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter Henrik","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Peter Henrik","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marie","key":"norredampau","last":"Norredam","locid":"b2ded723-225a-455c-ae7b-9be191ab1b53","name":"Norredam, Marie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Troels","key":"lillebaekpau","last":"Lillebaek","locid":"4c4e219b-6ac0-4067-a078-ef52b9c2beff","name":"Lillebaek, Troels","orcid":"0000-0002-2601-2718","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32380550"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ije/dyaa063","issn":["03005771","14643685"],"issn_org":["03005771"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Epidemiology","pages":"776-785","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Epidemiology","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089014102"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7ea830a4-3dee-40e7-9f20-7b22ecfa924f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Long-term risk of tuberculosis among migrants according to migrant status : a cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-469265","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Some start-ups treat regulatoryconstraints as exogenous and beyond their control, while other start-ups treatregulatory constraints as endogenous and possible to influence. However, thusfar, no explanation has been offered for why start-ups differ in their responsesto regulatory constraints. Based on 49interviews with start-ups and other industry actors this paper examines start-ups’responses to regulatory constraints in the market for drone applications. Wefind that variation in start-ups’ responses is instigated by start-ups’ temporalorientation. Start-ups pursuing applications targeted at present markets orfuture potential markets treat regulation as exogenous. In contrast, start-ups thatpursue market applications bridging current and future potential markets aremore likely to treat regulation as endogenous.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","Frederiksen, Marianne Harbo","Knudsen, Mette Præst","Krabbe, Anders Dahl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-606351"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"keyword":["Drone","Start up","Strategy","regulation markets"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the strategic responses of start ups to regulatory constraints in the nascent drone market","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/175205688/CINet_2019_v2_SAM_121736.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-606351","identifier":[{"id":"85087386526","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-73da44d6-6569-4f11-9507-7efd37a4de02"],"keyword":["Drone","M13 new firms","Sectorial Planning Methods","Start-ups, l22 firm organization and market structure, l52 industrial policy","regulation markets","start-up","strategy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-476BA5F34E9ABDB88B6A33DAFE4D5565"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/175205688/CINet_2019_v2_SAM_121736.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM), Centre for Integrative Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"46d2bbb6-cde6-45b4-b04d-dcbcbad97c83","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marianne Harbo","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","locid":"cfe310fc-a616-44d6-b340-91ceda7e4029","name":"Frederiksen, Marianne Harbo","orcid":"0000-0002-1518-7416","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Præst","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"efc4aa3e-11bb-4546-b241-8ce6dd970891","name":"Knudsen, Mette Præst","orcid":"0000-0002-2055-5308","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Dahl","key":"krabbepau","last":"Krabbe","name":"Krabbe, Anders Dahl","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.respol.2020.104055","issn":["00487333"],"issue":"10","journal":"Research Policy","paperid":"104055","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Research Policy","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85087386526"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-73da44d6-6569-4f11-9507-7efd37a4de02"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The strategic responses of start-ups to regulatory constraints in the nascent drone market","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-606351","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Individuals with neurofibromatosis 1 (NF1) may have problems in managing the transition between childhood and adulthood, such as forming a relationship or finding a partner. We aimed to determine the association between NF1 and forming and ending marital or cohabiting relationships by comparing a large Danish population of adults with NF1 with population comparisons. In this population-based cohort study, we compared a population of Danish adults who were hospitalized for or with complications to prior diagnosed NF1 (n = 787) with population comparisons matched on gender and birth year (n = 7787) through nationwide registries with annually updated information on marriage and cohabitation. Discrete-time survival models were used to estimate hazard ratios (HRs) and 95% confidence intervals (CIs) for the formation and termination of relationships, with adjustment for birth year, gender, and somatic and psychiatric comorbidities at entry. Individuals with NF1 were significantly less likely to form a relationship (HR = 0.65; 95% CI: 0.58-0.73), with the lowest association for individuals ≥33 years (HR 0.40; 95% CI: 0.25-0.63) and the highest for those aged 18-20 years (HR 0.82; 95% CI: 0.70-0.96). No significant difference was found for ending relationships (HR 1.00; 95% CI: 0.86-1.16). In conclusion, individuals who were hospitalized for NF1 are less likely to engage in marital or cohabiting relationships than population comparisons and are older when they form their first relationship. Once a relationship has been established, however, couples with a NF1-individual are not at greater risk of ending the relationship.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Kjaer, Trille Kristina","Andersen, Elisabeth Wreford","Olsen, Maja","Kenborg, Line","Bidstrup, Pernille Envold","Doser, Karoline","Hove, Hanne","Østergaard, John Rosendahl","Johansen, Christoffer","Sørensen, Sven Asger","Mulvihill, John J.","Winther, Jeanette Falck","Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-013858"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Kjaer, Trille Kristina"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oklahoma"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Denmark","Divorce statistics numerical data","Experience","Female","Hospitalization statistics numerical data","Humans","Male","Marriage statistics numerical data","Middle Aged","Neurofibromatosis 1 epidemiology","Type 1","Young adults"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forming and ending marital or cohabiting relationships in a danish population based cohort of individuals with neurofibromatosis 000000000001","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41431-020-0645-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-013858","identifier":[{"id":"32424325","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7382505","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85085209514","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000533845300002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-11ac222c-7978-4586-854d-be37de238532","ku-8f2a939f-6399-4d3f-99d6-17e7f46d8a0c"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Denmark","Divorce/statistics & numerical data","EXPERIENCE","Female","Hospitalization/statistics & numerical data","Humans","Male","Marriage/statistics & numerical data","Middle Aged","Neurofibromatosis 1/epidemiology","TYPE-1","YOUNG-ADULTS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-34C81D716C7A60111831D741BB3D57BE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41431-020-0645-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7382505/pdf/41431_2020_Article_645.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of oklahoma","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Oklahoma","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trille Kristina","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","name":"Kjaer, Trille Kristina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth Wreford","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Elisabeth Wreford","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Maja","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"kenborgpau","last":"Kenborg","name":"Kenborg, Line","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Envold","key":"bidstruppau","last":"Bidstrup","name":"Bidstrup, Pernille Envold","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karoline","key":"doserpau","last":"Doser","name":"Doser, Karoline","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hanne","key":"hovepau","last":"Hove","name":"Hove, Hanne","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"John R.","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"b69a2a94-da86-481e-9841-e510996269f0","name":"Østergaard, John Rosendahl","name_org":"Østergaard, John R.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Christoffer","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"18d62c73-2f35-499d-ac94-134ecd806296","name":"Johansen, Christoffer","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sven Asger","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Sven Asger","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"John J.","key":"mulvihillpau","last":"Mulvihill","name":"Mulvihill, John J.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette F.","key":"wintherpau","last":"Winther","locid":"11ca8ef7-98c5-4eed-9dbe-3b44124f948b","name":"Winther, Jeanette Falck","name_org":"Winther, Jeanette F.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Susanne Oksbjerg","key":"daltonpau","last":"Dalton","locid":"84d10468-fe5d-4cc7-952f-1d89d961390f","name":"Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32424325"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41431-020-0645-5","issn":["10184813","14765438"],"issn_org":["10184813"],"issue":"8","journal":"European Journal of Human Genetics","pages":"1028-1033","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Human Genetics","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085209514"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-11ac222c-7978-4586-854d-be37de238532","ku-8f2a939f-6399-4d3f-99d6-17e7f46d8a0c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Forming and ending marital or cohabiting relationships in a Danish population-based cohort of individuals with neurofibromatosis 1","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-013858","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Calcitonin gene-related peptide (CGRP) has recently been implicated in the pathogenesis of post-traumatic headache (PTH), which raises the prospect for therapeutic use of monoclonal antibodies targeting CGRP or its receptor. Therefore, we decided to assess the efficacy, tolerability, and safety of erenumab for prevention of persistent PTH attributed to mild traumatic brain injury. Methods: A single-center, non-randomized, single-arm, open-label study of erenumab for adults aged 18-65 years with persistent PTH. Patients were assigned to receive 140-mg erenumab monthly by two subcutaneous 1-mL injections, given every 4 weeks for 12 weeks. The primary outcome measure was the mean change in number of monthly headache days of moderate to severe intensity from baseline (4-week pretreatment period) to week 9 through 12. Tolerability and safety endpoints were adverse events (i.e. number and type). Results: Eighty-nine of 100 patients completed the open-label trial. At baseline, the mean monthly number of headache days of moderate to severe intensity was 15.7. By week 9 through 12, the number was reduced by 2.8 days. The most common adverse events were constipation (n = 30) and injection-site reactions (n = 15). Of 100 patients who received at least one dose of erenumab, two patients discontinued the treatment regimen due to adverse events. Conclusions: Among patients with persistent PTH, erenumab resulted in a lower frequency of moderate to severe headache days in this 12-week open-label trial. In addition, erenumab was well-tolerated as discontinuations due to adverse events were low. Placebo-controlled randomized clinical trials are needed to adequately evaluate the efficacy and safety of erenumab in patients with persistent PTH. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.Gov, NCT03974360. Registered on April 17, 2019-Retrospectively registered","author_count":15,"contributors":["Ashina, Håkan","Iljazi, Afrim","Al-Khazali, Haidar Muhsen","Eigenbrodt, Anna Kristina","Larsen, Eigil Lindekilde","Andersen, Amalie Middelboe","Hansen, Kevin John","Braüner, Karoline Bendix","Mørch-Jessen, Thomas","Chaudhry, Basit","Antic, Sonja","Christensen, Casper Emil","Ashina, Messoud","Amin, Faisal Mohammad","Schytz, Henrik Winther"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-026686"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Schytz, Henrik Winther"],"keyword":["Clinical management","Concussion","Head injury","Head trauma","Secondary headache"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficacy tolerability and safety of erenumab for the preventive treatment of persistent post traumatic headache attributed to mild traumatic brain injury an open label study","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s10194-020-01136-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-026686","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7271543","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85086007958","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32493206","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-c0f5d303-d6b2-4e04-ba15-0b6fbbf7441c","ku-2e61e23a-734c-47e5-9102-c065d472ea38"],"keyword":["Clinical management","Concussion","Head injury","Head trauma","Secondary headache"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8A74AB21E208B2590B461C9B46249CA0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250207141/s10194_020_01136_z.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s10194-020-01136-z","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Neurology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Neurology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Håkan","key":"ashinahåkanpau","last":"Ashina","name":"Ashina, Håkan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Afrim","key":"iljaziafrimpau","last":"Iljazi","name":"Iljazi, Afrim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Haidar Muhsen","key":"alkhazalihaidarmuhsenpau","last":"Al-Khazali","name":"Al-Khazali, Haidar Muhsen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna Kristina","key":"eigenbrodtannakristinapau","last":"Eigenbrodt","name":"Eigenbrodt, Anna Kristina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Eigil Lindekilde","key":"larseneigillindekildepau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Eigil Lindekilde","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Amalie Middelboe","key":"andersenamaliemiddelboepau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Amalie Middelboe","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kevin John","key":"hansenkevinjohnpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Kevin John","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Karoline Bendix","key":"braünerkarolinebendixpau","last":"Braüner","name":"Braüner, Karoline Bendix","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"mørchjessenthomaspau","last":"Mørch-Jessen","name":"Mørch-Jessen, Thomas","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Basit","key":"chaudhrybasitpau","last":"Chaudhry","name":"Chaudhry, Basit","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sonja","key":"anticsonjapau","last":"Antic","locid":"c4e6974d-31b5-4f28-a03f-ecc14ff997b8","name":"Antic, Sonja","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Casper Emil","key":"christensencasperemilpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Casper Emil","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Messoud","key":"ashinamessoudpau","last":"Ashina","locid":"0e941844-26c5-4777-a66a-64a163c19cd2","name":"Ashina, Messoud","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Faisal Mohammad","key":"aminfaisalmohammadpau","last":"Amin","locid":"5cea7989-5872-4bc7-bc2d-220a5536f5fb","name":"Amin, Faisal Mohammad","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik Winther","key":"schytzhenrikwintherpau","last":"Schytz","locid":"825ca3a5-a8f5-4f5b-95af-ed64c48207f9","name":"Schytz, Henrik Winther","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32493206"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s10194-020-01136-z","issn":["11292369","11292377"],"issn_org":["11292369"],"journal":"Journal of Headache and Pain","paperid":"62","publisher":"Springer-Verlag Italia s.r.l.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Headache and Pain","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086007958"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c0f5d303-d6b2-4e04-ba15-0b6fbbf7441c","ku-2e61e23a-734c-47e5-9102-c065d472ea38"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Efficacy, tolerability, and safety of erenumab for the preventive treatment of persistent post-traumatic headache attributed to mild traumatic brain injury : An open-label study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-026686","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Leg pain, especially of the knees and hips, is common among senior workers and may limit the ability to perform physically demanding work. In light of the aging workforce, this study determined the joint association of physical work demands and leg pain intensity for work-limiting pain in senior workers. METHODS: Currently employed senior workers (≥50 years) participated in the SeniorWorkingLife study in 2018 (n = 12,879). Associations between the combination of physical work demands and leg pain intensity (interaction) with work-limiting pain (outcome) were modeled using binary logistic regression analyses while controlling for potential covariates. RESULTS: We found a significant interaction (P < 0.001) between physical work demands and leg pain intensity for work-limiting pain. The combination of higher physical work demands and higher leg pain intensity had the worst outcome in terms of the odds of experiencing work-limiting pain. For example, 70% of those with the combination of high physical work demands and leg pain intensity ≥7 (scale 0-10) experienced that the pain limited them to at least some degree in their work. CONCLUSIONS: The combination of high physical work demands and high leg pain intensity are associated with limited ability to perform work among senior workers. These findings highlight the importance of prioritizing the physical work environment in physically demanding occupations, particularly among senior workers, for prolonging working life. Thus, adjusting the work demands, e.g. through use of assistive devices, and lowering the pain, e.g. through physical rehabilitation, may be necessary to sustain work ability to a high age in this group of workers. TRIAL REGISTRATION: This was registered as a cohort study in ClinicalTrials.gov (Identifier: NCT03634410 ) on the 18th of August 2018 (Retrospectively registered).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Skovlund, Sebastian Venge","Bláfoss, Rúni","Sundstrup, Emil","Thomassen, Kristina","Andersen, Lars L."],"cuid":["S03-099.97-766788"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Skovlund, Sebastian Venge"],"keyword":["Ergonomics","Krav i arbejdet","Manual labour","Musculoskeletal Diseases","Muskelskeletbesvær","Occupational medicine","Seniorer","Sustainable employment","Work ability","Workplace"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"joint association of physical work demands and leg pain intensity for work limitations due to pain in senior workers cross sectional study","src":["aau","nfa","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-020-09860-6","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was supported by a grant from the Danish foundation, TrygFonden. The funding body played no role in the design of the study or in the collection, analysis, and interpretation of data and in writing the manuscript."],"id":"S03-099.97-766788","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7672909","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85096192101","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33208134","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-754ce830-3a5f-48f2-896f-e6e599584674","nfa-dabab5b1-f1d1-4486-89ea-1191df10aeee","sdu-31f145e9-bbff-4694-ad60-452ddd1af221"],"keyword":["Ergonomics","Krav i arbejdet","Manual labour","Musculoskeletal diseases","Muskelskeletbesvær","Occupational medicine","Seniorer","Sustainable employment","Work ability","Workplace"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-74B4EC7B6E15EEF207AE77766F311DF3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https:/