org University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Sport Sciences - Performance and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Venge","key":"skovlundpau","last":"Skovlund","locid":"7ed308b6-7f4e-45d9-b04e-9d690a0cbfa2","name":"Skovlund, Sebastian Venge","orcid":"0000-0002-9820-2895","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rúni","key":"bláfosspau","last":"Bláfoss","locid":"a05a86ba-5cbf-4de0-a1da-0a5b02a69ab5","name":"Bláfoss, Rúni","orcid":"0000-0003-1843-6884","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil","key":"sundstruppau","last":"Sundstrup","locid":"688eab9a-3ad9-48b8-aad2-397c0a8ee105","name":"Sundstrup, Emil","orcid":"0000-0001-7408-222X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"thomassenpau","last":"Thomassen","name":"Thomassen, Kristina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars L","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"7698b281-bcfb-47ec-b41e-3ea20ceb5e52","name":"Andersen, Lars L.","name_org":"Andersen, Lars L","orcid":"0000-0003-2777-8085","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33208134"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12889-020-09860-6","issn":["14712458"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Public Health","pages":"1741","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Public Health","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096192101"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-754ce830-3a5f-48f2-896f-e6e599584674","nfa-dabab5b1-f1d1-4486-89ea-1191df10aeee","sdu-31f145e9-bbff-4694-ad60-452ddd1af221"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Joint association of physical work demands and leg pain intensity for work limitations due to pain in senior workers : cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.97-766788","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: In building LCAs, the calculations are carried out over a chosen reference study period (RSP), which is commonly set around 50-60 years. When developing the Danish LCA method for DGNB certification, and later for the preparation of the voluntary sustainability class for the building code, longer RSP's were suggested by technical committees. Therefore, the RSP has been based on a technical approach to the lifetime of buildings, assuming 80 years for offices, 100 years for hospitals and 120 years for residential buildings. In this study, the effects and arguments of a shorter RSP are investigated. Method: LCA-based carbon profiles of 11 building cases were carried out to compare how the RSP influences the results. RSPs of 50, 80, 100 and 120 years were investigated. The building cases represent different use types, structural systems, material choices, on-site electricity generation and installation scope. Results: Results show no notable difference in ranking, the building cases in-between, at RSPs of 50 and 120 years. Further, the relationship between the best and the worst performing building stays around a three-fold difference, regardless of the RSP. Conclusion: The longer RSPs have serious drawbacks regarding the increasing uncertainties associated with the scenarios. Further, annualizing results of longer RSPs entail a fundamental ethical issue of effectively allocating environmental loads to future generations. These specific drawbacks of uncertainty and impacts distribution are reduced by using an RSP of 50 years. The RSP of 50 years thus represents a compromise between ensuring that impacts from replacements of shorter-lived building materials will be reflected in the results, and between encouraging that more emphasis can be put on the crucial material related emissions that affects the global carbon budgets here and now.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Freja Nygaard","Zimmermann, Regitze Kjær","Kanafani, Kai","Andersen, Camilla Marlene Ernst","Birgisdottir, Harpa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-054549"],"event":{"end":"2020-11-04","place":"Gothenburg, se","start":"2020-11-02","title":"World Sustainable Built Environment - Beyond 2020, WSBE 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Birgisdottir, Harpa"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the choice of reference study period in building lca case based analysis and arguments","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1755-1315/588/3/032029","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-054549","identifier":[{"id":"85097128097","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0f67b01d-afb4-4fd2-bc3c-cd6109b2e73d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D84A635B95AF7EDE2ACE72631CF19453"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1755-1315/588/3/032029","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 3.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/402014642/Rasmussen_2020_IOP_Conf._Ser._Earth_Environ._Sci._588_032029.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Energy Efficiency, Indoor Climate and Sustainability of Buildings (EIS)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of the Built Environment, Division of Sustainability of Buildings"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"F. N.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"9d7de26f-e4f7-4e67-9313-22acf8a029b5","name":"Rasmussen, Freja Nygaard","name_org":"Rasmussen, F. N.","orcid":"0000-0002-9168-2021","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"R. K.","key":"zimmermannpau","last":"Zimmermann","locid":"34a89397-359f-47f6-9b91-a94d9eb8d75f","name":"Zimmermann, Regitze Kjær","name_org":"Zimmermann, R. K.","orcid":"0000-0001-5852-3136","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K.","key":"kanafanipau","last":"Kanafani","locid":"dad10dd8-9e72-4d74-b577-73db174faaae","name":"Kanafani, Kai","name_org":"Kanafani, K.","orcid":"0000-0002-8169-1610","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"C.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"a41e0ca0-6ba3-4468-b167-1b757ff74ab2","name":"Andersen, Camilla Marlene Ernst","name_org":"Andersen, C.","orcid":"0000-0001-7750-8329","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"H.","key":"birgisdóttirpau","last":"Birgisdóttir","locid":"4405aab9-4c7a-4134-9d93-04660d33c2b4","name":"Birgisdottir, Harpa","name_org":"Birgisdóttir, H.","orcid":"0000-0001-7642-4107","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Holger","key":"wallbaumpedh","last":"Wallbaum","name":"Wallbaum, Holger","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Alexander","key":"hollbergpedh","last":"Hollberg","name":"Hollberg, Alexander","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Liane","key":"thuvanderpedh","last":"Thuvander","name":"Thuvander, Liane","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Paula","key":"femeniaspedh","last":"Femenias","name":"Femenias, Paula","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Izabela","key":"kurkowskapedh","last":"Kurkowska","name":"Kurkowska, Izabela","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristina","key":"mjörnellpedh","last":"Mjörnell","name":"Mjörnell, Kristina","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Colin","key":"fudgepedh","last":"Fudge","name":"Fudge, Colin","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1755-1315/588/3/032029","issn":["17551307"],"issue":"3 (1.06-1.10)","pages":"1-8","publisher":"IOP Publishing","series":"IOP Conference Series: Earth and Environmental Science","status":"p","subtitle":"World Sustainable Built Environment online conference BEYOND 2020 : 2- 4 November 2020","title":"Conference Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097128097"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0f67b01d-afb4-4fd2-bc3c-cd6109b2e73d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"The choice of reference study period in building LCA - Case-based analysis and arguments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-054549","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The molecular foundation of chronic inflammatory diseases (CIDs) can differ markedly between individuals. As our understanding of the biochemical mechanisms underlying individual disease manifestations and progressions expands, new strategies to adjust treatments to the patient’s characteristics will continue to profoundly transform clinical practice. Nutrition has long been recognized as an important determinant of inflammatory disease phenotypes and treatment response. Yet empirical work demonstrating the therapeutic effectiveness of patient-tailored nutrition remains scarce. This is mainly due to the challenges presented by long-term effects of nutrition, variations in inter-individual gastrointestinal microbiota, the multiplicity of human metabolic pathways potentially affected by food ingredients, nutrition behavior, and the complexity of food composition. Historically, these challenges have been addressed in both human studies and experimental model laboratory studies primarily by using individual nutrition data collection in tandem with large-scale biomolecular data acquisition (e.g. genomics, metabolomics, etc.). This review highlights recent findings in the field of precision nutrition and their potential implications for the development of personalized treatment strategies for CIDs. It emphasizes the importance of computational approaches to integrate nutritional information into multi-omics data analysis and to predict which molecular mechanisms may explain how nutrients intersect with disease pathways. We conclude that recent findings point towards the unexhausted potential of nutrition as part of personalized medicine in chronic inflammation.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Demetrowitsch, Tobias J.","Schlicht, Kristina","Knappe, Carina","Zimmermann, Johannes","Jensen-Kroll, Julia","Pisarevskaja, Alina","Brix, Fynn","Brandes, Juliane","Geisler, Corinna","Marinos, Georgios","Sommer, Felix","Schulte, Dominik M.","Kaleta, Christoph","Andersen, Vibeke","Laudes, Matthias","Schwarz, Karin","Waschina, Silvio"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-624674"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Waschina, Silvio"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Christian-Albrechts-University of Kiel"],"keyword":["Chronic diseases","Dietary intervention","Disease prevention","Inflammation","Microbiota","Nutrition","Personalized medicine","Precision nutrition"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"precision nutrition in chronic inflammation","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fimmu.2020.587895","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The authors acknowledge the support by the Cluster of Excellence 2167 - “Precision medicine in chronic inflammation” - Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft, the Collaborative Research Centre"],"id":"S01-000.00-624674","identifier":[{"id":"33329569","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7719806","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85097398347","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-b3ad7c22-dda7-4ece-a773-6f4d8fc897da"],"keyword":["chronic diseases","dietary intervention","disease prevention","inflammation","microbiota","nutrition","personalized medicine","precision nutrition"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5453511DFBD7CCF6E5243BC08C5F25AB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fimmu.2020.587895","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/179013124/fimmu_11_587895.pdf","version":"Published Version"