{"abstract":"Aims: To explore the experiences and needs of patients on the endovascular therapy pathway. Design: A qualitative design using a phenomenological–hermeneutic approach. Methods: Semi-structured interviews and participant observations were carried out. Data were collected from April 2016–January 2017. Data were analysed using Ricoeur's theory of interpretation, capturing meaning and ensuring comprehensive understanding. The Consolidated Criteria for Reporting Qualitative Research checklist was used as a guideline. Results: The findings of this study show that the impact of stroke goes far beyond physical disability. During the structural analysis, four themes were identified: (1) Acute admission to a stroke unit – an overwhelming and blurred experience. (2) Being helpless and next to yourself. (3) The important care when you worry about dying. (4) Poststroke feelings of loneliness and uncertainty.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Sørensen, Kristina Eiskjær","Dreyer, Pia","Rasmussen, Mads","Simonsen, Claus Ziegler","Andersen, Grethe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-249965"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Kristina Eiskjær"],"keyword":["Acute admission","CARE","Endovascular therapy","Experience","Nursing","Qualitative Research","Ricoeur","Stroke","Support"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experiences and needs of patients on the endovascular therapy pathway after acute ischaemic stroke being helpless and next to yourself","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nop2.391","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-249965","identifier":[{"id":"31871714","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000492041000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC6917975","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85074555825","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-d336b92b-40ca-4eb0-8a91-e76ab5b9049d"],"keyword":["CARE","Ricoeur","acute admission","endovascular therapy","experience","nursing","qualitative research","stroke","support"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A1DD606508E5DF16727F01C06E24F9E2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/nop2.391","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Eiskjær","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Kristina Eiskjær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pia","key":"dreyerpau","last":"Dreyer","locid":"a30cdbd7-b134-4577-b1fc-0d4ebd98e698","name":"Dreyer, Pia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"10307123-564d-4db1-872d-d0a91168ce4e","name":"Rasmussen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0002-0416-6767","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus Z.","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"ccf2fb52-6a4a-45b2-adb0-d6e83324879f","name":"Simonsen, Claus Ziegler","name_org":"Simonsen, Claus Z.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Grethe","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"97e157c9-4cb4-4690-a971-06e4699b50fe","name":"Andersen, Grethe","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-2500","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31871714"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/nop2.391","issn":["20541058"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nursing Open","pages":"299-306","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","status":"p","title":"Nursing Open","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074555825"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d336b92b-40ca-4eb0-8a91-e76ab5b9049d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Experiences and needs of patients on the endovascular therapy pathway after acute ischaemic stroke : Being helpless and next to yourself","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-249965","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Hackathon formats have been praised for their potential for promoting innovative thinking and making in a short time-frame. For this reason, hackathons have also been embraced by many researchers who use hackathons as part of their research in various ways. Through an extensive review of 381 publications published during a 10 year time span, we document the multiple ways in which hackathons are embraced and used by researchers The paper contributes to a better understanding of hackathons as part of research by providing a broad overview as a resource for researchers. We identify three main motivations for using hackathons as part of research: 1) Structuring learning, 2) structuring processes, and 3) enabling participation. For each of the motivations, we identify research with hackathons, and research on hackathons as two main categories. Drawing on several examples from the review we discuss benefits and challenges of using hackathons as part of research.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Falk Olesen, Jeanette","Halskov, Kim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-270712"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Hackathons","Literature review","Research method"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000010 years of research with and on hackathons","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85090499104","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-270712","identifier":[{"id":"85090499104","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f7d5b072-294a-4e12-8ea6-be6596b7dda1"],"keyword":["Hackathons","Literature review","Research method"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-88BDBE43D25EA2539C5E48F97FD514D4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Department of Digital Design and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette","key":"falkolesenpau","last":"Falk Olesen","locid":"8d0554b5-436a-4db6-85e2-eb0ad4cf341f","name":"Falk Olesen, Jeanette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"halskovpau","last":"Halskov","locid":"3043cd86-47ac-46ef-b907-a367b2f0ca5a","name":"Halskov, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-7448-7577","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ron","key":"wakkarypedh","last":"Wakkary","name":"Wakkary, Ron","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristina","key":"andersenpedh","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Kristina","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3357236.3395543","eisbn":["9781450369749"],"isbn":["9781450369749"],"pages":"1073-1088","place":"Eindhoven","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"proceedings of the 2020 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference","title":"DIS 2020 - Proceedings of the 2020 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090499104"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f7d5b072-294a-4e12-8ea6-be6596b7dda1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"10 Years of Research With and On Hackathons","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-270712","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The aim was to investigate embryo-foetal effects of continuous maternal insulin-induced hypoglycaemia extending throughout gestation or until gestation day (GD)17 (typical last day of dosing during pre-clinical evaluation) providing comparator data for safety assessment of longer-acting insulin analogues in non-diabetic rats. Pregnant rats received human insulin (HI)-infusion during gestation until either GD20 or GD17 (HI-GD20; HI-GD17). On GD20, foetal abnormalities and skeletal ossification/mineralisation were evaluated. HI-infusion induced continuous hypoglycaemia. Foetal skeletal and eye malformations (e.g. bent ribs, microphthalmia) were common in both groups. Foetal size and skeletal ossification/mineralisation decreased, particularly with infusion throughout gestation. Concluding, insulin-induced hypoglycaemia during gestation in non-diabetic rats is damaging to embryo-foetal growth and skeletal development, particularly after GD17. Three days without HI-infusion after GD17 allows for some developmental catch-up. Eye development is sensitive to HI-infusion before GD17. These results should serve as a benchmark during pre-clinical safety assessment of longer-acting insulin analogues tested in rats.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jensen, Vivi Flou Hjorth","Mølck, Anne Marie","Lykkesfeldt, Jens","Fels, Johannes Josef","Andersen, Lene","Renaut, Ruth","McGuigan, Fiona","Åkesson, Kristina E.","Bøgh, Ingrid Brück"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-501009"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Division of Toxicology","Lund University"],"keyword":["Human insulin","Hypoglycaemia","Pre clinical","Toxicology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"importance of gestational hypoglycaemia for foetal malformations and skeletal development in rats","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-501009","identifier":[{"id":"85074344927","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31644949","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b41bf3a5-304c-4d85-9c55-4fb9c944bc6b"],"keyword":["Embryo-foetal development","Human insulin","Hypoglycaemia","Pre-clinical","Toxicology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-37DFE806FAB70524C2140E53A6516DAC"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Lifepharm","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Preclinical Disease Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"division of toxicology","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Division of Toxicology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Vivi Flou Hjorth","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"9e985a49-692c-42a5-b57f-b69a5ef4d6c8","name":"Jensen, Vivi Flou Hjorth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne Marie","key":"mølckpau","last":"Mølck","name":"Mølck, Anne Marie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"lykkesfeldtpau","last":"Lykkesfeldt","locid":"6e71ebed-c114-42ab-9ae9-6333f14bf8ad","name":"Lykkesfeldt, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6514-8407","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Johannes Josef","key":"felspau","last":"Fels","name":"Fels, Johannes Josef","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lene","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Lene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ruth","key":"renautpau","last":"Renaut","name":"Renaut, Ruth","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Fiona","key":"mcguiganpau","last":"McGuigan","name":"McGuigan, Fiona","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Kristina E.","key":"åkessonpau","last":"Åkesson","name":"Åkesson, Kristina E.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ingrid Brück","key":"bøghpau","last":"Bøgh","name":"Bøgh, Ingrid Brück","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31644949"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.reprotox.2019.10.003","issn":["08906238","18731708"],"issn_org":["08906238"],"journal":"Reproductive Toxicology","pages":"14-26","status":"p","title":"Reproductive Toxicology","volume":"91"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074344927"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b41bf3a5-304c-4d85-9c55-4fb9c944bc6b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Importance of gestational hypoglycaemia for foetal malformations and skeletal development in rats","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-501009","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Den grønne omstilling af produktionsprocesser er essentiel, hvis det skal lykkes at realisere FNs dagsorden og omsætte Verdensmålene for bæredygtig udvikling (SDG17) til handling inden 2030. Robotteknologi har potentiale til at spille en afgørende rolle i denne proces. Robotteknologi bidrager allerede i vidt omfang til den grønne omstilling af erhvervslivet med energibesparende løsninger og reduceret transportbehov mellem produktionssteder og markeder. Den danske robotindustri er i en global førerposition og vækster målt på både omsætning, antal arbejdspladser og eksport. Derfor har danske robotvirksomheder et godt udgangspunkt for at udnytte robotteknologi til at realisere de kommercielle muligheder, der er forbundet med den grønne omstilling.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","Wanscher, Christina E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-593045"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bæredygtighed","Grøn omstilling","Robot","Robotteknologi"],"level":"pop","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Odense Robotics"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robotteknologi og grøn omstilling hvordan bidrager robotteknologi til den grønne omstilling","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.odenserobotics.dk/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/Rapport-2020_Robotteknologi-og-gron-omstilling.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-593045","ids":["sdu-45381305-4956-495c-a312-bd4851995dcd"],"keyword":["FNs verdensmål for bæredygtig omstilling","bæredygtighed","grøn omstilling","robot","robotteknologi"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CBEABB7247B2FE90B8592E0EB82CED1B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.odenserobotics.dk/wp-content/uploads/2020/12/Rapport-2020_Robotteknologi-og-gron-omstilling.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM), Centre for Integrative Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Odense Robotics"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"46d2bbb6-cde6-45b4-b04d-dcbcbad97c83","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina E.","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Christina E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"51","publisher":"Odense Robotics","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","sdg":["17. Partnerships for the Goals","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-45381305-4956-495c-a312-bd4851995dcd"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Robotteknologi og grøn omstilling : Hvordan bidrager robotteknologi til den grønne omstilling","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-593045","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Aims We examined the extent to which associations between education and cardiovascular disease (CVD) morbidity and mortality are attributable to income and work stress. Methods and results We included all employed Danish residents aged 30–59 years in 2000. Cardiovascular disease morbidity analyses included 1 638 270 individuals, free of cardiometabolic disease (CVD or diabetes). Mortality analyses included 41 944 individuals with cardiometabolic disease. We assessed education and income annually from population registers and work stress, defined as job strain, with a job-exposure matrix. Outcomes were ascertained until 2014 from health registers and risk was estimated using Cox regression. During 10 957 399 (men) and 10 776 516 person-years (women), we identified 51 585 and 24 075 incident CVD cases, respectively. For men with low education, risk of CVD was 1.62 [95% confidence interval (CI) 1.58–1.66] before and 1.46 (95% CI 1.42–1.50) after adjustment for income and job strain (25% reduction). In women, estimates were 1.66 (95% CI 1.61–1.72) and 1.53 (95% CI 1.47–1.58) (21% reduction). Of individuals with cardiometabolic disease, 1736 men (362 234 person-years) and 341 women (179 402 person-years) died from CVD. Education predicted CVD mortality in both sexes. Estimates were reduced with 54% (men) and 33% (women) after adjustment for income and job strain. Conclusion Low education predicted incident CVD in initially healthy individuals and CVD mortality in individuals with prevalent cardiometabolic disease. In men with cardiometabolic disease, income and job strain explained half of the higher CVD mortality in the low education group. In healthy men and in women regardless of cardiometabolic disease, these factors explained 21–33% of the higher CVD morbidity and mortality.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Framke, Elisabeth","Sørensen, Jeppe Karl","Andersen, Per Kragh","Svane-Petersen, Annemette Coop","Alexanderson, Kristina","Bonde, Jens Peter","Farrants, Kristin","Flachs, Esben Meulengracht","Hanson, Linda L. Magnusson","Nyberg, Solja T.","Villadsen, Ebbe","Kivimaki, Mika","Rugulies, Reiner","Madsen, Ida E. H."],"cuid":["S02-098.03-769166"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Clinicum, Faculty of Medicine, and Helsinki Institute of Life Science, University of Helsinki, Helsinki, Finland.","Department of Epidemiology and Public Health, University College London, London, UK.","Karolinska Institutet","Stress Research Institute, Stockholm University, Stockholm, Sweden."],"keyword":["Cardiovascular disease","Cardiovascular mortality","Mechanisms","Nationwide study","Social determinants","Universal coverage"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Department of Public Health, University of Helsinki, Helsinki, Finland."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"contribution of income and job strain to the association between education and cardiovascular disease in 000000000001 000000000006 million danish employees","src":["ku","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/eurheartj/ehz870","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.03-769166","identifier":[{"id":"85081944585","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31844881","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7071845","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000522660900006","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-b80ce7ec-4ddc-49f2-8e25-ef6a5f351b20","nfa-435cba14-6af8-4ea3-be34-72ba4f6fc136"],"keyword":["Cardiovascular disease","Cardiovascular mortalit