{"abstract":"En svensk undersøgelse viser, at intensiveret politikontrol nedsætter den gennemsnitlige kørehastighed og bidrager til færre hastighedsovertrædelser.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Krogh Andersen, Sandra Kristina","Møller, Mette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-360878"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"øget hastighedskontrol sænker antallet af hastighedsovertrædelser","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/185947432/_get_hastighedskontrol_s_nker_antallet_af_hastighedsovertr_delser.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-360878","ids":["dtu-bc6d1536-fe71-4b46-81a9-094a8a5cd95b"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-49053AB9797AAE9EDDB44F49FD7CA832"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.trafiksikkerhedsforskning.dtu.dk/arkiv/nr-45/svensk-undersoegelse","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/185947432/_get_hastighedskontrol_s_nker_antallet_af_hastighedsovertr_delser.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transport","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transport, Transport Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra Kristina","key":"kroghandersenpau","last":"Krogh Andersen","locid":"b35dc181-b805-4bfd-8753-398a7f4021f4","name":"Krogh Andersen, Sandra Kristina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"bc2c2ce5-846a-48d8-8f1c-98639e8c7604","name":"Møller, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-0012-8691","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"Nyhedsbrevet Trafiksikkerhedsforskning","publisher":"DTU Transport","status":"p","title":"Nyhedsbrevet Trafiksikkerhedsforskning","title_org":"Nyhedsbrevet trafiksikkerhedsforskning","volume":"45"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bc6d1536-fe71-4b46-81a9-094a8a5cd95b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Øget hastighedskontrol sænker antallet af hastighedsovertrædelser","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-360878","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Diabetes is a diverse and complex disease, with considerable variation in phenotypic manifestation and severity. This variation hampers the study of etiological differences and reduces the statistical power of analyses of associations to genetics, treatment outcomes, and complications. We address these issues through deep, fine-grained phenotypic stratification of a diabetes cohort. Text mining the electronic health records of 14,017 patients, we matched two controlled vocabularies (ICD-10 and a custom vocabulary developed at the clinical center Steno Diabetes Center Copenhagen) to clinical narratives spanning a 19 year period. The two matched vocabularies comprise over 20,000 medical terms describing symptoms, other diagnoses, and lifestyle factors. The cohort is genetically homogeneous (Caucasian diabetes patients from Denmark) so the resulting stratification is not driven by ethnic differences, but rather by inherently dissimilar progression patterns and lifestyle related risk factors. Using unsupervised Markov clustering, we defined 71 clusters of at least 50 individuals within the diabetes spectrum. The clusters display both distinct and shared longitudinal glycemic dysregulation patterns, temporal co-occurrences of comorbidities, and associations to single nucleotide polymorphisms in or near genes relevant for diabetes comorbidities.","author_count":27,"contributors":["Kirk, I.K.","Simon, C.","Banasik, K.","Holm, P.C.","Haue, A.D.","Jensen, P.B.","Jensen, L. Juhl","Rodríguez, C.L.","Pedersen, M.K.","Eriksson, R.","Andersen, H.U.","Almdal, T.","Bork-Jensen, J.","Grarup, N.","Borch-Johnsen, K.","Pedersen, O.","Pociot, F.","Hansen, T.","Bergholdt, R.","Rossing, P.","Brunak, Søren"],"cuid":["S03-099.04-035208"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Rossing, P.","Rossing, Peter"],"keyword":["Comorbidities","Computational Biology","Diabetes","EHR","Epidemiology","Genotyping","Global Health","Human","Systems biology","Text mining"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"linking glycemic dysregulation in diabetes to symptoms comorbidities and genetics through ehr data mining","src":["dtu","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.44941","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.04-035208","identifier":[{"id":"000502273800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"31818369","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85076272755","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6904221","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-725c39fd-8854-4059-8fe2-e570e3ea5b6f","ku-e5e30b13-d13b-4f65-879f-2292326e88e0","sdu-a3ef77ef-45f6-452a-a3cc-3d2893902db0"],"keyword":["EHR","comorbidities","computational biology","diabetes","diabetes subtypes","epidemiology","genotyping","global health","human","systems biology","text mining"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-0BED896EFBE24D3EC499FCBDB7B6C1CD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/158786519/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.44941","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/248893172/elife_44941_v1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backe