{"abstract":"En svensk undersøgelse viser, at erhvervschauffører oplever, at de er mindre søvnige sammenlignet med ikke-professionelle chauffører i situationer, hvor objektive målinger i form af blinkefrekvens, kørehastighed mv. indikerer, at de er mere søvnige.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Krogh Andersen, Sandra Kristina","Møller, Mette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352059"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"har erhvervschauffører højere tolerance over for søvnmangel","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.trafiksikkerhedsforskning.dtu.dk/arkiv/nr-46/anund-et-al","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352059","ids":["dtu-9f305466-463f-446f-a9e5-f75009bcdd40"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AB05CC35A9746FFAF9C2A70975A434CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.trafiksikkerhedsforskning.dtu.dk/arkiv/nr-46/anund-et-al","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/195527446/4_Har_erhvervschauff_rer_h_jere_tolerance_over_for_s_vnmangel.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transport","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transport, Transport Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra Kristina","key":"kroghandersenpau","last":"Krogh Andersen","locid":"b35dc181-b805-4bfd-8753-398a7f4021f4","name":"Krogh Andersen, Sandra Kristina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"bc2c2ce5-846a-48d8-8f1c-98639e8c7604","name":"Møller, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-0012-8691","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"Nyhedsbrevet Trafiksikkerhedsforskning","publisher":"DTU Transport","status":"p","title":"Nyhedsbrevet Trafiksikkerhedsforskning","title_org":"Nyhedsbrevet trafiksikkerhedsforskning","volume":"46"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9f305466-463f-446f-a9e5-f75009bcdd40"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Har erhvervschauffører højere tolerance over for søvnmangel?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352059","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The identification of genetic variants implicated in human developmental disorders has been revolutionized by second-generation sequencing combined with international pooling of cases. Here, we describe seven individuals who have diverse yet overlapping developmental anomalies, and who all have de novo missense FBXW11 variants identified by whole exome or whole genome sequencing and not reported in the gnomAD database. Their phenotypes include striking neurodevelopmental, digital, jaw, and eye anomalies, and in one individual, features resembling Noonan syndrome, a condition caused by dysregulated RAS signaling. FBXW11 encodes an F-box protein, part of the Skp1-cullin-F-box (SCF) ubiquitin ligase complex, involved in ubiquitination and proteasomal degradation and thus fundamental to many protein regulatory processes. FBXW11 targets include β-catenin and GLI transcription factors, key mediators of Wnt and Hh signaling, respectively, critical to digital, neurological, and eye development. Structural analyses indicate affected residues cluster at the surface of the loops of the substrate-binding domain of FBXW11, and the variants are predicted to destabilize the protein and/or its interactions. In situ hybridization studies on human and zebrafish embryonic tissues demonstrate FBXW11 is expressed in the developing eye, brain, mandibular processes, and limb buds or pectoral fins. Knockdown of the zebrafish FBXW11 orthologs fbxw11a and fbxw11b resulted in embryos with smaller, misshapen, and underdeveloped eyes and abnormal jaw and pectoral fin development. Our findings support the role of FBXW11 in multiple developmental processes, including those involving the brain, eye, digits, and jaw.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Holt, Richard J.","Young, Rodrigo M.","Crespo, Berta","Ceroni, Fabiola","Curry, Cynthia J.","Bellacchio, Emanuele","Bax, Dorine A.","Ciolfi, Andrea","Simon, Marleen","Fagerberg, Christina","van Binsbergen, Ellen","De Luca, Alessandro","Memo, Luigi","Dobyns, William B.","Mohammed, Alaa Afif","Clokie, Samuel J.H.","Zazo Seco, Celia","Jiang, Yong Hui","Sørensen, Kristina Pilekær","Andersen, Helle","Sullivan, Jennifer","Powis, Zöe","Chassevent, Anna","Smith-Hicks, Constance","Petrovski, Slavé","Antoniadi, Thalia","Shashi, Vandana","Gelb, Bruce D.","Wilson, Stephen W.","Gerrelli, Dianne","Tartaglia, Marco","Chassaing, Nicolas","Calvas, Patrick","Ragge, Nicola K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-584351"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Ragge, Nicola K."],"country":["Australia","Egypt","France","Italy","Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ambry Genetics Corporation","AstraZeneca","Bambino Gesù Children’s Hospital","Cairo University","Duke University Medical Center","INP-EI PURPAN","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","Institute for Global Health","Institute of Psychiatry Psychology and Neuroscience","Kennedy Krieger Institute","Molecular Genetics Unit","Oxford Edu Centre Ltd. (Ph.D. Oxford Brookes University)","Seattle Children's Research Institute","Service de Génétique Médicale","UCL Great Ormond Street Institute of Child Health","Unità Operativa Complessa di Pediatria e Patologia Neonatale","University College London","University Medical Center Utrecht","University of California","University of Melbourne","University of Washington"],"keyword":["Brain","Development","Eye","Neurodevelopment","Noonan syndrome","WNT"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"de novo missense variants in fbxw000000000011 cause diverse developmental phenotypes including brain eye and digit anomalies","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["