{"abstract":"Tuberculosis (TB) remains a public health emergency worldwide. WHO recommends low-incidence countries to increase awareness of latent tuberculosis infection (LTBI) as part of a national preventive strategy. This review focuses on the burden of TB in Denmark, which might be reduced, if more focus was paid on diagnosing LTBI in relevant patients, and treatment to prevent future active TB cases was initiated. LTBI testing should be considered in persons at risk of TB disease, who will benefit from LTBI treatment, e.g. recently infected persons or persons having undergone organ transplantation or having comorbidity such as HIV, dialyses, and immunosuppression.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nordholm, Anne Christine","Ravn, Pernille","Kristensen, Kristina Langholz","Nygaard, Ulrikka","Jensen, Sidse Graff","Wejse, Christian","Andersen, Åse Bengård","Lillebaek, Troels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809258"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"testing for latent tuberculosis infection needs to be improved in denmark","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85075927547&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-809258","identifier":[{"id":"31791459","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85075927547","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-201a39d7-0086-4e93-a89d-ebb37bff6d01"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6A7FEC592A65C2397B7C899C0FD7449B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: infection medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Anne Christine","key":"nordholmpau","last":"Nordholm","name":"Nordholm, Anne Christine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pernille","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"3f19690c-0d72-4d09-a542-a309efd6fb0a","name":"Ravn, Pernille","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristina Langholz","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Kristina Langholz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ulrikka","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"43b2e239-ddc1-4676-a8db-0a0f23906813","name":"Nygaard, Ulrikka","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sidse Graff","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"2ec64e63-f712-4d2b-b84b-96fbd89704fa","name":"Jensen, Sidse Graff","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"wejsepau","last":"Wejse","name":"Wejse, Christian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Åse Bengård","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"9743bacd-2b00-49d3-b6b4-5babe5045e25","name":"Andersen, Åse Bengård","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Troels","key":"lillebækpau","last":"Lillebæk","locid":"4c4e219b-6ac0-4067-a078-ef52b9c2beff","name":"Lillebaek, Troels","name_org":"Lillebæk, Troels","orcid":"0000-0002-2601-2718","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31791459"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"48","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"181"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-201a39d7-0086-4e93-a89d-ebb37bff6d01"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Testing for latent tuberculosis infection needs to be improved in Denmark","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809258","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Cardiomyocytes (CMs) derived from human embryonic stem cells (hESCs) or induced pluripotent stem cells (iPSCs) are used to study cardiogenesis and mechanisms of heart disease, and are being used in methods for toxiological screening of drugs. The phenotype of stem-cell-derived CMs should ideally resemble native CMs. Here, we compare embryonic/fetal CMs with hESC-derived CMs according to function and morphology. CM clusters were obtained from human embryonic/fetal hearts from elective terminated pregnancies before gestational week 12, and separated into atrial and ventricular tissues. Specific markers for embryonic CMs and primary cilia were visualized using immunofluorescence microscopy analysis. Contracting human embryonic cardiomyocyte (hECM) clusters morphologically and phenotypically resemble CMs in the embryonic/fetal heart. In addition, the contracting hECM clusters expressed primary cilia similar to that of cells in the embryonic/fetal heart. The electrophysiological characteristics of atrial and ventricular CMs were established by recording action potentials (APs) using sharp electrodes. In contrast to ventricular APs, atrial APs displayed a marked early repolarization followed by a plateau phase. hESC-CMs displayed a continuum of AP shapes. In all embryonic/fetal clusters, both atrial and ventricular, AP duration was prolonged by exposure to the K V 11.1 channel inhibitor dofetilide (50 nM); however, the prolongation was not significant, possibly due to the relatively small number of experiments. This study provides novel information on APs and functional characteristics of atrial and ventricular CMs in first trimester hearts, and demonstrates that K v 11.1 channels play a functional role already at these early stages. These results provide information needed to validate methods being developed on the basis of in vitro-derived CMs from either hESC or iPSC, and although there was a good correlation between the morphology of the two types of CMs, differences in electrophysiological characteristics exist.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Grubb, Søren","Vestergaard, Maj Linea","Andersen, Astrid Sten","Rasmussen, Karen Koefoed","Mamsen, Linn Salto","Tuckute, Greta","Grunnet-Lauridsen, Kristina","Møllgård, Kjeld","Ernst, Erik","Christensen, Søren Tvorup","Calloe, Kirstine","Andersen, Claus Yding"],"cuid":["S02-099.02-024421"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Claus Yding"],"keyword":["Action potential","Cardiomyogenesis","Heart development","Primary cilia","hESC","iPSC"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of cultured human cardiomyocyte clusters obtained from embryos fetuses or derived from human embryonic stem cells","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85065098992","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.02-024421","identifier":[{"id":"85065098992","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30755084","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-a091bec8-a401-40f8-95a3-48ac74c34845","ku-bf7a4619-edd8-43c6-b194-436b659a46ea"],"keyword":["action potential","cardiomyogenesis","hECM","hESC","heart development","iPSC","primary cilia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2CA4F4577404D36BB5753735263A4062"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Pathobiological Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Søren J","key":"grubbsørenpau","last":"Grubb","locid":"c6f60e1b-8fbc-4ef5-b31d-c9bc4bfa1072","name":"Grubb, Søren","name_org":"Grubb, Søren J","orcid":"0000-0002-6710-9655","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Maj Linea","key":"vestergaardmajlineapau","last":"Vestergaard","name":"Vestergaard, Maj Linea","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Astrid Sten","key":"andersenastridstenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Astrid Sten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karen Koefod","key":"rasmussenkarenkoefoedpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"53d6c30a-2cdf-4ef5-ac6f-63e05b3