:"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hannah","key":"zuckermanhannahpau","last":"Zuckerman","name":"Zuckerman, Hannah","rank":1577,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ran","key":"lyuranpau","last":"Lyu","name":"Lyu, Ran","rank":1578,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Wayne","key":"pullanwaynepau","last":"Pullan","name":"Pullan, Wayne","rank":1579,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33326193"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/database/baz085","issn":["17580463"],"journal":"Database: The Journal of Biological Databases and Curation","pages":"1-67","paperid":"085","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Database: The Journal of Biological Databases and Curation","title_org":"Database","volume":"2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85082592913"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-88b053a3-63ab-4380-ab20-90a54b540224","au-6bf5b1c8-6cc1-4ee4-b711-48f478a90279","ku-291608f7-132f-41ac-94ae-fe9aa192baf0","sdu-a9479d7b-e13c-4f9b-8edd-dd71403513e8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Large expert-curated database for benchmarking document similarity detection in biomedical literature search","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-087.05-006608","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Aims: To examine the effect of progressive resistance training (PRT) on health related quality of life and a predefined symptom cluster of pain-sleep-fatigue. Methods: This study was a planned secondary analysis of a randomized controlled trial examining the effect of PRT on prevention of arm lymphedema in a population of women between 18 and 75 years undergoing breast cancer surgery with axillary lymph node dissection. Participants were allocated by computer randomization to usual care control or a PRT intervention in a 1:1 ratio. The intervention, initiated in the third post-operative week, consisted of three times PRT per week, supervised in groups in the first 20 weeks, and self-administered in the following 30 weeks. Questionnaire assessments were made at baseline, 20 weeks and 12 months, with the European Organization for Research and Treatment in Cancer Core questionnaire (EORTC QLQ C30) and the Functional Assessment of Chronic Illness Therapy-(FACIT) fatigue questionnaire. The symptom cluster of pain-sleep-fatigue was measured with a constructed score adding EORTC C30 subscales of insomnia, pain, and fatigue. Data were treated as repeated measurements and analyzed with mixed models. Results: Among 158 recruited participants, we found a clinically relevant increased emotional functioning with nine points at both follow-ups (p = .02), and 16 and 11 points at 20 weeks and 12 months respectively (p = .04) in social functioning. Furthermore, in the subgroup of women with the symptom cluster pain-sleep-fatigue present at baseline, a significant effect was found for global health status (p = .01) and social functioning (p = .02). Conclusion: To our knowledge, this is the first study to report clinically relevant effects of PRT on social and emotional functioning in the first postoperative year after breast cancer surgery. Furthermore, a subgroup of women with the pain-sleep-fatigue symptom cluster had particular benefit from PRT on global health status and social functioning.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Ammitzbøll, Gunn","Kristina Kjær, Trille","Johansen, Christoffer","Lanng, Charlotte","Wreford Andersen, Elisabeth","Kroman, Niels","Zerahn, Bo","Hyldegaard, Ole","Envold Bidstrup, Pernille","Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-417733"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Breast Neoplasms surgery","Fatigue etiology","Female","Humans","Mastectomy adverse effects","Middle Aged","Postoperative Complications etiology","Quality of Life","Resistance Training","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of progressive resistance training on health related quality of life in the first year after breast cancer surgery results from a randomized controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-417733","identifier":[{"id":"85060860888","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30702006","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-28a68268-c241-4deb-8e92-d38e0bb0c04d"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Breast Neoplasms/surgery","Fatigue/etiology","Female","Humans","Lymphedema/prevention & control","Mastectomy/adverse effects","Middle Aged","Postoperative Complications/etiology","Quality of Life","Resistance Training","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-40B700327007E4C760E167AACF25DC9B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Gunn","key":"ammitzbøllpau","last":"Ammitzbøll","name":"Ammitzbøll, Gunn","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Trille","key":"kristinakjærpau","last":"Kristina Kjær","name":"Kristina Kjær, Trille","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christoffer","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"18d62c73-2f35-499d-ac94-134ecd806296","name":"Johansen, Christoffer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte","key":"lanngpau","last":"Lanng","locid":"b04fdfe6-0f49-4d2e-9ece-1a2a1ee00ab7","name":"Lanng, Charlotte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Elisabeth","key":"wrefordandersenpau","last":"Wreford Andersen","name":"Wreford Andersen, Elisabeth","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Niels","key":"kromanpau","last":"Kroman","locid":"e120d8b8-6f8e-4b09-a51f-4eca94999f55","name":"Kroman, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-6631-2993","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bo","key":"zerahnpau","last":"Zerahn","name":"Zerahn, Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ole","key":"hyldegaardpau","last":"Hyldegaard","locid":"b3f6c355-9c6b-4db3-84c2-870d09643475","name":"Hyldegaard, Ole","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pernille","key":"envoldbidstruppau","last":"Envold Bidstrup","name":"Envold Bidstrup, Pernille","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Susanne","key":"oksbjergdaltonpau","last":"Oksbjerg Dalton","locid":"84d10468-fe5d-4cc7-952f-1d89d961390f","name":"Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","name_org":"Oksbjerg Dalton, Susanne","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30702006"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2018.1563718","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"665-672","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060860888"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-28a68268-c241-4deb-8e92-d38e0bb0c04d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of progressive resistance training on health-related quality of life in the first year after breast cancer surgery - results from a randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-417733","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Tuberculosis (TB) remains a public health emergency worldwide. WHO recommends low-incidence countries to increase awareness of latent tuberculosis infection (LTBI) as part of a national preventive strategy. This review focuses on the burden of TB in Denmark, which might be reduced, if more focus was paid on diagnosing LTBI in relevant patients, and treatment to prevent future active TB cases was initiated. LTBI testing should be considered in persons at risk of TB disease, who will benefit from LTBI treatment, e.g. recently infected persons or persons having undergone organ transplantation or having comorbidity such as HIV, dialyses, and immunosuppression.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nordholm, Anne Christine","Ravn, Pernille","Kristensen, Kristina Langholz","Nygaard, Ulrikka","Jensen, Sidse Graff","Wejse, Christian","Andersen, Åse Bengård","Lillebæk, Troels"],"cuid":["S03-088.73-014562"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Nordholm, Anne Christine"],"keyword":["Denmark","HIV Infections","Humans","Latent Tuberculosis diagnosis","Tuberculin Test","Tuberculosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vi skal blive bedre til at teste for latent tuberkulose i danmark","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://ugeskriftet.dk/videnskab/vi-skal-blive-bedre-til-teste-latent-tuberkulose-i-danmark","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-088.73-014562","identifier":[{"id":"85075927547","type":"scopus"},{"id":"85126971997","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31791459","type