k","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fiona M.","key":"gribblefionampau","last":"Gribble","name":"Gribble, Fiona M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Reidar","key":"albrechtsenreidarpau","last":"Albrechtsen","locid":"64d14495-256d-4a74-ba12-f4c9a525d5af","name":"Albrechtsen, Reidar","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bolette","key":"hartmannbolettepau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"eb04fc6b-068a-4d5b-a106-1b7be3f7e12b","name":"Hartmann, Bolette","orcid":"0000-0001-8509-2036","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mette","key":"rosenkildemettempau","last":"Rosenkilde","locid":"d902feb8-1594-4fa8-bcb1-9f646dc30dd3","name":"Rosenkilde, Mette M.","name_org":"Rosenkilde, Mette","orcid":"0000-0001-9600-3254","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Juul","key":"holstjensjuulpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29656109"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.molmet.2018.03.007","issn":["22128778"],"journal":"Molecular Metabolism","pages":"84-95","status":"p","title":"Molecular Metabolism","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85045244666"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c3776646-bf4e-4caa-b8e2-487a952caba4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bile acids are important direct and indirect regulators of the secretion of appetite- and metabolism-regulating hormones from the gut and pancreas.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-510128","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Current prognostic markers allocate the majority of lymph node (LN) negative and estrogen receptor (ER) positive breast cancer patients into the high-risk group. Accordingly, most patients receive systemic treatments although approximately 40% of these patients may have been cured by surgery and radiotherapy alone. Two studies identified seven prognostic microRNAs in systemically untreated, LN negative and ER positive breast cancer patients which may allow more precise patient classification. However, six of the seven microRNAs were analyzed in both studies but only found to be prognostic in one study. To validate their prognostic potential, we analyzed microRNA expression in an independent cohort (n = 110) using a pairmatched study design minimizing dependence of classical markers. The expression of hsa-miR-548c-5p was significantly associated with abridged disease-free survival (hazard ratio [HR]:1.96, p = 0.027). Contradicting published results, high hsa-miR516-3p expression was associated with favorable outcome (HR:0.29, p = 0.0068). The association is probably time-dependent indicating later relapse. Additionally, re-analysis of previously published expression data of two matching cohorts (n = 100, n = 255) supports an association of hsa-miR-128-3p with shortened diseasefree survival (HR:2.48, p = 0.0033) and an upregulation of miR-7-5p (p = 0.0038; p = 0.039) and miR-210-3p (p = 0.031) in primary tumors of patients who experienced metastases. Further analysis may verify the prognostic potential of these microRNAs.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Block, Ines","Burton, Mark","Sørensen, Kristina Pilekær","Andersen, Lars","Larsen, Martin Jakob","Bak, Martin","Cold, Søren","Thomassen, Mads","Tan, Qihua","Kruse, Torben A"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-636824"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Estrogen receptor positive","Low risk breast cancer","Lymph node negative","Prognosis","microRNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association of mir 000000000548c 000000000005p mir 000000000007 000000000005p mir 000000000210 000000000003p mir 000000000128 000000000003p with recurrence in systemically untreated breast cancer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18632/oncotarget.24088","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-636824","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5823652","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85041387247","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29507672","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-de1cc175-3b6f-4c65-b714-29e2f7580e9e"],"keyword":["Estrogen receptor positive","Low-risk breast cancer","Lymph node negative","MicroRNA","Prognosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B89981B8B3B165FD24F661EB3CD7D62E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/137570762/Association_of_miR_548c_5p_miR_7_5p_miR_210_3p_miR_128_3p_with_recurrence_in_systemically_untreated_breast_cancer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18632/oncotarget.24088","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Genetics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ines","key":"blockpau","last":"Block","locid":"f03d6e9f-91a1-4177-a2f3-4ef9e036b2ca","name":"Block, Ines","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"burtonpau","last":"Burton","locid":"1279f5b8-9ebb-423f-8bc7-a9956bbbcc0a","name":"Burton, Mark","orcid":"0000-0002-3782-5933","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Pilekær","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"648df5d2-8bcb-45ad-a3e8-d4fe5730537b","name":"Sørensen, Kristina Pilekær","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"eed16b38-5605-4ed2-85c8-8a01ce795d57","name":"Andersen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-6148-1341","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Jakob","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7cfc93bc-88f4-48fa-86de-6b0147dc2825","name":"Larsen, Martin Jakob","orcid":"0000-0003-4107-8771","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","locid":"29014efb-3f03-419f-af10-c72cdf94a9a4","name":"Bak, Martin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"coldpau","last":"Cold","locid":"078d86c7-0a89-4959-9b4b-86312179bcc1","name":"Cold, Søren","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"thomassenpau","last":"Thomassen","locid":"428f2151-f2aa-4a5e-bdee-4184c0586467","name":"Thomassen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0003-0078-1217","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Qihua","key":"tanpau","last":"Tan","locid":"8fcbdce6-6fd7-4033-8a08-80ebfb8f63da","name":"Tan, Qihua","orcid":"0000-0003-3194-0030","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben A","key":"krusepau","last":"Kruse","locid":"7fe49118-5068-4af6-83f9-fadeb1abe87a","name":"Kruse, Torben A","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29507672"],"pub":{"doi":"10.18632/oncotarget.24088","issn":["19492553"],"issue":"10","journal":"OncoTarget","pages":"9030-9042","publisher":"Impact Journals LLC","status":"p","title":"OncoTarget","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041387247"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-de1cc175-3b6f-4c65-b714-29e2f7580e9e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Association of miR-548c-5p, miR-7-5p, miR-210-3p, miR-128-3p with recurrence in systemically untreated breast cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-636824","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This is a review of the recommendations regarding pregnancy after bariatric surgery from the Danish Society of Obstetrics and Gynaecology. The risk of vitamin/mineral deficiencies should be emphasized and checked with blood samples. Measurements of fetal growth should be offered at gestational age 28 and 34 as a supplement to the standard prenatal procedures because of the increased risk of intrauterine growth retardation. Because of persistent obesity there is still an increased risk of hypertension and diabetes mellitus. In case of abdominal pain internal herniation should be suspected.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kjær, Mette Mandrup","Torvin-Andersen, Lise Lotte","Damm, Peter","Jensen, Dorte Møller","Lauenborg, Jeannet","Stentebjerg, Louise Laage","Støving, René Klinkeby","Renault, Kristina Martha"],"cuid":["S02-088.10-047089"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Bariatric Surgery adverse effects","Denmark","Dietary Supplements","Female","Humans","Obesity Morbid complications","Practice Guidelines as Topic","Preconception Care","Pregnancy","Pregnancy Complications etiology","Recommended Dietary Allowances","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"graviditet efter bariatrisk kirurgi","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?eid=2-s2.0-85060167430&partnerID=MN8TOARS","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-088.10-047089","identifier":[{"id":"29212591","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85048731175","type":"scopus"},{"id":"85060167430","type":"scopus"}]