{"abstract":"This paper explores labor market mechanisms of intra-professional status change following fast organizational failure. We undertake a case study of a collapsed high-profile bunker oil company, selected on account of its failure’s scale, speed, and organizational and geographical heterogeneity. Using unique hand-collected qualitative and quantitative data, we examine the careers of the organization’s displaced employees. At odds with extant theory on stigma, we do not find any general status loss. We explain this by the fast decline and aftermath after bankruptcy of this particular organization, allowing insufficient time for a stigmatization mechanism. We find that displaced employees most prone to status loss are those having worked organizationally and geographically proximately to the locus of the organization’s failure. We suggest that in lieu of stigma, status change is driven by a mechanism of blame, i.e. perceived culpability of those displaced employees with comparatively strong association to organizational failure. Comparing this new theoretical notion with the extant notion of stigma, we suggest that while both are mechanisms compensating for imperfect information, stigma entails weaker association to failure and hence \"taints with a broader brush\" compared to blame’s \"pointed brush\".","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nowinska, Agnieszka","Vaarst Andersen, Kristina","Lorenzen, Mark"],"cuid":["S03-087.80-698091"],"event":{"end":"2018-06-13","place":"Frederiksberg, dk","start":"2018-06-11","title":"Strategic Management Society","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the broad vs the pointed brush status change stigma and blame following fast organizational failure","src":["cbs","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://conference.druid.dk/acc_papers/96k63cl87twge9t807y6btfetuw3ub.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-087.80-698091","ids":["cbs-76504a21-d168-44e4-a87e-d11443f5e896","sdu-5f0058cf-575f-4e93-9321-18a8bf441404","sdu-cef876a9-a497-47bf-9af4-f1736327e3ed"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-3-0F7AC57AB179663841FC41C41D6B303A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://conference.druid.dk/acc_papers/96k63cl87twge9t807y6btfetuw3ub.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategic Management and Globalization","Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM), Centre for Integrative Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Agnieszka","key":"nowinskapau","last":"Nowinska","locid":"f4b34d91-51f7-4f16-b712-94402ecda4bf","name":"Nowinska, Agnieszka","orcid":"0000-0003-1914-5544","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"46d2bbb6-cde6-45b4-b04d-dcbcbad97c83","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mark","key":"lorenzenpau","last":"Lorenzen","locid":"197bb07e-e2b9-4b82-805b-c89e9b79eb1b","name":"Lorenzen, Mark","orcid":"0000-0001-8913-1143","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-76504a21-d168-44e4-a87e-d11443f5e896","sdu-5f0058cf-575f-4e93-9321-18a8bf441404","sdu-cef876a9-a497-47bf-9af4-f1736327e3ed"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Broad vs. the Pointed Brush : Status Change, Stigma and Blame Following Fast Organizational Failure","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-087.80-698091","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Sufficient antibiotic dosing in septic patients is essential for reducing mortality. Piperacillin-tazobactam is often used for empirical treatment, but due to the pharmacokinetic (PK) variability seen in septic patients, optimal dosing may be a challenge. We determined the PK profile for piperacillin given at 4 g every 8 h in 22 septic patients admitted to a medical ward. Piperacillin concentrations were compared to the clinical breakpoint MIC for Pseudomonas aeruginosa (16 mg/liter), and the following PK/pharmacodynamic (PD) targets were evaluated: the percentage of the dosing interval that the free drug concentration is maintained above the MIC (fTMIC) of 50% and 100%. A two-compartment population PK model described the data well, with clearance being divided into renal and nonrenal components. The renal component was proportional to the estimated creatinine clearance (eCLCR) and constituted 74% of the total clearance in a typical individual (eCLCR, 83.9 ml/min). Patients with a high eCLCR (>130 ml/min) were at risk of subtherapeutic concentrations for the current regimen, with a 90% probability of target attainment being reached at MICs of 2.0 (50% fTMIC) and 0.125 mg/liter (100% fTMIC). Simulations of alternative dosing regimens and modes of administration showed that dose increment and prolonged infusion increased the chance of achieving predefined PK/PD targets. Alternative dosing strategies may therefore be needed to optimize piperacillin exposure in septic patients. (This study has been registered at ClinicalTrials.gov under identifier NCT02569086.).","author_count":6,"contributors":["Andersen, Maria Goul","Thorsted, Anders","Storgaard, Merete","Kristoffersson, Anders N","Friberg, Lena E","Öbrink-Hansen, Kristina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-192899"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Augmented renal clearance","Clinical outcomes","Critically ill patients","Dosage optimization","Infections","Meropenem","Metaanalysis","Pharmacodynamics","Piperacillin","Population pharmacokinetics","Sepsis","beta lactam antibiotics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"population pharmacokinetics of piperacillin in sepsis patients should alternative dosing strategies be considered","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5923116/pdf/e02306-17.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-192899","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5923116","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29507062","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000431341200054","type":"wos"},{"id":"85046033328","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-6f60d3f7-d455-4472-bdf1-ddb2bca50a33"],"keyword":["Augmented renal clearance","BETA-LACTAM ANTIBIOTICS","CARE-UNIT PATIENTS","CLINICAL-OUTCOMES","CRITICALLY-ILL PATIENTS","Dosage optimization","INFECTIONS","MEROPENEM","METAANALYSIS","PHARMACODYNAMICS","PROLONGED INFUSION","Piperacillin","Population pharmacokinetics","Sepsis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D74652211B9500D6EEA8ACA9E27F3434"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC5923116/pdf/e02306-17.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Goul","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Maria Goul","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"thorstedpau","last":"Thorsted","name":"Thorsted, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Merete","key":"storgaardpau","last":"Storgaard","locid":"2c2b23fe-581a-47b7-9194-ab66b60773d3","name":"Storgaard, Merete","orcid":"0000-0001-6110-5963","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders N","key":"kristofferssonpau","last":"Kristoffersson","name":"Kristoffersson, Anders N","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena E","key":"fribergpau","last":"Friberg","name":"Friberg, Lena E","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"öbrinkhansenpau","last":"Öbrink-Hansen","name":"Öbrink-Hansen, Kristina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29507062"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/aac.02306-17","issn":["00664804","10706283"],"issn_org":["00664804"],"issue":"5","journal":"Antimicrobial Agents and Chemotherapy","paperid":"e02306","publisher":"American Society for Microbiology","status":"p","title":"Antimicrobial Agents and Chemotherapy","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85046033328"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6f60d3f7-d455-4472-bdf1-ddb2bca50a33"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Population Pharmacokinetics of Piperacillin in Sepsis Patients : Should Alternative Dosing Strategies Be Considered?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-192899","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Background and Purpose-The GOLIATH trial (General or Local Anesthesia in Intra-Arterial Therapy) compared infarct growth and outcome in patients undergoing endovascular therapy under either general anesthesia or conscious sedation. Magnetic resonance imaging was performed before and after the procedure to study infarct growth. In this post hoc analysis of GOLIATH, we aimed to characterize the workflow of patients undergoing magnetic resonance imaging selection before endovascular therapy. Methods-We randomized 128 patients with anterior circulation large vessel occlusion stroke within 6 hours of onset to either general anesthesia or conscious sedation (1:1 allocation). We studied workflow time intervals to examine whether magnetic resonance imaging conferred a time delay in treatment when compared with computed tomography-based studies that emphasized rapid workflow. Results-Of 128 patients enrolled between March 2015 and February 2017, 65 were randomized to general anesthesia. Baseline demographic and clinical variables were balanced between the treatment arms. The median interval from scan to groin puncture was 56.5 minutes (interquartile range, 44.5-73.5) for all patients. The median interval from admission to groin puncture was 68 minutes (interquartile range, 54.5-87 minutes). Comparable intervals in recent randomized data were 51 minutes (interquartile range, 39-68) for scan to groin puncture in the ESCAPE trial (Endovascular Treatment for Small Core and Anterior Circulation Proximal Occlusion With Emphasis on Minimizing CT to Recanalization Times) and 90 minutes (interquartile range, 69-120 minutes) for door to groin puncture in the SWIFT-PRIME study (Solitaire With the Intention for Thrombectomy as Primary Endovascular Treatment). Conclusions-Workflow in GOLIATH demonstrates that magnetic resonance imaging selection for endovascular therapy can be accomplished rapidly and within a similar time frame as computed tomography-based selection.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Simonsen, Claus Ziegler","Yoo, Albert J","Rasmussen, Mads","Sørensen, Kristina E","Leslie-Mazwi, Thabele","Andersen, Grethe","Sørensen, Leif Hougaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-255392"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, Massachusetts, USA."],"keyword":["Conscious Sedation","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Stroke","Thrombectomy","Workflow"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"magnetic resonance imaging selection for endovascular stroke therapy workflow in the goliath trial","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85050603954","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-255392","identifier":[{"id":"29739917","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85050603954","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-dcde53f4-1773-4fdd-8436-a1038b040a3d"],"keyword":["conscious sedation","magnetic resonance imaging","stroke","thrombectomy","workflow"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A0F2A7E239AE73040A3B2C3F88071870"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Neurology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital (AUH)"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"massachusetts general hospital boston massachusetts usa","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts General Hospital, Boston, Massachusetts, USA.","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus Ziegler","key":"simonsenclauszieglerpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"ccf2fb52-6a4a-45b2-adb0-d6e83324879f","name":"Simonsen, Claus Ziegler","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Albert J","key":"yooalbertjpau","last":"Yoo","name":"Yoo, Albert J","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"rasmussenmadspau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"10307123-564d-4db1-872d-d0a91168ce4e","name":"Rasmussen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0002-0416-6767","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina E","key":"sørensenkristinaepau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Kristina E","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Thabele","key":"lesliemazwithabelepau","last":"Leslie-Mazwi","name":"Leslie-Mazwi, Thabele","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Grethe","key":"andersengrethepau","last":"Andersen","locid":"97e157c9-4cb4-4690-a971-06e4699b50fe","name":"Andersen, Grethe","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-2500","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leif H","key":"sørensenleifhougaardpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"c61295b9-5523-47cf-8bb6-bfca2f638826","name":"Sørensen, Leif Hougaard","name_org":"Sørensen, Leif H","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29739917"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/strokeaha.118.021038","issn":["00392499","15244628"],"issn_org":["00392499"],"issue":"6","journal":"Stroke","pages":"1402-1406","publisher":"Wolters Kluwer Health","status":"p","title":"Stroke","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85050603954"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-dcde53f4-1773-4fdd-8436-a1038b040a3d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Magnetic Resonance Imaging Selection for Endovascular Stroke Therapy - Workflow in the GOLIATH Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-255392","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The transition to renewable energy sources has created need for stationary, low-cost electrical energy storage. A possible technology to address both cost and environmental concerns are batteries based on organic materials. The use of oligoanthraquinones as a replacement for metal hydrides or cadmium in nickel hydroxide rechargeable batteries is investigated in detail regarding polymer composition, electrochemical reversibility and electroactive species cost. Two different oligoanthraquinones are paired with a nickel hydroxide cathode and demonstrate cycling stability dependent on parameters such as supporting electrolyte strength, C-rate, and anode swelling. The energy efficiencies are up to 75% and the cell potential up to 1.13 V. Simple functionalization of the basic structure increases the cell potential by 100 mV.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Dražević, Emil","Andersen, Anders Søndergaard","Wedege, Kristina","Henriksen, Martin Lahn","Hinge, Mogens","Bentien, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-259817"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anthraquinone","Energy storage","Rechargeable battery","Renewable energy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigation of low cost oligoanthraquinones for alkaline aqueous rechargeable batteries with cell potential up to 000000000001 000000000013 v","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85041552847","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-259817","identifier":[{"id":"85041552847","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e4884233-67f0-4a8f-aaf0-317adf55f07a"],"keyword":["Anthraquinone","Energy storage","Rechargeable battery","Renewable energy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FF666788F352707E148FA1EFA452A1D8"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Engineering, Department of Engineering - Electrochemical Energy Conversion and Batteries"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Emil","key":"draževićpau","last":"Dražević","locid":"b0668396-9bc9-41a7-b416-c55b8af8bd3d","name":"Dražević, Emil","orcid":"0000-0001-5412-2431","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Søndergaard","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"03a54886-dd7b-4362-b4d3-824bd24fbafd","name":"Andersen, Anders Søndergaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"wedegepau","last":"Wedege","locid":"c8f65125-c315-4522-93dd-2f9e0c9ee957","name":"Wedege, Kristina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"25cf5b38-ed1a-45cf-8375-fb19db3eb73f","name":"Henriksen, Martin Lahn","name_org":"Henriksen, Martin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mogens","key":"hingepau","last":"Hinge","locid":"5e496355-7cb5-42ca-a3b7-305c447e678c","name":"Hinge, Mogens","orcid":"0000-0002-8787-5314","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"bentienpau","last":"Bentien","locid":"233be99b-5e60-4512-8072-d8ac7d8e64fd","name":"Bentien, Anders","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jpowsour.2018.01.092","issn":["03787753","18732755"],"issn_org":["03787753"],"journal":"Journal of Power Sources","pages":"94-100","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Power Sources","volume":"381"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041552847"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e4884233-67f0-4a8f-aaf0-317adf55f07a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Investigation of low-cost oligoanthraquinones for alkaline, aqueous rechargeable batteries with cell potential up to 1.13 V","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-259817","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Baggrund: Sundhedsprofessionelle i Danmark er jf. Sundhedsloven forpligtet til at yde den bedste behandling, hvilket vil sige at leve op til de stigende krav om dokumentation og sikre, at praksis bygger på forskningsbaseret viden og evidens (1, 2). For at arbejde evidensbaseret er det bl.a. nødvendigt at gøre brug af standardiserede undersøgelsesredskaber som AMPS, der genererer valide og reliable data (3, p. 17(11)). Flere studier undersøger hvilke udfordringer der opstår ifm. anvendelse og implementering af AMPS i England, hvorfor det nu kunne være interessant at undersøge i dansk ergoterapi praksis (4, 5).  Formål: Formålet med projektet er at beskrive den aktuelle status på anvendelse og implementering af AMPS i dansk ergoterapi praksis. Anvendte metoder: Projektet er et kvantitativt, deskriptivt tværsnitsstudie, hvor data indsamles ved hjælp af et landsdækkende, elektronisk spørgeskema (6, 7, 8).  Resultater: Det fremgår, at størstedelen af respondenterne i projektet anvender AMPS, og at redskabet oftest anvendes i region Midtjylland og inden for det neurologiske område. AMPS anvendes typisk <1 gang om ugen og oftest i vurderingsfasen. Det fremmer typisk anvendelsen af AMPS, når der, udover den nødvendige tid til rådighed, er opbakning fra ledelsen, mens anvendelsen af AMPS hæmmes, når den nødvendige tid ikke altid er til rådighed. På under halvdelen af respondenternes arbejdspladser er AMPS helt implementeret, af disse er det for halvdelen op til den enkelte ergoterapeut at afgøre, om AMPS skal anvendes. Det, der typisk fremmer implementeringen, er, når arbejdspladsen har faglig sparring. Resultaterne har vist, at årsagen, til at AMPS typisk ikke implementeres, er, at den nødvendige tid til undersøgelsen mangler. Konklusion: Det konkluderes, at en stor andel af respondenterne og deres arbejdspladser har intentioner om at anvende og implementere AMPS, men at det ikke er lykkedes fuldt ud.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Kristina Tomra","Pedersen, Kathrina Strøm","Nielsen, Louise Lyngsø","Andersen, Michelle Simone","Lenz, Susanne","Wæhrens, Eva Ejlersen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-651679"],"event":{"end":"2018-11-07","place":"Kolding , dk","start":"2018-11-06","title":"ERGO 18","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["AMPS","Ergoterapi"],"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Studerende ved Ergoterapeutuddannelsen, UCN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anvendelse og implementering af assessment of motor and process skills amps i dansk ergoterapi praksis","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-651679","ids":["ucn-99268904-c059-41b8-904a-0a672113a5cb"],"keyword":["AMPS","ergoterapi"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-E5ECD78965545C600338FF3FDDF7CDBC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Ergoterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Studerende ved Ergoterapeutuddannelsen, UCN"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Parker Instituttet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Tomra","key":"nielsenkristinatomrapau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2b848116-080f-4b20-bb1a-03255c905245","name":"Nielsen, Kristina Tomra","orcid":"0000-0002-4944-9453","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kathrina Strøm","key":"pedersenkathrinastrømpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Kathrina Strøm","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Lyngsø","key":"nielsenlouiselyngsøpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Louise Lyngsø","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle Simone","key":"andersenmichellesimonepau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Michelle Simone","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne","key":"lenzsusannepau","last":"Lenz","name":"Lenz, Susanne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva Ejlersen","key":"wæhrensevaejlersenpau","last":"Wæhrens","name":"Wæhrens, Eva Ejlersen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucn-99268904-c059-41b8-904a-0a672113a5cb"],"src":["UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Anvendelse og implementering af Assessment of Motor and Process Skills (AMPS) i dansk ergoterapi praksis","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-651679","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Følgende notat indeholder fire litteraturundersøgelser, der hver især redegør for forskellige aspekter med relevans for vedr. ændrede aldersgrænser for erhvervelse af kørekort til stor knallert og lille motorcykel. Litteraturundersøgelserne er sammenfatninger baseret på gennemgange af den internationale forskningslitteratur og udarbejdet med henblik på at klarlægge den eksisterende viden og de relevante erfaringer ift. ændrede aldersgrænser. Litteraturundersøgelserne omhandler hhv.: I. Ændrede aldersgrænsers betydning for unges transportmønstre II. Tohjulede køretøjers betydning for trafiksikkerheden III. Overførsel af kompetencer IV. Etablering af transportvaner på længere sigt","author_count":3,"contributors":["Møller, Mette","Bonde, Nanna Skou","Krogh Andersen, Sandra Kristina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-367786"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"litteraturundersøgelser vedrørende tohjulede motorkøretøjer delnotat vii","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/164663361/Del_VII_Litteraturunders_gelser_vedr_rende_tohjulede_motork_ret_jer.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-367786","ids":["dtu-d38f93c4-aa66-4da6-80e1-06b6959aa6cf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4325584C2728027F7751DDB92BF8EEBE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/164663361/Del_VII_Litteraturunders_gelser_vedr_rende_tohjulede_motork_ret_jer.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Technology and Innovation Management","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Transport DTU"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"bc2c2ce5-846a-48d8-8f1c-98639e8c7604","name":"Møller, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-0012-8691","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna Skou","key":"bondepau","last":"Bonde","locid":"f3163949-cb40-41ce-ae66-9c54a00af84b","name":"Bonde, Nanna Skou","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sandra Kristina","key":"kroghandersenpau","last":"Krogh Andersen","locid":"b35dc181-b805-4bfd-8753-398a7f4021f4","name":"Krogh Andersen, Sandra Kristina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"31","place":"Lyngby, Denmark","publisher":"Technical University of Denmark","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d38f93c4-aa66-4da6-80e1-06b6959aa6cf"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Litteraturundersøgelser vedrørende tohjulede motorkøretøjer: Delnotat VII","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-367786","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Glucagon-like peptide 1 receptor agonists differ in chemical structure, duration of action, and in their effects on clinical outcomes. The cardiovascular effects of once-weekly albiglutide in type 2 diabetes are unknown. We aimed to determine the safety and efficacy of albiglutide in preventing cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction, or stroke. METHODS: We did a double-blind, randomised, placebo-controlled trial in 610 sites across 28 countries. We randomly assigned patients aged 40 years and older with type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease (at a 1:1 ratio) to groups that either received a subcutaneous injection of albiglutide (30-50 mg, based on glycaemic response and tolerability) or of a matched volume of placebo once a week, in addition to their standard care. Investigators used an interactive voice or web response system to obtain treatment assignment, and patients and all study investigators were masked to their treatment allocation. We hypothesised that albiglutide would be non-inferior to placebo for the primary outcome of the first occurrence of cardiovascular death, myocardial infarction, or stroke, which was assessed in the intention-to-treat population. If non-inferiority was confirmed by an upper limit of the 95% CI for a hazard ratio of less than 1·30, closed testing for superiority was prespecified. This study is registered with ClinicalTrials.gov, number NCT02465515. FINDINGS: Patients were screened between July 1, 2015, and Nov 24, 2016. 10 793 patients were screened and 9463 participants were enrolled and randomly assigned to groups: 4731 patients were assigned to receive albiglutide and 4732 patients to receive placebo. On Nov 8, 2017, it was determined that 611 primary endpoints and a median follow-up of at least 1·5 years had accrued, and participants returned for a final visit and discontinuation from study treatment; the last patient visit was on March 12, 2018. These 9463 patients, the intention-to-treat population, were evaluated for a median duration of 1·6 years and were assessed for the primary outcome. The primary composite outcome occurred in 338 (7%) of 4731 patients at an incidence rate of 4·6 events per 100 person-years in the albiglutide group and in 428 (9%) of 4732 patients at an incidence rate of 5·9 events per 100 person-years in the placebo group (hazard ratio 0·78, 95% CI 0·68-0·90), which indicated that albiglutide was superior to placebo (p<0·0001 for non-inferiority; p=0·0006 for superiority). The incidence of acute pancreatitis (ten patients in the albiglutide group and seven patients in the placebo group), pancreatic cancer (six patients in the albiglutide group and five patients in the placebo group), medullary thyroid carcinoma (zero patients in both groups), and other serious adverse events did not differ between the two groups. There were three (<1%) deaths in the placebo group that were assessed by investigators, who were masked to study drug assignment, to be treatment-related and two (<1%) deaths in the albiglutide group. INTERPRETATION: In patients with type 2 diabetes and cardiovascular disease, albiglutide was superior to placebo with respect to major adverse cardiovascular events. Evidence-based glucagon-like peptide 1 receptor agonists should therefore be considered as part of a comprehensive strategy to reduce the risk of cardiovascular events in patients with type 2 diabetes. FUNDING: GlaxoSmithKline.","author_count":30,"contributors":["Hernandez, Adrian F","Green, Jennifer B","Janmohamed, Salim","D'Agostino, Ralph B","Granger, Christopher B","Jones, Nigel P","Leiter, Lawrence A","Rosenberg, Anne E","Sigmon, Kristina N","Somerville, Matthew C","Thorpe, Karl M","McMurray, John J V","Del Prato, Stefano","Holman, Rury","DeMets, David","Riddle, Matthew","Galatius, Søren","Andersen, Ulla","Brønnum-Schou, Jens","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","Jensen, Jan Skov","Kober, Lars","Kristiansen, Ole Peter","Lund, Per","Melchior, Thomas","Nyvad, Ole","Schou, Morten","Kumar, Somesh","Patil, Suradnya","Mandal, Trisha"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-511529"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["Harmony Outcomes committees and investigators"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Cardiovascular Diseases etiology","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 complications","Double Blind Method","Drug Administration Schedule","Female","Glucagon Like Peptide 1 administration dosage","Humans","Hypoglycemic Agents administration dosage","Injections Subcutaneous","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction etiology","Stroke etiology","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"albiglutide and cardiovascular outcomes in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes and cardiovascular disease harmony outcomes a double blind randomised placebo controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-511529","identifier":[{"id":"85055101508","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30291013","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c5d447d8-b920-484e-96ee-21731ffe557e"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Cardiovascular Diseases/etiology","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/complications","Double-Blind Method","Drug Administration Schedule","Female","Glucagon-Like Peptide 1/administration & dosage","Humans","Hypoglycemic Agents/administration & dosage","Injections, Subcutaneous","Kaplan-Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction/etiology","Stroke/etiology","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9B2E0DC5061A13077955D52208AF9626"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universit