sbjerg, Micke","orcid":"0000-0002-7240-2450","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","locid":"d095fb26-6bde-4e85-843c-f409670947ae","name":"Eriksen, Kristina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"pittelkowpau","last":"Pittelkow","locid":"06c9cf58-d88e-45f7-99e5-55a77e030d6d","name":"Pittelkow, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-3371-9500","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ijch.201700129","issn":["00212148","18695868"],"issn_org":["00212148"],"issue":"3-4","journal":"Israel Journal of Chemistry","pages":"435-448","status":"p","title":"Israel Journal of Chemistry","volume":"58"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85043376944"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d2a5e0e0-2d5b-47a8-8f6a-cff564e28f1a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hemicucurbit[<em>n</em>]urils and Their Derivatives - Synthesis and Applications","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-519294","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Impairment of endothelial function with aging is accompanied by reduced nitric oxide (NO) production. T-type Cav3.1 channels augment nitric oxide and co-localize with eNOS. Therefore, the hypothesis was that T-type channels contribute to the endothelial dysfunction of aging. Endothelial function was determined in mesenteric arteries (perfusion) and aortae (isometric contraction) of young and old wild-type (WT), Cav3.1, and Cav3.2 knockout mice. NO production was measured by fluorescence imaging in mesenteric arteries. With age, endothelium-dependent subsequent dilatation (following depolarization with KCl) of mesenteric arteries was diminished in the arteries of WT mice, unchanged in Cav3.2(-/-) preparations but increased in those of Cav3.1(-/-) mice. NO synthase inhibition abolished the subsequent dilatation in mesenteric arteries and acetylcholine-induced relaxations in aortae. NO levels were significantly reduced in mesenteric arteries of old compared to young WT mice. In Cav3.1(-/-) and Cav3.2(-/-) preparations, NO levels increased significantly with age. Relaxations to acetylcholine were significantly smaller in the aortae of old compared to young WT mice, while such responses were comparable in preparations of young and old Cav3.1(-/-) and Cav3.2(-/-) mice. The expression of Cav3.1 was significantly reduced in aortae from aged compared to young WT mice. The level of phosphorylated eNOS was significantly increased in aortae from aged Cav3.1(-/-) mice. In conclusion, T-type calcium channel-deficient mice develop less age-dependent endothelial dysfunction. Changes in NO levels are involved in this phenomenon in WT and Cav3.1(-/-) mice. These findings suggest that T-type channels play an important role in age-induced endothelial dysfunction.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Thuesen, Anne Daugaard","Andersen, Kenneth","Lyngsø, Kristina Sanne","Burton, Mark","Brasch-Andersen, Charlotte","Vanhoutte, Paul M","Hansen, Pernille B L"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-597505"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Pernille B L"],"country":["Hong Kong","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","AstraZeneca Sweden","The University of Hong Kong"],"keyword":["Aging metabolism","Animals","Calcium Channels T Type genetics","Endothelium Vascular metabolism","Female","Gene Deletion","Male","Mice","Mice Inbred C57BL","Nitric Oxide metabolism","Vasoconstriction","Vasodilation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deletion of t type calcium channels cav000000000003 000000000001 or cav000000000003 000000000002 attenuates endothelial dysfunction in aging mice","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85032489889","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-597505","identifier":[{"id":"29082441","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85032489889","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-54bcbdb6-cb0f-41e1-91d6-6029cbe99d9a"],"keyword":["Aging/metabolism","Animals","Aorta/growth & development","Calcium Channels, T-Type/genetics","Endothelium, Vascular/metabolism","Female","Gene Deletion","Male","Mesenteric Arteries/growth & development","Mice","Mice, Inbred C57BL","Nitric Oxide/metabolism","Vasoconstriction","Vasodilation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6506853D82C9DC03D00A717E2EB46DA8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Molecular Medicine, Cardiovascular and Renal Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"hk","key":"the university of hong kong","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"The University of Hong Kong","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"astrazeneca sweden","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AstraZeneca Sweden","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne D","key":"thuesenpau","last":"Thuesen","locid":"8018335d-6b93-4d02-a85c-f9b93db52cf9","name":"Thuesen, Anne Daugaard","name_org":"Thuesen, Anne D","orcid":"0000-0001-5954-2689","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"c0f63d50-9350-4359-b4a2-c0e82dfff7f2","name":"Andersen, Kenneth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina S","key":"lyngsøpau","last":"Lyngsø","locid":"a3858182-77f4-4505-9b59-3aeddfc7edb4","name":"Lyngsø, Kristina Sanne","name_org":"Lyngsø, Kristina S","orcid":"0000-0002-3250-4049","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark","key":"burtonpau","last":"Burton","locid":"1279f5b8-9ebb-423f-8bc7-a9956bbbcc0a","name":"Burton, Mark","orcid":"0000-0002-3782-5933","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"braschandersenpau","last":"Brasch-Andersen","locid":"3fe4d15d-5f04-4ec0-87b8-000b5f993ed1","name":"Brasch-Andersen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-4273-0047","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul M","key":"vanhouttepau","last":"Vanhoutte","name":"Vanhoutte, Paul M","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille B L","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d8859077-5138-45dc-ad86-4039d18a5a84","name":"Hansen, Pernille B L","orcid":"0000-0003-0661-1665","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29082441"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00424-017-2068-x","issn":["00316768","14322013"],"issn_org":["00316768"],"issue":"2","journal":"Pflügers Archiv - European Journal of Physiology","pages":"355-365","publisher":"Springer Science+Business Media","status":"p","title":"Pflügers Archiv - European Journal of Physiology","volume":"470"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85032489889"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-54bcbdb6-cb0f-41e1-91d6-6029cbe99d9a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Deletion of T-type calcium channels Cav3.1 or Cav3.2 attenuates endothelial dysfunction in aging mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-597505","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Professionals often face a choice between gathering experience abroad or increasing embeddedness in their local context, this paper explores whether professionals benefit from these different types of experience depends on project characteristics. The paper builds on extent theories, which clearly demonstrate the advantages of diverse experience in the production of highly creative innovations, and extends this theoretical framework with an important contingency, namely project characteristics. This theorizing is tested on longitudinal data from the Danish film industry, and the results show that project characteristics determine the value of professional experience abroad: Professionals’ likelihood of contributing to high performing creative innovations increases with professional experience abroad when projects are characterized by a low level of constraints. However, when projects are characterized by a high level of constraints the effect is not merely moderated, but even reversed. The value of professional experience abroad increases with distance between the local and foreign context decreases with increased availability of professional experience abroad.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-614525"],"event":{"end":"2018-09-25","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2018-09-22","title":"Strategic Management Society","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how professional experience abroad contributes to high performing creative innovations","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-614525","ids":["sdu-90283df0-7d32-4f72-84d5-c585de11929c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7B30FD6A40998A944A39EA7C01AC811F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM), Centre for Integrative Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"46d2bbb6-cde6-45b4-b04d-dcbcbad97c83","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-90283df0-7d32-4f72-84d5-c585de11929c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"How professional experience abroad contributes to high performing creative innovations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-614525","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
