{"abstract":"A rotating bed reactor (RBR) has been modeled using computational fluid dynamics (CFD). The flow pattern in the RBR was investigated and the flow through the porous material in it was quantified. A simplified geometry representing the more complex RBR geometry was introduced and the simplified model was able to reproduce the main characteristics of the flow. Alternating reactor shapes were investigated, and it was concluded that the use of baffles has a very large impact on the flows through the porous material. The simulations suggested, therefore, that even faster reaction rates could be achieved by making the baffles deeper. Two-phase simulations were performed, which managed to reproduce the deflection of the gas–liquid interface in an unbaffled system. A chemical reaction was implemented in the model, describing the ion-exchange phenomena in the porous material using four different Sherwood number correlations. The simulations were overall in good agreement with experimental data.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsson, Hilde Kristina","Schjøtt Andersen, Patrick Alexander","Byström, Emil","Gernaey, Krist","Krühne, Ulrich"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-367935"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","SpinChem AB"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cfd modeling of flow and ion exchange kinetics in a rotating bed reactor system","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.iecr.7b00224","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-367935","identifier":[{"id":"85020019097","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-d40d84f2-956e-442b-879d-beaf8651c965"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-99DEAF17B3305F4A99A1313D802ADAE6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.iecr.7b00224","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CAPEC-PROCESS"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"spinchem ab","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SpinChem AB","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hilde Kristina","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","locid":"cd1f4f93-ef22-4f8f-8f97-9f4116fbb0da","name":"Larsson, Hilde Kristina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patrick Alexander","key":"schjøttandersenpau","last":"Schjøtt Andersen","name":"Schjøtt Andersen, Patrick Alexander","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emil","key":"byströmpau","last":"Byström","name":"Byström, Emil","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Krist","key":"gernaeypau","last":"Gernaey","locid":"cc1a5662-82ba-4420-96be-f2a9d371b22d","name":"Gernaey, Krist","orcid":"0000-0002-0364-1773","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrich","key":"krühnepau","last":"Krühne","locid":"d6c591c0-1289-4e13-bfbd-0194f9d93346","name":"Krühne, Ulrich","orcid":"0000-0001-7774-7442","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.iecr.7b00224","issn":["08885885","15205045"],"issn_org":["08885885"],"issue":"14","journal":"Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research","pages":"3853-3865","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Industrial & Engineering Chemistry Research","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85020019097"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d40d84f2-956e-442b-879d-beaf8651c965"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"CFD Modeling of Flow and Ion Exchange Kinetics in a Rotating Bed Reactor System","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-367935","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"A Swedish pedigree with an autosomal dominant inheritance of idiopathic scoliosis was initially studied by genetic linkage analysis, prioritising genomic regions for further analysis. This revealed a locus on chromosome 1 with a putative risk haplotype shared by all affected individuals. Two affected individuals were subsequently exome-sequenced, identifying a rare, non-synonymous variant in the CELSR2 gene. This variant is rs141489111, a c.G6859A change in exon 21 (NM_001408), leading to a predicted p.V2287I (NP_001399.1) change. This variant was found in all affected members of the pedigree, but showed reduced penetrance. Analysis of tagging variants in CELSR1-3 in a set of 1739 Swedish-Danish scoliosis cases and 1812 controls revealed significant association (p = 0.0001) to rs2281894, a common synonymous variant in CELSR2. This association was not replicated in case-control cohorts from Japan and the US. No association was found to variants in CELSR1 or CELSR3. Our findings suggest a rare variant in CELSR2 as causative for idiopathic scoliosis in a family with dominant segregation and further highlight common variation in CELSR2 in general susceptibility to idiopathic scoliosis in the Swedish-Danish population. Both variants are located in the highly conserved GAIN protein domain, which is necessary for the auto-proteolysis of CELSR2, suggesting its functional importance.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Einarsdottir, Elisabet","Grauers, Anna","Wang, Jingwen","Jiao, Hong","Escher, Stefan A","Danielsson, Aina","Simony, Ane","Andersen, Mikkel Østerheden","Christensen, Steen Bach","Åkesson, Kristina","Kou, Ikuyo","Khanshour, Anas M","Ohlin, Acke","Wise, Carol","Ikegawa, Shiro","Kere, Juha","Gerdhem, Paul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-625955"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Japan","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institute","King's College London","Lund University","RIKEN Center for Integrative Medical Sciences","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","Sundsvall and Härnösand County Hospital","The University of Texas Southwestern Medical Center","University of Gothenburg","University of Helsinki"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Sarah M. and Charles E. Seay Center for Musculoskeletal Research, Texas Scottish Rite Hospital for Children, Dallas, Texas, United States of America."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"celsr000000000002 is a candidate susceptibility gene in idiopathic scoliosis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0189591","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-625955","identifier":[{"id":"85038599608","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5730153","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29240829","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-b7e55a11-6e73-4852-9a26-05e4b6b212db"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-490C0DEC2A8AACFEB8B3C139C97C9A2E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129784783/CELSR2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0189591","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"karolinska institute","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"na