{"abstract":"The goal for this workshop is to provide a venue at CHI for research through design practitioners to materially share their work with each other. Conversation will largely be centered upon a discussion of objects produced through a research through design process. Bringing together researchers as well as their physical work is a means of gaining insight into the practices and outcomes of research through design. If research through design is to continue to develop as a research practice for generating knowledge within HCI, this requires developing ways of attending to its made, material outcomes. The premise of this workshop is simple: We need additional spaces for interacting with and reflecting upon material design outcomes at CHI. The goal of this workshop is to experiment with such a space, and to initially do so without a strong theoretical or conceptual framing.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jenkins, Tom","Andersen, Kristina","Gaver, William","Odom, William","Pierce, James","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384007"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Netherlands","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Mellon University","Georgia Institute of Technology","Goldsmiths, University of London","STEIM","Simon Fraser University"],"keyword":["Design practices","HCI","Interdisciplinary workshop","Material outcomes","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"attending to objects as outcomes of design research","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85014580893","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384007","identifier":[{"id":"85014580893","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bb7443c2-74b6-4847-9aab-1c7384fce428"],"keyword":["Design practices","HCI","Interdisciplinary workshop","Material outcomes","Research through design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7EB975E30BB4B6F45CD5F1C879BFAA7A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"georgia institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Georgia Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"steim","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"STEIM","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"goldsmiths university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Goldsmiths, University of London","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"simon fraser university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Simon Fraser University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"carnegie mellon university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Carnegie Mellon University","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"jenkinspau","last":"Jenkins","name":"Jenkins, Tom","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Kristina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"William","key":"gaverpau","last":"Gaver","name":"Gaver, William","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"William","key":"odompau","last":"Odom","name":"Odom, William","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"James","key":"piercepau","last":"Pierce","name":"Pierce, James","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2851581.2856508","isbn":["9781450340823"],"pages":"3423-3430","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"ACM Annual Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","status":"p","subtitle":"CHI EA '16","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 CHI Conference Extended Abstracts on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85014580893"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bb7443c2-74b6-4847-9aab-1c7384fce428"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Attending to Objects as Outcomes of Design Research","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384007","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND PURPOSE: To test the effect of longitudinal feedback on late effects reported by survivors of head-and-neck cancer (HNC) to clinicians during regular follow-up. MATERIAL AND METHODS: A total of 266 participants were sequentially assigned to either control or intervention group and filled in electronic versions of the EORTC QLQ C-30, H&N35, HADS and a study-specific list of symptoms at up to two consecutive follow-up visits. Participants' symptoms displayed according to severity were provided to the clinician for the intervention group but not for the control group. Linear mixed-effects models were used to examine the number of symptoms assessed by clinicians (primary outcome). Multivariate linear regression models examined participants' long-term symptom control and QoL (secondary outcome). RESULTS: More symptoms were assessed by clinicians in the intervention group at all three visits (P<0.001, <0.001, and P=0.04). No effect was observed on most patient outcomes. When prompted by patient-reported outcomes at consultations, clinicians and patients were in better agreement about the occurrence of severe symptoms at all three visits. CONCLUSION: Timely patient-reported outcomes to clinicians in routine follow-up of HNC survivors enhanced clinicians' rates of assessment of late symptoms. Giving reports of patient-reported outcome to clinicians had limited impact on participants' QoL or symptom burden.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kjaer, Trille Kristina","Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","Andersen, Elo","Karlsen, Randi V","Nielsen, Anni Linnet","Hansen, Merete Kjaer","Frederiksen, Kirsten","Johansen, Christoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-521527"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Female","Follow Up Studies","Head and Neck Neoplasms","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Quality of Life","Research Design","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Surveys and Questionnaires","Survivors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a controlled study of use of patient reported outcomes to improve assessment of late effects after treatment for head and neck cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-521527","identifier":[{"id":"27178143","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84973643679","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d6631326-2738-46f4-be11-3bd7178d4760"],"keyword":["Female","Follow-Up Studies","Head and Neck Neoplasms","Humans","Journal Article","Male","Middle Aged","Patient Reported Outcome Measures","Quality of Life","Research Design","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Surveys and Questionnaires","Survivors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9BBE65BA01ECB1F6997FEAA0F8FEDE56"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Trille Kristina","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","name":"Kjaer, Trille Kristina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Susanne Oksbjerg","key":"daltonpau","last":"Dalton","name":"Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elo","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Elo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Randi V","key":"karlsenpau","last":"Karlsen","name":"Karlsen, Randi V","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anni Linnet","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anni Linnet","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Merete Kjaer","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Merete Kjaer","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kirsten","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","name":"Frederiksen, Kirsten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"18d62c73-2f35-499d-ac94-134ecd806296","name":"Johansen, Christoffer","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27178143"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.radonc.2016.04.034","issn":["01678140"],"issue":"2","journal":"Radiotherapy and Oncology","pages":"221-228","status":"p","title":"Radiotherapy and Oncology","title_org":"Radiotherapy and oncology : journal of the European Society for Therapeutic Radiology and Oncology","volume":"119"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84973643679"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d6631326-2738-46f4-be11-3bd7178d4760"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A controlled study of use of patient-reported outcomes to improve assessment of late effects after treatment for head-and-neck cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-521527","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":9,"contributors":["Kjaer, Trille Kristina","Johansen, Christoffer","Andersen, Elo","Karlsen, Randi V","Nielsen, Anni Linnet","Frederiksen, Kirsten","Rørth, Mikael","Ibfelt, Else","Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-531292"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of social factors on patient reported late symptoms report from a controlled trial among long term head and neck cancer survivors in denmark","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-531292","identifier":[{"id":"84949871045","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26613661","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e6d6200e-e9fe-48c8-bde3-54cbb4d66a87"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D3E5646B36F49E96058A8CA2B402451"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Trille Kristina","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","name":"Kjaer, Trille Kristina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"18d62c73-2f35-499d-ac94-134ecd806296","name":"Johansen, Christoffer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Elo","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Elo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Randi V","key":"karlsenpau","last":"Karlsen","name":"Karlsen, Randi V","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anni Linnet","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anni Linnet","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kirsten","key":"frederiksenpau","last":"Frederiksen","name":"Frederiksen, Kirsten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikael","key":"rørthpau","last":"Rørth","locid":"3495a8d7-73b7-40a5-a9de-ee95073dfe42","name":"Rørth, Mikael","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Else","key":"ibfeltpau","last":"Ibfelt","name":"Ibfelt, Else","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Susanne Oksbjerg","key":"daltonpau","last":"Dalton","name":"Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26613661"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/hed.24306","issn":["10433074","10970347"],"issn_org":["10433074"],"issue":"S1","journal":"Head & Neck","status":"p","title":"Head & Neck","title_org":"Head & Neck (Print Edition)","volume":"38"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949871045"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e6d6200e-e9fe-48c8-bde3-54cbb4d66a87"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Influence of social factors on patient-reported late symptoms : Report from a controlled trial among long-term head and neck cancer survivors in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-531292","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Rank-ordered relationships depicturing status and status differences have been shown to emerge in social settings as different as film production, professional sport, education, wine making, open source communities, and medical doctors. These status hierarchies tend to be relatively stable, but at times individuals or organizations successfully climb the status hierarchy or fall from grace. A growing body of research focuses on these status dynamics rather than static status measures. Based on data from 826 scientists affiliated with a Large Scale Research Facility (LSRF) collaborating on 1282 on-site and 151,302 off-site publications we analyze relationships between status dynamics, tie formation and performance among scientists. We find that there is a cost of collaborating with rising stars – in the form of increasing status - as collaboration partners’ positive status shifts is negatively associated with the focal scientist’s performance. Also, we find that the association between individual scientists’ status attainment and tie creation follows and inverted U-shape, while the relationship between status attainment and performance is positive. Finally, we find that status decline has a negative association with both tie creation and subsequent performance.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Jacob","Andersen, Kristina Vaarst"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-285288"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-15","place":"København, dk","start":"2016-06-13","title":"The DRUID 20th Anniversary Conference 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the cost of collaborating with climbers of status hierarchies status dynamics tie creation and performance in science","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://druid8.sit.aau.dk/druid/acc_papers/hfld3tv38v6891n045ds8mmh5nr1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-285288","ids":["cbs-6707b625-a369-485e-968b-0647d66b201b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9EE6DFBC01E64DE7E8E8B1A111CB0EBC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://druid8.sit.aau.dk/druid/acc_papers/hfld3tv38v6891n045ds8mmh5nr1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation, Department of Innovation and Organizational Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"8b2b644b-5bed-4d26-ad6f-2d87be498450","name":"Jeppesen, Jacob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina","key":"vaarstandersenpau","last":"Vaarst Andersen","locid":"e64ee7c1-08fa-4113-947a-18da853e6a39","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","name_org":"Vaarst Andersen, Kristina","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-6707b625-a369-485e-968b-0647d66b201b"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"The Cost of Collaborating with Climbers of Status Hierarchies : Status Dynamics, Tie Creation and Performance in Science","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-285288","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Status provides preferential access to resources, as well as favorable judgment, which in turn may lead to increases in performance. Prior work has established that such benefits even spill over between collaboration partners, thus allowing collaboration partners of high status individuals to bask in their reflected glory and enjoy status related benefits. Yet, we still know relatively little about the underlying mechanisms that affect how individual performance is affected by changes in the status of collaboration partners. In this paper, we analyze how collaboration partners’ status increase affects individual performance. We argue that collaboration partners’ increased status may divert their allocation of effort and focus to other projects. This in turn may lead to a negative spillover effect for individual performance. These arguments are tested using unique data on scientists collaborating on papers in a large-scale research facility and we find empirical support for a negative spillover effect of co-authors’ status increase. Further, we find that in some cases the negative spillover effect of co-authors’ status increase is reduced or even reversed.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","Mors, Marie Louise","Jeppesen, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-616702"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-15","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2016-06-13","title":"20th Danish Research Unit for Industrial Dynamics Anniversary Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the cost of collaborating with climbers of status hierarchies","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-616702","ids":["sdu-97d84496-bbb9-4ce4-999f-2f90d2db71e0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5B316AD878D9AE3B5F2B4D43F16B029E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM), Centre for Integrative Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"46d2bbb6-cde6-45b4-b04d-dcbcbad97c83","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Louise","key":"morspau","last":"Mors","name":"Mors, Marie Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","name":"Jeppesen, Jacob","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-97d84496-bbb9-4ce4-999f-2f90d2db71e0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Cost of Collaborating with Climbers of Status Hierarchies","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-616702","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: A correct diagnosis of preeclampsia and gestational hypertension is important for treatment and epidemiological studies. Changes in diagnostic criteria and underreporting in certain subsets of patients may hamper validity of the diagnoses. MATERIALS AND METHODS: We validated the discharge diagnoses of preeclampsia and gestational hypertension, which are reported to the Danish National Patient Registry, in a cohort of 2163 pregnant women by retrospective evaluation of electronic hospital data. RESULTS: A preeclampsia discharge diagnosis was found in 113 (5.2%) of the participants. After validation, significantly more patients fulfilled criteria for diagnosis of preeclampsia (n = 163, 7.5%, p = 0.002); more had severe preeclampsia, 14 (0.6%) vs. 70 (3.2%), p < 0.001 and gestational hypertension, 62 (2.9%) vs. 46 (2.1%), p = 0.12. The diagnostic sensitivity for preeclampsia by discharge diagnosis was 55.8%; severe preeclampsia 18.6%; gestational hypertension 39.1%. Corresponding positive predictive values were 80.5, 92.9 and 29.0%. Misclassification occurred in 4.3, 2.7 and 3.3%, respectively. Misclassification was more prevalent in obese compared to lean women (10% vs. 3.6%, p < 0.0001). CONCLUSIONS: Discharge diagnoses substantially underestimated the prevalence of preeclampsia, especially severe preeclampsia. Misclassification was most common in obese preeclamptic women. These findings depict the limitations associated with the direct use of discharge diagnoses of hypertensive disorders in pregnancy for research purposes.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Møller Luef, Birgitte","Andersen, Louise Bjørkholt","Renault, Kristina M","Nohr, Ellen A","Jørgensen, Jan Stener","Christesen, Henrik Thybo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-629680"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["High risk pregnancy","Obesity","Pre Eclampsia","Pregnancy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validation of hospital discharge diagnoses for hypertensive disorders of pregnancy","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84991717218","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-629680","identifier":[{"id":"27562930","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84991717218","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-c519a78c-ff39-4a2a-971b-e2725729b093"],"keyword":["High-risk Pregnancy","hypertension in pregnancy","obesity","pre-eclampsia","pregnancy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E9C9649976567C93FA19579C941A5348"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte","key":"møllerluefpau","last":"Møller Luef","locid":"56eea240-e90c-49ff-b82d-91ebca356cf6","name":"Møller Luef, Birgitte","orcid":"0000-0002-8356-5925","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise B","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"26e73134-b29b-450a-b9fd-b71c20be9185","name":"Andersen, Louise Bjørkholt","name_org":"Andersen, Louise B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Martha","key":"renaultpau","last":"Renault","locid":"71450333-81f3-4739-a961-71ee3f220084","name":"Renault, Kristina M","name_org":"Renault, Kristina Martha","orcid":"0000-0002-6387-9652","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ellen A","key":"nohrpau","last":"Nohr","locid":"7cacab04-e162-47a1-8d07-cf73fa62b4fc","name":"Nohr, Ellen A","orcid":"0000-0001-7039-1105","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan S","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"4e1adaff-d975-48d8-95b5-73bc6d115a5e","name":"Jørgensen, Jan Stener","name_org":"Jørgensen, Jan S","orcid":"0000-0001-5222-2535","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Boye Thybo","key":"christesenpau","last":"Christesen","locid":"c8317e72-7a09-4c80-81e9-b69855b68e8f","name":"Christesen, Henrik Thybo","name_org":"Christesen, Henrik Boye Thybo","orcid":"0000-0001-5330-6853","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27562930"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aogs.13006","issn":["00016349"],"issue":"11","journal":"Acta Obstetricia et Gynecologica Scandinavica","pages":"1288-1294","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Acta Obstetricia et Gynecologica Scandinavica","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84991717218"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c519a78c-ff39-4a2a-971b-e2725729b093"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Validation of hospital discharge diagnoses for hypertensive disorders of pregnancy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-629680","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents one-way cyclic tension tests on a pile segment installed in dense sand in a laboratory test setup. The test setup allowed application of surcharges to increase the vertical effective stress. The open-ended pipe pile segment was 0.5 m in diameter and 1 m in length. The test results showed that cyclic loading with small amplitudes can increase the shaft capacity, but increase of the cyclic amplitude can result in large accumulated displacements and decreased cyclic reloading stiffness. The test results are compared to an existing interaction diagram.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Thomassen, Kristina","Andersen, Lars Vabbersgaard","Ibsen, Lars Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-070299"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cyclic loading","Laboratory testing","Piles","Sand"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"axial cyclic loading tests on pile segments in sand","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17736/ijope.2016.cl01","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-070299","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000391844800006","type":"wos"},{"id":"85007137315","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-45e6fb89-c51e-4deb-ac65-0f62f391fdfc"],"keyword":["Cyclic loading","Laboratory testing","Piles","Sand","Tension loading"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-20AF90E5E6D9A301C212DE91698120E5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17736/ijope.2016.cl01","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university",