,"All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e80e7782-c617-4c1a-9fd4-eecb3901b77c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Guidelines for the use and interpretation of assays for monitoring autophagy : 3rd edition","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-532017","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"When organizations encounter rare events they often find it challenging to extract learning from the experience. We analyze opportunities for organizational learning in one such rare event, namely Intellectual Property (IP) litigation, i.e., when organizations take disputes regarding their intellectual property to court. We propose, that organizations can learn to litigate, although it is a rare event, by applying mechanisms in a current litigation case that have been successful in previous litigation cases. However, we also posit, that the usefulness of these learning mechanisms for a current litigation case is contingent on the type of litigation, contract versus infringement cases. If the organization is involved in litigation based on a contract breach, we suggest that learning will be less useful because the contract preceding the litigation defines the modus operandi and leaves the organization little discretion to utilize any learning from past litigation success. Thus, learning appears be to most beneficial in infringement cases. Based on statistical analysis of 10,211 litigation court cases in China, we find support for our hypotheses. Our findings suggest that organizations can learn to litigate, although litigation is a relatively rare event, if they leverage what they have learned from previously successful litigations. However, learning is less likely to be applicable to contract cases than it will be in infringement cases.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","Beukel, Karin","Tyler, Beverly B."],"cuid":["S03-092.23-031636"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-15","place":"København, dk","start":"2016-06-13","title":"20th Danish Research Unit for Industrial Dynamics Anniversary Conference","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","North Carolina State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"organizational learning in rare events the case of learning to litigate intellectual property ip","src":["cbs","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://druid8.sit.aau.dk/druid/acc_papers/o02pi11ifsc7rcd2l3qqkinfaqqi.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-092.23-031636","ids":["cbs-6aee9a73-da19-4519-a7c7-4dc85bf70eb8","ku-b70f7c39-0925-46ee-bee4-6f704ca7e6ec","sdu-fd1b4c89-e870-4560-bced-aa73c4bbf73a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-3-B0FDF32C73A29D290E74AF4CC5B2D279"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://druid8.sit.aau.dk/druid/acc_papers/o02pi11ifsc7rcd2l3qqkinfaqqi.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://conference.druid.dk/acc_papers/o02pi11ifsc7rcd2l3qqkinfaqqi.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation, Department of Innovation and Organizational Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM)","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business & Management (DBM), Centre for Integrative Innovation Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food and Resource Economics, Section for Production, Markets and Policy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"north carolina state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"North Carolina State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina","key":"vaarstandersenpau","last":"Vaarst Andersen","locid":"e64ee7c1-08fa-4113-947a-18da853e6a39","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","name_org":"Vaarst Andersen, Kristina","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Vaarst","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"46d2bbb6-cde6-45b4-b04d-dcbcbad97c83","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Karin","key":"beukelpau","last":"Beukel","locid":"8ea5e817-3e82-4011-a28d-daea7f59221d","name":"Beukel, Karin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Beverly B.","key":"tylerpau","last":"Tyler","name":"Tyler, Beverly B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Publis