{"abstract":"The paper analyzes status antecedents and their effect on tie creation and performance. We couple social exchange theory with focus theory, to improve our understanding of how individuals perceive, pursue and utilize status. We utilize two comparable contexts of varying duration to isolate the importance of durability for individuals? status seeking behavior. The paper is based on quantitative analyses of 3402 scientists affiliated with a large scale research facility 2006-2011, publishing 1282 on-site publications and 97,361 off-site publications. Through comparison of collaboration patterns, tie creation and performance we find that status in a long durability context increases status and performance, while status in a temporary context decreases network centrality and performance. This indicates that status antecedents and effects depend on the context of status attainment.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Jacob","Andersen, Kristina Vaarst"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-294078"],"event":{"end":"2015-06-17","place":"Rome, it","start":"2015-06-15","title":"The DRUID Society Conference 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"restless plate spinners and rising stars how organizational foci and status dynamics impact tie creation and high impact science","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-294078","ids":["cbs-c454d85a-ef5f-4daa-885e-4bf4664e0769"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C3DF81E9A3FF2010D11A421659441F71"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation, Department of Innovation and Organizational Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"8b2b644b-5bed-4d26-ad6f-2d87be498450","name":"Jeppesen, Jacob","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina","key":"vaarstandersenpau","last":"Vaarst Andersen","locid":"e64ee7c1-08fa-4113-947a-18da853e6a39","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","name_org":"Vaarst Andersen, Kristina","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-c454d85a-ef5f-4daa-885e-4bf4664e0769"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Restless Plate Spinners and Rising Stars : How Organizational Foci and Status Dynamics impact Tie Creation and High Impact Science","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-294078","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Organic farming is based on the concept of working ‘with nature’ instead of against it; however, compared with conventional farming, organic farming reportedly has lower productivity. Ideally, the goal should be to narrow this yield gap. In this review, we specifically discuss the feasibility of new breeding techniques (NBTs) for rewilding, a process involving the reintroduction of properties from the wild relatives of crops, as a method to close the productivity gap. The most efficient methods of rewilding are based on modern biotechnology techniques, which have yet to be embraced by the organic farming movement. Thus, the question arises of whether the adoption of such methods is feasible, not only from a technological perspective, but also from conceptual, socioeconomic, ethical, and regulatory perspectives.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Andersen, Martin Marchman","Landes, Xavier","Xiang, Wen","Anyshchenko, Artem","Falhof, Janus","Østerberg, Jeppe Thulin","Olsen, Lene Irene","Edenbrandt, Anna Kristina","Vedel, Suzanne Elizabeth","Thorsen, Bo Jellesmark","Sandøe, Peter","Gamborg, Christian","Kappel, Klemens","Palmgren, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-438495"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasibility of new breeding techniques for organic farming","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.cell.com/trends/plant-science/abstract/S1360-1385(15)00112-0","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-438495","identifier":[{"id":"84937526022","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26027462","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4b8e1bb5-55ca-45d1-92bc-9901a596b5ef"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A1B08BA63492C0C40C6948BE0E3D4178"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Martin Marchman","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"484eff7d-667a-41f9-a384-ff62b0047da4","name":"Andersen, Martin Marchman","orcid":"0000-0002-1710-213X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xavier","key":"landespau","last":"Landes","locid":"40e1e2e8-bd45-4c7a-b814-af7b51a68581","name":"Landes, Xavier","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Wen","key":"xiangpau","last":"Xiang","locid":"b83ac3c5-f5c3-4588-bb75-f1858703a6ea","name":"Xiang, Wen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Artem","key":"anyshchenkopau","last":"Anyshchenko","locid":"ea5adf28-f04a-4c39-ac48-3782b1fbc8fa","name":"Anyshchenko, Artem","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Janus","key":"falhofpau","last":"Falhof","locid":"00e3ca2e-5e81-4aaa-8e67-29ae29536c63","name":"Falhof, Janus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jeppe Thulin","key":"østerbergpau","last":"Østerberg","locid":"c4b9a818-bdde-4b6e-a448-3e8e86e0b89a","name":"Østerberg, Jeppe Thulin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Irene","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"155d7444-3912-4449-8e74-6250b33ee309","name":"Olsen, Lene Irene","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna Kristina","key":"edenbrandtpau","last":"Edenbrandt","locid":"94d178f1-c1b5-4b50-a84f-02974ace8ea2","name":"Edenbrandt, Anna Kristina","orcid":"0000-0002-9298-6705","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Suzanne Elizabeth","key":"vedelpau","last":"Vedel","locid":"57a3de99-d342-49b6-a6b8-2d5620d84055","name":"Vedel, Suzanne Elizabeth","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo Jellesmark","key":"thorsenpau","last":"Thorsen","locid":"a11f0f2d-120f-475b-9d08-eadc2de0f6b6","name":"Thorsen, Bo Jellesmark","orcid":"0000-0002-3305-8343","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"sandøepau","last":"Sandøe","locid":"1e8ff72f-573c-4453-9c10-e6e09658b1ed","name":"Sandøe, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-0397-3273","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"gamborgpau","last":"Gamborg","locid":"6e80ba80-9b7a-4618-b458-01b8411a7168","name":"Gamborg, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-3150-8280","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Klemens","key":"kappelpau","last":"Kappel","locid":"d8c98df7-137f-48e9-ae27-c5897843bf64","name":"Kappel, Klemens","orcid":"0000-0001-7176-6976","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Broberg","key":"palmgrenpau","last":"Palmgren","locid":"28d7c382-c542-4a79-83e5-b479c3fe763e","name":"Palmgren, Michael","name_org":"Palmgren, Michael Broberg","orcid":"0000-0002-9982-6114","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26027462"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.tplants.2015.04.011","issn":["13601385","18784372"],"issn_org":["13601385"],"issue":"7","journal":"Trends in Plant Science","pages":"426-434","status":"p","title":"Trends in Plant Science","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84937526022"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4b8e1bb5-55ca-45d1-92bc-9901a596b5ef"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Feasibility of new breeding techniques for organic farming","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-438495","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND CONTEXT: Idiopathic scoliosis is a spinal deformity affecting approximately 3% of otherwise healthy children or adolescents. The etiology is still largely unknown but has an important genetic component. Genome-wide association studies have identified a number of common genetic variants that are significantly associated with idiopathic scoliosis in Asian and Caucasian populations, rs11190870 close to the LBX1 gene being the most replicated finding. PURPOSE: The aim of the present study was to investigate the genetics of idiopathic scoliosis in a Scandinavian cohort by performing a candidate gene study of four variants previously shown to be associated with idiopathic scoliosis and exome sequencing of idiopathic scoliosis patients with a severe phenotype to identify possible novel scoliosis risk variants. STUDY DESIGN: This was a case control study. PATIENT SAMPLE: A total of 1,739 patients with idiopathic scoliosis and 1,812 controls were included. OUTCOME MEASURE: The outcome measure was idiopathic scoliosis. METHODS: The variants rs10510181, rs11190870, rs12946942, and rs6570507 were genotyped in 1,739 patients with idiopathic scoliosis and 1,812 controls. Exome sequencing was performed on pooled samples from 100 surgically treated idiopathic scoliosis patients. Novel or rare missense, nonsense, or splice site variants were selected for individual genotyping in the 1,739 cases and 1,812 controls. In addition, the 5'UTR, noncoding exon and promoter regions of LBX1, not covered by exome sequencing, were Sanger sequenced in the 100 pooled samples. RESULTS: Of the four candidate genes, an intergenic variant, rs11190870, downstream of the LBX1 gene, showed a highly significant association to idiopathic scoliosis in 1,739 cases and 1,812 controls (p=7.0×10(-18)). We identified 20 novel variants by exome sequencing after filtration and an initial genotyping validation. However, we could not verify any association to idiopathic scoliosis in the large cohort of 1,739 cases and 1,812 controls. We did not find any variants in the 5'UTR, noncoding exon and promoter regions of LBX1. CONCLUSIONS: Here, we confirm LBX1 as a susceptibility gene for idiopathic scoliosis in a Scandinavian population and report that we are unable to find evidence of other genes of similar or stronger effect.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Grauers, Anna","Wang, Jingwen","Einarsdottir, Elisabet","Simony, Ane","Danielsson, Aina","Åkesson, Kristina","Ohlin, Acke","Halldin, Klas","Grabowski, Pawel","Tenne, Max","Laivuori, Hannele","Dahlman, Ingrid","Andersen, Mikkel Østerheden","Christensen, Steen Bach","Karlsson, Magnus K","Jiao, Hong","Kere, Juha","Gerdhem, Paul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-602259"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Exome sequencing","GENE","Idiopathic scoliosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Middelfart Sygehus"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"candidate gene analysis and exome sequencing confirm lbx000000000001 as a susceptibility gene for idiopathic scoliosis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spinee.2015.05.013","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-602259","identifier":[{"id":"84942504402","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25987191","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-658f5fe6-f28c-4f92-8b08-a898f58e1f58"],"keyword":["Gene","Idiopathic Scoliosis","LBX1","exome sequencing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A377A30F70A4DD60835669EE1FBDFB9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.spinee.2015.05.013","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/135418457/Einarsdottir_CELSR2_manu_03072017.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Sygehus Lillebælt, Forskningsenhed for Rygkirurgi (Kolding)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Spine Center of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Middelfart Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"grauerspau","last":"Grauers","name":"Grauers, Anna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jingwen","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jingwen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabet","key":"einarsdottirpau","last":"Einarsdottir","name":"Einarsdottir, Elisabet","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ane","key":"simonypau","last":"Simony","locid":"489efac7-1bcf-4816-83d2-66a2fbf0c263","name":"Simony, Ane","orcid":"0000-0002-1788-1161","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Aina","key":"danielssonpau","last":"Danielsson","name":"Danielsson, Aina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"åkessonpau","last":"Åkesson","name":"Åkesson, Kristina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Acke","key":"ohlinpau","last":"Ohlin","name":"Ohlin, Acke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Klas","key":"halldinpau","last":"Halldin","name":"Halldin, Klas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Pawel","key":"grabowskipau","last":"Grabowski","name":"Grabowski, Pawel","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Max","key":"tennepau","last":"Tenne","name":"Tenne, Max","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hannele","key":"laivuoripau","last":"Laivuori","name":"Laivuori, Hannele","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingrid","key":"dahlmanpau","last":"Dahlman","name":"Dahlman, Ingrid","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"cea27719-0afc-440f-b74e-4f0560170438","name":"Andersen, Mikkel Østerheden","name_org":"Andersen, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-8478-8218","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen Bach","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Steen Bach","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Magnus K","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","name":"Karlsson, Magnus K","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hong","key":"jiaopau","last":"Jiao","name":"Jiao, Hong","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Juha","key":"kerepau","last":"Kere","name":"Kere, Juha","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul","key":"gerdhempau","last":"Gerdhem","name":"Gerdhem, Paul","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25987191"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.spinee.2015.05.013","issn":["15299430","18781632"],"issn_org":["15299430"],"issue":"10","journal":"Spine Journal","pages":"2239-2246","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Spine Journal","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84942504402"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-658f5fe6-f28c-4f92-8b08-a898f58e1f58"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Candidate gene analysis and exome sequencing confirm LBX1 as a susceptibility gene for idiopathic scoliosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-602259","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The serotonin transporter (SERT) terminates serotonergic neurotransmission by performing reuptake of released serotonin, and SERT is the primary target for antidepressants. SERT mediates the reuptake of serotonin through an alternating access mechanism, implying that a central substrate site is connected to both sides of the membrane by permeation pathways, of which only one is accessible at a time. The coordinated conformational changes in SERT associated with substrate translocation are not fully understood. Here, we have identified a Leu to Glu mutation at position 406 (L406E) in the extracellular loop 4 (EL4) of human SERT, which induced a remarkable gain-of-potency (up to >40-fold) for a range of SERT inhibitors. The effects were highly specific for L406E relative to six other mutations in the same position, including the closely related L406D mutation, showing that the effects induced by L406E are not simply charge-related effects. Leu(406) is located >10 Å from the central inhibitor binding site indicating that the mutation affects inhibitor binding in an indirect manner. We found that L406E decreased accessibility to a residue in the cytoplasmic pathway. The shift in equilibrium to favor a more outward-facing conformation of SERT can explain the reduced turnover rate and increased association rate of inhibitor binding we found for L406E. Together, our findings show that EL4 allosterically can modulate inhibitor binding within the central binding site, and substantiates that EL4 has an important role in controlling the conformational equilibrium of human SERT.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rannversson, Hafsteinn","Wilson, Pamela","Kristensen, Kristina Birch","Sinning, Steffen","Kristensen, Anders Skov","Strømgaard, Kristian","Andersen, Jacob"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-030410"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"importance of the extracellular loop 000000000004 in the human serotonin transporter for inhibitor binding and substrate translocation","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M114.629071","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-030410","identifier":[{"id":"25903124","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4505525","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84930652742","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f5fc094b-9571-465f-b895-530901cdd023","ku-9a250bb7-3696-46ae-8471-7fcede89719c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-293A1E2A7D3158236AD9045D1FA973C7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M114.629071","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Medicinal Chemistry Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Translational Neuropsychiatry Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Hafsteinn","key":"rannverssonhafsteinnpau","la