Subserved by the ipRGCs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-535765","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: HIV-infected controllers control viral replication and maintain normal CD4 T cell counts. Long-term nonprogressors (LTNPs) also maintain normal CD4 T cell counts but have ongoing viral replication. We hypothesized that immunoregulatory mechanisms are involved in preserved CD4 T cell counts in controllers and in LTNPs. METHODS: Twenty HIV-infected viremic controllers, 5 elite controllers (ECs), and 14 LTNPs were included in this cross-sectional study. For comparison, 25 progressors and 34 healthy controls were included. Regulatory T cells (Tregs), Treg subpopulations, CD161+Th17 cells, and CD3+CD8+CD161(high)Tc17 cells in peripheral blood were measured using flow cytometry. Tregs in lymphoid tissue were determined in tonsil biopsies and evaluated using immunolabeling. The production of transforming growth factor beta (TGF-β), interleukin (IL)-10, and IL-17 upon stimulation with phytohemagglutinin in peripheral blood was determined by Luminex. RESULTS: All groups of HIV-infected patients displayed similar percentages of Tregs in both peripheral blood and lymphoid tissue. However, a larger percentage of Tregs in ECs and LTNPs were activated compared with that in controls, progressors, and viremic controllers. Further, ECs as the only group of HIV-infected patients, displayed elevated percentages of CD161+Th17 cells, preserved CD3+CD8+CD161(high)Tc17 cells, and preserved IL-10 production. CONCLUSIONS: Overall, Treg percentage was similar in both blood and lymphoid tissue in all groups of patients and controls. However, both ECs and LTNPs displayed a large proportion of activated Tregs suggesting immunoregulatory mechanisms to be involved in preserving CD4 T cell counts in HIV-infected nonprogressors.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Gaardbo, Julie C","Ronit, Andreas","Hartling, Hans J","Gjerdrum, Lise Mette Rahbek","Springborg, Karoline","Ralfkiaer, Elisabeth","Thorsteinsson, Kristina","Ullum, Henrik","Andersen, Åse Bengård","Nielsen, Susanne D"],"cuid":["S02-081.50-047268"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Antigens CD3","CD4 Lymphocyte Count","CD8 Positive T Lymphocytes","CD8 Positive T Lymphocytes immunology","Case Control Studies","Cross Sectional Studies","Female","Flow Cytometry","HIV","HIV Infections","HIV Infections immunology","HIV Long Term Survivors","Humans","Interleukin 10","Interleukin 10 blood","Interleukin 17","Interleukin 17 blood","Lymphocyte Subsets","Lymphoid Tissue","Male","Middle Aged","Nonprogression","T Lymphocytes Regulatory","T Lymphocytes Regulatory immunology","Th17 Cells immunology","Th17 cells","Transforming Growth Factor beta","regulatory T cells"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immunoregulatory t cells may be involved in preserving cd000000000004 t cell counts in hiv infected long term nonprogressors and controllers","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/QAI.0b013e3182a7c932","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-081.50-047268","identifier":[{"id":"84893750215","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23995946","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-effdbfee-4a0b-4fdb-be5d-785241560c48","sdu-88b5e5fb-9555-43fe-96c5-745d58f57446"],"keyword":["Activated Tregs","Adult","Antigens, CD3","CD3 Complex/immunology","CD4 Lymphocyte Count","CD8-Positive T-Lymphocytes","CD8-Positive T-Lymphocytes/immunology","Case-Control Studies","Cross-Sectional Studies","Female","Flow Cytometry","HIV","HIV Infections","HIV Infections/immunology","HIV Long-Term Survivors","Humans","Interleukin-10","Interleukin-10/blood","Interleukin-17","Interleukin-17/blood","LTNP","Lymphocyte Subsets","Lymphocyte Subsets/immunology","Lymphoid tissue","Male","Middle Aged","NK Cell Lectin-Like Receptor Subfamily B","NK Cell Lectin-Like Receptor Subfamily B/immunology","Nonprogression","Regulatory T cells","T-Lymphocytes, Regulatory","T-Lymphocytes, Regulatory/immunology","Tc17 cells","Th17 Cells","Th17 Cells/immunology","Transforming Growth Factor beta","Transforming Growth Factor beta/blood"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9FC4FA67869D328C78D37AC55723386F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/QAI.0b013e3182a7c932","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Julie C","key":"gaardbopau","last":"Gaardbo","name":"Gaardbo, Julie C","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas","key":"ronitpau","last":"Ronit","name":"Ronit, Andreas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans J","key":"hartlingpau","last":"Hartling","name":"Hartling, Hans J","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lise M R","key":"g