{"abstract":"Boundary spanning is one way to accumulate diverse knowledge. This paper examines the conditions under which boundary spanning increases the value of project participants contributions to team production. Statistical findings from logit regressions show that the cost-benefit tradeoff of boundary spanning depends on whether the focal project is aimed at exploitation or exploration. If the focal project is mostly explorative, diverse knowledge is a valuable resource; in projects where the focus is on exploitation, diverse knowledge impedes project performance. The findings in this paper confirm and extend research on boundary spanning and organizational learning.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-279392"],"event":{"end":"2012-06-21","place":"Frederiksberg, dk","start":"2012-06-19","title":"The DRUID Society Conference 2012 on Innovation and Competitiveness","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oracle or obstacle individual level knowledge heterogeinity and innovation","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-279392","ids":["cbs-2a5a348c-ae15-4e9f-aa8e-28e1d48c269d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-032CD33CC4D984B8D90214594B0B9ED3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation, Department of Innovation and Organizational Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina","key":"vaarstandersenpau","last":"Vaarst Andersen","locid":"e64ee7c1-08fa-4113-947a-18da853e6a39","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","name_org":"Vaarst Andersen, Kristina","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-2a5a348c-ae15-4e9f-aa8e-28e1d48c269d"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Oracle or Obstacle? : Individual Level Knowledge, Heterogeinity and Innovation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-279392","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
