{"abstract":"One third of the pregnant Danish women are overweight or obese. Maternal obesity is an independent risk factor for adverse maternal and foetal outcomes including infertility, miscarriage, congenital malformations, preeclampsia, gestational diabetes, complicated deliveries, caesarean section, macrosomia and childhood obesity. This article reviews the effect of maternal obesity on obstetric and neonatal outcomes and provides recommendations for management of obesity in pregnancy.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Vinter, Christina Anne","Honnens Tanvig, Mette","Damm, Peter","Naver, Klara","Andreasen, Kirsten Riis","Andersen, Lise Lotte Torvin","Liest, Sara","Lunde, Søren","Dorte Møller, Jensen","Renault, Kristina Martha"],"cuid":["S02-084.10-045930"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"overvægtige gravide og komplikationer i relation til graviditet og fødsel","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ugeskriftet.dk/videnskab/overvaegtige-gravide-og-komplikationer-i-relation-til-graviditet-og-foedsel","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-084.10-045930","identifier":[{"id":"22510547","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84862004353","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c19d6c67-ef10-468d-a095-83ed1032c219","sdu-0d7f5253-df3a-4a5b-8659-9b6a505372d6"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-7-0C6F21233626CD678FF36C5493818AA4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ugeskriftet.dk/videnskab/overvaegtige-gravide