871e199a2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Thalidomide and dexamethasone vs. bortezomib and dexamethasone for melphalan refractory myeloma : a randomized study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-021522","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This article uses a mixed-method study of Denmark to investigate whether and how Richard Florida's creative class theory should be adapted to small welfare economies. First, we carry out an econometric analyses showing that like in North America, the Danish creative class propels economic growth and exhibits a tendency of congregating in major cities with diverse service and cultural offers and tolerance to non-mainstream lifestyles. However, we find that a range of smaller Danish cities also attract the creative class. Second, we undertake qualitative interviews that facilitate theory building. We suggest that many creatives are attracted by the smaller cities' cost advantages, specialized job offers, attractive work/life balances, and authenticity and sense of community. The article synthesizes its results into four stylized types of creative cities, and concludes by discussing the policy challenges associated with these different cities.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lorenzen, Mark","Andersen, Kristina Vaarst"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-282529"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clusters","Creative class","Services","Welfare economy"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"different creative cities exploring danish data to adapt the creative class argument to small welfare economies","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://esc-web.lib.cbs.dk/login?url=http://search.ebscohost.com/login.aspx?direct=true&db=bth&AN=77733911&site=ehost-live&scope=site","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-282529","identifier":[{"id":"84870567155","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-4b34ec01-0446-4196-b4e7-10ee2b4b20dd"],"keyword":["Services","clusters","creative city types","creative class","cultural offer","welfare economy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2C15A04863EA58935933009D377D76E0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation, Department of Innovation and Organizational Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mark","key":"lorenzenpau","last":"Lorenzen","locid":"197bb07e-e2b9-4b82-805b-c89e9b79eb1b","name":"Lorenzen, Mark","orcid":"0000-0001-8913-1143","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina","key":"vaarstandersenpau","last":"Vaarst Andersen","locid":"e64ee7c1-08fa-4113-947a-18da853e6a39","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","name_org":"Vaarst Andersen, Kristina","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1386/cij.4.2.123_1","issn":["17510694","17510708"],"issn_org":["17510694"],"issue":"1","journal":"Creative Industries Journal","pages":"123-136","publisher":"Taylor and Francis Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Creative Industries Journal","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84870567155"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-4b34ec01-0446-4196-b4e7-10ee2b4b20dd"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Different Creative Cities : Exploring Danish Data to Adapt the Creative Class Argument to Small Welfare Economies","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-282529","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Embeddedness has been touted as a framework for knowledge exchange and innovation, and thus as an important precondition for high-level performance. Embeddedness of economic action in social relations improves access to resources, but over-embeddedness impedes performance. However, until now the association between embeddedness and performance in different markets has been neglected. This paper challenges the predominant view of embeddedness and over-embeddedness as absolute and mutually exclusive conditions. Through regression analyses of novel data from a project-based industry, the paper tests the association between embeddedness and economic performance in different markets, finding a positive association in the domestic market, but a negative association in foreign markets. This divergence in performance is caused in part by selection bias in the access to foreign markets, and in part by accumulation of localized knowledge.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Andersen, Kristina Vaarst"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-292373"],"event":{"end":"2012-08-07","place":"Boston, us","start":"2012-08-03","title":"72nd Annual Meeting of the Academy of Management, AOM 2012","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Embeddedness","Knowledge transfer","Opportunity allocation"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the problem of embeddedness revisited collaboration and market types","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-292373","ids":["cbs-b308d3ff-472d-48cd-8994-c83247198c0b"],"keyword":["Embeddedness","Knowledge transfer","Opportunity allocation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A8369D2D5F2DC26CB7A7F9AB43A06060"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Strategy and Innovation, Department of Innovation and Organizational Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina","key":"vaarstandersenpau","last":"Vaarst Andersen","locid":"e64ee7c1-08fa-4113-947a-18da853e6a39","name":"Andersen, Kristina Vaarst","name_org":"Vaarst Andersen, Kristina","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-6832","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-b308d3ff-472d-48cd-8994-c83247198c0b"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"The Problem of Embeddedness Revisited : Collaboration and Market Types","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-292373","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
